<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.282">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>quinate/shikimate dehydrogenase [NAD(P)(+)]</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>quinate/shikimate dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.282#SIP3F85DE9F27FAFE52"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.282#SIP6C0C3D6BF697C3B2"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.282#SIPCE4402C52A57D828"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.282#SIP24AEE14746EF382F"/>
<rdfs:comment>This is the second shikimate dehydrogenase enzyme found in Escherichia coli.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can use both quinate and shikimate as substrates and either NAD(+) or NADP(+) as acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The low catalytic efficiency with both quinate and shikimate suggests that neither may be the physiological substrate. cf. EC 1.1.1.24, EC 1.1.1.25, and EC 1.1.5.8.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12624088"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12637497"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
