<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.351">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phosphogluconate dehydrogenase [NAD(P)(+)-dependent, decarboxylating]</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.351#SIP2F6BA0F4C7028619"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.351#SIP5EA5E651C1FBBEED"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in the oxidative branch of the pentose phosphate pathway, whose main purpose is to produce reducing power and pentose for biosynthetic reactions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 1.1.1.44, it is not specific for NADP(+) and can accept both cofactors with similar efficiency. cf. EC 1.1.1.343.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6402366"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7350909"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8579362"/>
