<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.433">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sulfoacetaldehyde reductase (NADH)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.433#SIP8A3AC7E79A47BFDD"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from the bacteria Bilophila wadsworthia and Clostridium sp. MSTE9 catalyze the reaction only in the reduction direction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the bacterium Bifidobacterium kashiwanohense the optimal reaction pH for sulfoacetaldehyde reduction is 7.5, while that for isethionate oxidation is 10.0. cf. EC 1.1.1.313.</rdfs:comment>
