<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1042/bsr20190715</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/SIPA92E437F3CD7880E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1021/acscatal.1c04321</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.434">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-dehydro-3-deoxy-L-fuconate 4-dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.434#SIP6CF779490048BD52"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.434#SIPAAE6F867CD6910BB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, originally described from the bacterium Xanthomonas campestris pv. campestris, participates in an L-fucose degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also act on 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-L-galactonate and 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-pentonate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17144652"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30655589"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.434#SIP6CF779490048BD52">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-dehydro-3-deoxy-L-fuconate + NAD(+) = 2,4-didehydro-3-deoxy-L-rhamnonate + H(+) + NADH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.434#SIPAAE6F867CD6910BB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-arabinonate + NAD(+) = 5-hydroxy-2,4-dioxopentanoate + H(+) + NADH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17144652">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17144652"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17144652"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1021/bi061687o</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30655589">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/30655589"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30655589"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41598-018-36774-6</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.435">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-fucose dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.435#SIPC9330E523EF66FE7"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.435#SIPD36E57B7339C08BE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Burkholderia multivorans, participates in an L-fucose degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of beta-L-fucopyranose to L-fucono-1,5-lactone, which is unstable and is rapidly converted to L-fucono-1,4-lactone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The alpha anomer is not recognized.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also act on beta-L-galactopyranose and D-arabinose with lower activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NADP(+) is a better cosubstrate than NAD(+).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23214453"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.435#SIPC9330E523EF66FE7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>beta-L-fucose + NADP(+) = H(+) + L-fucono-1,5-lactone + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.435#SIPD36E57B7339C08BE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>D-arabinose + NADP(+) = D-arabinono-1,5-lactone + H(+) + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23214453">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/23214453"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23214453"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1021/bi3015554</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.436">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.3.1.110"/>
<skos:prefLabel>lactate dehydrogenase (NAD(+),ferredoxin)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>electron bifurcating LDH/Etf complex</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.436#SIP9EE9B87F4324D3AC"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Acetobacterium woodii, uses flavin-based electron confurcation to drive endergonic lactate oxidation with NAD(+) as oxidant at the expense of simultaneous exergonic electron flow from reduced ferredoxin to NAD(+).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24762045"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.436#SIP9EE9B87F4324D3AC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>lactate + 2 NAD(+) + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = 2 NADH + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + pyruvate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24762045">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/24762045"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24762045"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1111/1462-2920.12493</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.437">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>5-dehydrofumagillol 5-reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.1.437#SIPF3D592C71BAA3BB5"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the mold Aspergillus fumigatus, participates in the biosynthesis of the meroterpenoid fumagillin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is a partial polyketide synthase (PKS) consisting of only a dehydratase (DH) and a ketoreductase (KR) domain.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24568283"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.1.437#SIPF3D592C71BAA3BB5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>fumagillol + NADP(+) = 5-dehydrofumagillol + H(+) + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24568283">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/24568283"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24568283"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1021/ja500881e</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
