<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.2.10">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>lanthanide-dependent methanol dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Ce(3+)-induced methanol dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cerium dependent MDH</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>La(3+)-dependent MDH</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.2.10#SIPF0A96B636B9138B6"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from the bacterium Methylacidiphilum fumariolicum and many Methylobacterium species.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Requires La(3+), Ce(3+), Pr(3+) or Nd(3+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The higher lanthanides show decreasing activity with Sm(3+), Eu(3+) and Gd(3+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The lanthanide is coordinated by the enzyme and pyrroloquinoline quinone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Shows little activity with Ca(2+), the required cofactor of EC 1.1.2.7.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21256798"/>
