<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.98.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ribonucleoside-triphosphate reductase (formate)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>anaerobic ribonucleoside-triphosphate reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.98.6#SIPAD8BECABB46723E4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which is expressed in the bacterium Escherichia coli during anaerobic growth, contains an iron sulfur center.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The active form of the enzyme contains an oxygen-sensitive glycyl (1-amino-2-oxoethan-1-yl) radical that is generated by the activating enzyme NrdG via chemistry involving S-adenosylmethionine (SAM) and a [4Fe-4S] cluster.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The glycyl radical is involved in generation of a transient thiyl (sulfanyl) radical on a cysteine residue, which attacks the substrate, forming a ribonucleotide 3'-radical, followed by water loss to form a ketyl (alpha-oxoalkyl) radical.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The ketyl radical gains an electron from a cysteine residue and a proton from formic acid, forming 3'-keto-deoxyribonucleotide and generating a thiosulfuranyl (1lambda(4)-disulfan-1-yl) radical bridge between methionine and cysteine residues.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Oxidation of formate by the thiosulfuranyl radical results in the release of CO2 and regeneration of the thiyl radical. cf. EC 1.17.4.1 and EC 1.17.4.2.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1460049"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7568012"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8381402"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9305874"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24827372"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.98.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.98.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.98.6#SIPAD8BECABB46723E4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a ribonucleoside 5'-triphosphate + formate + H(+) = a 2'-deoxyribonucleoside 5'-triphosphate + CO2 + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
