<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.98.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>serine-type anaerobic sulfatase-maturating enzyme</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.98.7#SIP7AF45F736E650521"/>
<rdfs:comment>A bacterial radical S-adenosyl-L-methionine (AdoMet) enzyme that contains three [4Fe-4S] clusters.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in some bacteria, activates a type I sulfatase enzyme (EC 3.1.6.1) by converting a conserved L-serine residue in the active site to a unique 3-oxo-L-alanine residue that is essential for the sulfatase activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While the enzyme from Klebsiella pneumoniae is specific for L-serine, the enzyme from Clostridium perfringens can also act on L-cysteine, see EC 1.8.98.7.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10336424"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14749327"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18558715"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.98.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.98.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.98.7#SIP7AF45F736E650521">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-seryl-[sulfatase] + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3-oxo-L-alanyl-[sulfatase] + 5'-deoxyadenosine + H(+) + L-methionine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
