<activity rdf:resource="1.1.99.6#SIPED8AEFDE4B84A6D8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the archaeon Archaeoglobus fulgidus cannot utilize NAD(+), cytochrome C, methylene blue or dimethylnaphthoquinone as acceptors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In vitro it is active with artificial electron acceptors such as 2,6-dichlorophenolindophenol, but the physiological acceptor is not yet known.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10601217"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
