<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.99.42">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>4-pyridoxate dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.1.99.42#SIP23DF186E8ED85453"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Pseudomonas sp. MA-1 and Mesorhizobium loti, participates in the degradation of pyridoxine (vitamin B6).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is membrane bound and contains FAD.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme has been assayed in vitro in the presence of the artificial electron acceptor dichloroindophenol (DCPIP).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6348042"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18216065"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.1.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.1.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.1.99.42#SIP23DF186E8ED85453">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4-pyridoxate + A = 5-formyl-3-hydroxy-2-methylpyridine-4-carboxylate + AH2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
