<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.10">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acetaldehyde dehydrogenase (acetylating)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acylating acetaldehyde dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>aldehyde dehydrogenase (acylating)</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.1.10#SIPA023BAA5E1C1B5F4"/>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts, more slowly, on glycolaldehyde, propanal and butanal.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In several bacterial species this enzyme forms a bifunctional complex with EC 4.1.3.39.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from the bacteria Burkholderia xenovorans and Thermus thermophilus also perform the reaction of EC 1.2.1.87.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the meta-cleavage pathway for the degradation of phenols, methylphenols and catechols.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NADP(+) can replace NAD(+) but the rate of reaction is much slower.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7458347"/>
