<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the marine bacterium Vibrio sp. EJY3, is involved in a degradation pathway for 3,6-anhydro-alpha-L-galactose, a major component of the polysaccharides produced by red macroalgae, such as agarose and porphyran.</rdfs:comment>
