<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.95">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-2-aminoadipate reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>alpha-aminoadipate reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.1.95#SIP812E6AB4A0DE3802"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, characterized from the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae, catalyzes the reduction of L-2-aminoadipate to (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate during L-lysine biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>An adenylation domain activates the substrate at the expense of ATP hydrolysis, and forms L-2-aminoadipate adenylate, which is attached to a peptidyl-carrier protein (PCP) domain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Binding of NADPH results in reductive cleavage of the acyl-S-enzyme intermediate, releasing (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Different from EC 1.2.1.31 which catalyzes a similar transformation in the opposite direction without ATP hydrolysis.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10320345"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.95#SIP812E6AB4A0DE3802">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate + AMP + diphosphate + NADP(+) = ATP + H(+) + L-2-aminoadipate + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10320345">
