<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.101">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-tyrosine reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.1.101#SIPCEF77EC058D55458"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the ascomycete fungus Aspergillus flavus, is specific for L-tyrosine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It contains three domains - an adenylation domain, a peptidyl-carrier protein (PCP) domain, and a reductase domain, and requires activation by attachment of a phosphopantetheinyl group.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme activates its substrate to an adenylate form, followed by a transfer to the PCP domain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The resulting thioester is subsequently transferred to the reductase domain, where it is reduced to the aldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23281040"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.101#SIPCEF77EC058D55458">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>AMP + diphosphate + L-tyrosinal + NADP(+) = ATP + H(+) + L-tyrosine + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
