<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.104">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>pyruvate dehydrogenase system</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PDH</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pyruvate dehydrogenase complex</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.1.104#SIPEF79DA26336A226A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The pyruvate dehydrogenase system (PDH) is a large enzyme complex that belongs to the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase system family, which also includes EC 1.2.1.25, EC 1.2.1.105, EC 1.4.1.27 and EC 2.3.1.190.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>With the exception of the glycine cleavage system, which contains 4 components, the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase systems share a common structure, consisting of three main components, namely a 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase (E1), a dihydrolipoamide acyltransferase (E2), and a dihydrolipoamide dehydrogenase (E3).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction catalyzed by this system is the sum of three activities: EC 1.2.4.1, EC 2.3.1.12, and EC 1.8.1.4.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The mammalian system also includes E3 binding protein, which is involved in the interaction between the E2 and E3 subunits.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/329143"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1103138"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2227213"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3905803"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7032507"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.104#SIPEF79DA26336A226A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>CoA + NAD(+) + pyruvate = acetyl-CoA + CO2 + NADH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
