<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.1.105">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-oxoglutarate dehydrogenase system</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-oxoglutarate dehydrogenase complex</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.1.105#SIPDA0CBB892E7BB5F6"/>
<rdfs:comment>The 2-oxoglutarate dehydrogenase system is a large enzyme complex that belongs to the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase system family, which also includes EC 1.2.1.25, EC 1.2.1.104, EC 1.4.1.27 and EC 2.3.1.190.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>With the exception of the glycine cleavage system, which contains 4 components, the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase systems share a common structure, consisting of three main components, namely a 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase (E1), a dihydrolipoamide acyltransferase (E2), and a dihydrolipoamide dehydrogenase (E3).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme system converts 2-oxoglutarate to succinyl-CoA and produces NADH and CO2 in a complicated series of irreversible reactions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction catalyzed by this system is the sum of three activities: EC 1.2.4.2, EC 2.3.1.61 and EC 1.8.1.4.</rdfs:comment>
