<skos:altLabel>retinal oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.3.1#SIP883273BF4CF37DCD"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.3.1#SIP52C12CF86C6A19B7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from liver exhibits a broad substrate specificity, and is involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics, including the oxidation of N-heterocycles and aldehydes and the reduction of N-oxides, nitrosamines, hydroxamic acids, azo dyes, nitropolycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, and sulfoxides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is also responsible for the oxidation of retinal, an activity that was initially attributed to a distinct enzyme (EC 1.2.3.11).</rdfs:comment>
