<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.3.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>indole-3-acetaldehyde oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>IAAld oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>IAA oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>indoleacetaldehyde oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.3.7#SIPC7D484E67ED141D3"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isoform of EC 1.2.3.1.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Has a preference for aldehydes having an indole-ring structure as substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>May play a role in plant hormone biosynthesis as its activity is higher in the auxin-overproducing mutant, super-root1, than in wild-type Arabidopsis thaliana.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While (indol-3-yl)acetaldehyde is the preferred substrate, it also oxidizes indole-3-carbaldehyde and acetaldehyde, but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9489015"/>
