<skos:altLabel>pyruvate oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.5.1#SIPCB1292729DC1E428"/>
<rdfs:comment>This bacterial enzyme is located on the inner surface of the cytoplasmic membrane and coupled to the respiratory chain via ubiquinone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Does not accept menaquinone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity is greatly enhanced by lipids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Requires thiamine diphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also form acetoin.</rdfs:comment>
