<skos:altLabel>pyruvate synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pyruvic-ferredoxin oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.7.1#SIPC311E6DC9E163454"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.7.1#SIPA401275E22A64CC8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also decarboxylates 2-oxobutanoate with lower efficiency, but shows no activity with 2-oxoglutarate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is a member of the 2-oxoacid oxidoreductases, a family of enzymes that oxidatively decarboxylate different 2-oxoacids to form their CoA derivatives, and are differentiated based on their substrate specificity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>For examples of other members of this family, see EC 1.2.7.3 and EC 1.2.7.7.</rdfs:comment>
