<skos:prefLabel>2-oxoglutarate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-ketoglutarate ferredoxin oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-oxoglutarate ferredoxin oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>alpha-ketoglutarate-ferredoxin oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>alpha-ketoglutarate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>KGOR</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.7.3#SIP523DEE097D79BC02"/>
<rdfs:comment>Highly specific for 2-oxoglutarate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is a member of the 2-oxoacid oxidoreductases, a family of enzymes that oxidatively decarboxylate different 2-oxoacids to form their CoA derivatives, and are differentiated based on their substrate specificity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>For examples of other members of this family, see EC 1.2.7.1 and EC 1.2.7.7.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4286833"/>
