<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.7.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.2.99.2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>anaerobic carbon-monoxide dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>carbon-monoxide dehydrogenase (ferredoxin)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Ni-CODH</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.7.4#SIPC576ADE66349AEE0"/>
<rdfs:comment>This prokaryotic enzyme catalyzes the reversible reduction of CO2 to CO.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The electrons are transferred to redox proteins such as ferredoxin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In purple sulfur bacteria and methanogenic archaea it catalyzes the oxidation of CO to CO2, which is incorporated by the Calvin-Benson-Basham cycle or released, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In acetogenic and sulfate-reducing microbes it catalyzes the reduction of CO2 to CO, which is incorporated into acetyl CoA by EC 2.3.1.169, with which the enzyme forms a tight complex in those organisms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In purple sulfur bacteria the enzyme forms complexes with the Ni-Fe-S protein EC 1.12.7.2 which catalyze the overall reaction: CO + H2O = CO2 + H2. cf. EC 1.2.5.3.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3029096"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6687389"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6687458"/>
