<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.98.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.2.99.4"/>
<skos:prefLabel>formaldehyde dismutase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.2.98.1#SIPFD27B37AE04B2C3C"/>
<rdfs:comment>Enzyme-bound NADPH formed by oxidation of formaldehyde to formate is oxidized back to NADP(+) by reaction with a second formaldehyde, yielding methanol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Mycobacterium sp. DSM 3803 also catalyzes the reactions of EC 1.1.99.36 and EC 1.1.99.37.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Formaldehyde and acetaldehyde can act as donors; formaldehyde, acetaldehyde and propanal can act as acceptors.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3514215"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19875438"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.2.98.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.2.98.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.2.98.1#SIPFD27B37AE04B2C3C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 formaldehyde + H2O = formate + H(+) + methanol.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
