<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dihydrouracil dehydrogenase (NAD(+))</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.1#SIP736C8F1929EDF07F"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.1#SIP8B218850B0914D33"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme was originally discovered in the uracil-fermenting bacterium, Clostridium uracilicum, which utilizes uracil and thymine as nitrogen and carbon sources for growth.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Since then the enzyme was found in additional organisms including Alcaligenes eutrophus, Pseudomonas strains and Escherichia coli.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1903745"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8806723"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10030006"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11759049"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13462991"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21169495"/>
