<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>enoyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase (NADH)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>enoyl-ACP reductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NADH-enoyl acyl carrier protein reductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NADH-specific enoyl-ACP reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.9#SIP64E8E113151A4600"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes an essential step in fatty acid biosynthesis, the reduction of the 2,3-double bond in enoyl-acyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] derivatives of the elongating fatty acid moiety.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli accepts substrates with carbon chain length from 4 to 18.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The FAS-I enzyme from the bacterium Mycobacterium tuberculosis prefers substrates with carbon chain length from 12 to 24 carbons.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4384650"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6756317"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22042840"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.9#SIP64E8E113151A4600">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 2,3-saturated acyl-[ACP] + NAD(+) = a (2E)-enoyl-[ACP] + H(+) + NADH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
