<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.74#SIP51DF949E58B68D51"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.74#SIPE63F03E6A20F8ED3"/>
<rdfs:comment>Highly specific for 4-hydroxynon-2-enal and non-2-enal.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Alk-2-enals of shorter chain have lower affinities.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Exhibits high activities also for alk-2-enones such as but-3-en-2-one and pent-3-en-2-one.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Inactive with cyclohex-2-en-1-one and 12-oxophytodienoic acid.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the detoxification of alpha,beta-unsaturated aldehydes and ketones (cf. EC 1.3.1.102).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11524419"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12514241"/>
