<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.75">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3,8-divinyl protochlorophyllide a 8-vinyl-reductase (NADPH)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>[4-vinyl]chlorophyllide a reductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>4VCR</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>divinyl chlorophyllide a 8-vinyl-reductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>plant-type divinyl chlorophyllide a 8-vinyl-reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.75#SIPDBFA4861378721A5"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.75#SIP97C085191656A946"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in higher plants, green algae, and some phototrophic bacteria, is involved in the production of monovinyl versions of (bacterio)chlorophyll pigments from their divinyl precursors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also act on 3,8-divinyl chlorophyllide a. cf. EC 1.3.7.13.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1390630"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8678296"/>
