<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.78">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>arogenate dehydrogenase (NADP(+))</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>arogenic dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pretyrosine dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TyrAa</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TyrAAT1</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TyrAAT2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.78#SIPD062D24BDA07B97B"/>
<rdfs:comment>Arogenate dehydrogenases may utilize NAD(+) (EC 1.3.1.43), NADP(+) (EC 1.3.1.78), or both (EC 1.3.1.79).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NADP(+)-dependent enzymes usually predominate in higher plants.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the cyanobacterium Synechocystis sp. PCC 6803 and the TyrAAT1 isoform of the plant Arabidopsis thaliana cannot use prephenate as a substrate, while the Arabidopsis isoform TyrAAT2 can use it very poorly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12354106"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15171683"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
