</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.85">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>crotonyl-CoA carboxylase/reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CCR</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>crotonyl-CoA reductase (carboxylating)</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.85#SIP120E5806620D88F4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction is catalyzed in the reverse direction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Rhodobacter sphaeroides, catalyzes (E)-but-2-enoyl-CoA-dependent oxidation of NADPH in the presence of CO2.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>When CO2 is absent, the enzyme catalyzes the reduction of (E)-but-2-enoyl-CoA to butanoyl-CoA, but with only 10% of maximal activity (relative to (E)-but-2-enoyl-CoA carboxylation).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17548827"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19458256"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.85#SIP120E5806620D88F4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2S)-ethylmalonyl-CoA + NADP(+) = (2E)-butenoyl-CoA + CO2 + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
