</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.105">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-methylene-furan-3-one reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>enone oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.105#SIPBAE1B7E09C8C94C9"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.105#SIP984E469435E35A47"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.105#SIP08FD3AE7A30DAEA6"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme was dicovered in strawberry (Fragaria x ananassa), where it produces furaneol, one of the major aroma compounds in the fruits.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has also been detected in tomato (Solanum lycopersicum) and pineapple (Ananas comosus).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also act on derivatives substituted at the methylene functional group.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae acts on (2E)-2-ethylidene-4-hydroxy-5-methylfuran-3(2H)-one and produces homofuraneol, an important aroma compound in soy sauce and miso.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NADPH is the preferred cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16517758"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17636940"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23589283"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27865643"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.105#SIPBAE1B7E09C8C94C9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4-hydroxy-2,5-dimethyl-furan-3(2H)-one + NADP(+) = 4-hydroxy-5-methyl-2-methylenefuran-3(2H)-one + H(+) + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.105#SIP984E469435E35A47">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4-hydroxy-2,5-dimethyl-furan-3(2H)-one + NAD(+) = 4-hydroxy-5-methyl-2-methylenefuran-3(2H)-one + H(+) + NADH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.105#SIP08FD3AE7A30DAEA6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-ethyl-4-hydroxy-5-methyl-3(2H)-furanone + NADP(+) = (2E)-2-ethylidene-4-hydroxy-5-methylfuran-3(2H)-one + H(+) + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
