</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.107">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sanguinarine reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.107#SIPEF8D90C92A1842B9"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.107#SIPC40401B099E05E14"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.107#SIPA6208E0802CF6EBC"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.107#SIP961B9241185E6618"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, purified from the California poppy (Eschscholzia californica), is involved in detoxifying the phytoalexin sanguinarine produced by poppy itself (cf. EC 1.5.3.12), when it binds to the cell wall of the poppy cell.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction with NADPH is up to three times faster than that with NADH at low concentrations (&lt;10 uM) of the dinucleotide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>At higher concentrations the reaction with NADPH is inhibited but not that with NADH.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17080644"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20378534"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.107#SIPEF8D90C92A1842B9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dihydrosanguinarine + NADP(+) = NADPH + sanguinarine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.107#SIPC40401B099E05E14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dihydrosanguinarine + NAD(+) = NADH + sanguinarine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.107#SIPA6208E0802CF6EBC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dihydrochelirubine + NAD(+) = chelirubine + NADH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.107#SIP961B9241185E6618">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dihydrochelirubine + NADP(+) = chelirubine + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
