<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.118">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>meromycolic acid enoyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.118#SIPDAF859F25A8E4CE1"/>
<rdfs:comment>InhA is a component of the fatty acid synthase (FAS) II system of Mycobacterium tuberculosis, catalyzing an enoyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase step.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme acts on very long and unsaturated fatty acids that form the meromycolic component of mycolic acids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It extends FASI-derived C20 fatty acids to form C60 to C90 mycolic acids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which forms a homotetramer, is the target of the preferred antitubercular drug isoniazid.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7599116"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10336454"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10708367"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10869086"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18552191"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25891098"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.118#SIPDAF859F25A8E4CE1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 2,3-saturated meromycolyl-[ACP] + NAD(+) = a trans-Delta(2)-meromycolyl-[ACP] + H(+) + NADH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
