<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.1.124">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2,4-dienoyl-CoA reductase [(3E)-enoyl-CoA-producing]</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Delta(2),Delta(4)-dienoyl-CoA reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.124#SIP86E4A97FE073F5F3"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.1.124#SIP7A409B5BC7180A3D"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, characterized from eukaryotic organisms, catalyzes the reduction of either (2E,4E)-2,4-dienoyl-CoA or (2E,4Z)-2,4-dienoyl-CoA to (3E)-3-enoyl-CoA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The best substrates for the enzyme from bovine liver have a chain-length of 8 or 10.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Mammals possess both mitochondrial and peroxisomal variants of this enzyme. cf. EC 1.3.1.34.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/729581"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6749495"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9268358"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10464321"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11514237"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15531764"/>
