<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.2.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-galactonolactone dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>galactonolactone dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GLDase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GLDHase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-galactono-gamma-lactone dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.2.3#SIPF38A06B76EADD0FC"/>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the final step in the biosynthesis of L-ascorbic acid in higher plants and in nearly all higher animals with the exception of primates and some birds.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Very specific for its substrate L-galactono-1,4-lactone as D-galactono-gamma-lactone, D-gulono-gamma-lactone, L-gulono-gamma-lactone, D-erythronic-gamma-lactone, D-xylonic-gamma-lactone, L-mannono-gamma-lactone, D-galactonate, D-glucuronate and D-gluconate are not substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>FAD, NAD(+), NADP(+) and O2 (cf. EC 1.3.3.12) cannot act as electron acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7775377"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9374475"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13126085"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13126087"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.2.3#SIPF38A06B76EADD0FC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4 Fe(III)-[cytochrome c] + L-galactono-1,4-lactone = 4 Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] + 5 H(+) + L-dehydroascorbate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
