<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.2.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>fumarate reductase (cytochrome)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.2.4#SIP199F4FAC5ABE1F04"/>
<rdfs:comment>Contains a non-covalently bound FAD cofactor and four heme c groups.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Shewanella frigidimarina, is a soluble periplasmic protein that functions as a terminal electron acceptor during anaerobic growth.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The direct electron donor is the membrane-bound tetraheme c-type cytochrome CymA (EC 7.1.1.8), which receives the electrons from the membrane quinol pool.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1333793"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7742319"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9579067"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10978153"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11004445"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12196158"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.2.4#SIP199F4FAC5ABE1F04">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome c] + succinate = 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] + fumarate + 2 H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
