<skos:prefLabel>oxazoline dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>azoline oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cyanobactin oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>thiazoline oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.3.16#SIPB737B084D283910D"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.3.16#SIP528733B74B305A73"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.3.16#SIPB24767736B7F53E8"/>
<rdfs:comment>Contains FMN.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme oxidizes 2-oxazoline, 5-methyl-2-oxazoline, and 2-thiazoline within peptides, which were formed by EC 6.2.2.2 and EC 6.2.2.3 to the respective pyrrole-type rings.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is found as either a stand-alone protein or as a domain within a multifunctional protein (the G protein) that also functions as a peptidase.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8895467"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15883371"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27841750"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30661981"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.3.-"/>
