<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.7.13">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3,8-divinyl protochlorophyllide a 8-vinyl-reductase (ferredoxin)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cyano-type divinyl chlorophyllide a 8-vinyl-reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.7.13#SIP43CA6402AFDF18F4"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.7.13#SIP9EDDDB95199281BC"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in many phototrophic bacteria, land plants, and some green and red algae, is involved in the production of monovinyl versions of (bacterio)chlorophyll pigments from their divinyl precursors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also act on 3,8-divinyl chlorophyllide a, 3,8-divinyl chlorophyll a, and chlorophyll c2. cf. EC 1.3.1.75.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17148453"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24151992"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24399236"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.7.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.7.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.7.13#SIP43CA6402AFDF18F4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + protochlorophyllide a = 3,8-divinyl protochlorophyllide a + 2 H(+) + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.7.13#SIP9EDDDB95199281BC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>chlorophyllide a + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = 3,8-divinyl chlorophyllide a + 2 H(+) + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
