<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.8.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.3.99.21"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(R)-benzylsuccinyl-CoA dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.8.3#SIP06CF6D100C28B93F"/>
<rdfs:comment>Contains a tightly-bound FAD cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike other acyl-CoA dehydrogenases, this enzyme exhibits high substrate- and enantiomer specificity; it is highly specific for (R)-benzylsuccinyl-CoA and is inhibited by (S)-benzylsuccinyl-CoA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Forms the third step in the anaerobic toluene metabolic pathway in Thauera aromatica.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Ferricenium ion is an effective artificial electron acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10589736"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12420174"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.8.-"/>
