<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.8.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.3.99.7"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase (ETF)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.8.6#SIPFF7D7D23DF9407F2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of glutaryl-CoA to glutaconyl-CoA (which remains bound to the enzyme), and the decarboxylation of the latter to crotonyl-CoA (cf. EC 7.2.4.5).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>FAD is the electron acceptor in the oxidation of the substrate, and its reoxidation by electron-transfer flavoprotein completes the catalytic cycle.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The anaerobic, sulfate-reducing bacterium Desulfococcus multivorans contains two glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenases: a decarboxylating enzyme (this entry), and a non-decarboxylating enzyme that only catalyzes the oxidation to glutaconyl-CoA (EC 1.3.99.32).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4304226"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8439237"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10446367"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17176108"/>
