<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.8.9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.3.99.3"/>
<skos:prefLabel>very-long-chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.8.9#SIPE85EFB17B93E7EB7"/>
<rdfs:comment>One of several enzymes that catalyze the first step in fatty acids beta-oxidation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is most active toward long-chain acyl-CoAs such as C14, C16 and C18, but is also active with very-long-chain acyl-CoAs up to 24 carbons.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It shows no activity for substrates of less than 12 carbons.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It's specific activity toward palmitoyl-CoA is more than 10-fold that of the long-chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase. cf. EC 1.3.8.1, EC 1.3.8.7 and EC 1.3.8.8.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1730632"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7769092"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18227065"/>
