<skos:prefLabel>dihydroorotate oxidase (fumarate)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DHOD</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DHODase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DHOdehase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dihydoorotic acid dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dihydroorotate dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dihydroorotate oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.98.1#SIPF57E519E0AD84FB2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction, which takes place in the cytosol, is the only redox reaction in the de novo biosynthesis of pyrimidine nucleotides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Molecular oxygen can replace fumarate in vitro.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Other class 1 dihydroorotate dehydrogenases use either NAD(+) (EC 1.3.1.14) or NADP(+) (EC 1.3.1.15) as electron acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The membrane bound class 2 dihydroorotate dehydrogenase (EC 1.3.5.2) uses quinone as electron acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9405053"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9655329"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12732650"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17617217"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18808149"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19932077"/>
