<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.98.5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>hydrogen peroxide-dependent heme synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>coproheme III oxidative decarboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.98.5#SIP9C672566111A89A5"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in a heme biosynthesis pathway found in Gram-positive bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The initial decarboxylation step is fast and yields the three-propanoate harderoheme isomer III.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The second decarboxylation is much slower, cf. EC 1.3.98.6.</rdfs:comment>
