<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.99.8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-furoyl-CoA dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>furoyl-CoA hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.99.8#SIPF5C71D75FB0B742A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The oxygen atom of the -OH produced is derived from water, not O2.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The actual oxidative step is probably dehydrogenation of a hydrated form -CHOH-CH2- to -C(OH)=CH-, which tautomerizes non-enzymically to -CO-CH2-, giving (5-oxo-4,5-dihydro-2-furoyl)-CoA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Methylene blue, nitro blue tetrazolium and a membrane fraction from Pseudomonas putida can act as acceptors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.99.8#SIPF5C71D75FB0B742A">
