<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.99.23">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>all-trans-retinol 13,14-reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(13,14)-all-trans-retinol saturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>retinol saturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RetSat</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.99.23#SIP78B231744AADFC02"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction is only known to occur in the opposite direction to that given above, with the enzyme being specific for all-trans-retinol as substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Neither all-trans-retinoic acid nor 9-cis, 11-cis or 13-cis-retinol isomers are substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>May play a role in the metabolism of vitamin A.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15358783"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
