<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.99.32">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase (acceptor)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.99.32#SIPF95287B8021E2608"/>
<rdfs:comment>The anaerobic, sulfate-reducing bacterium Desulfococcus multivorans contains two glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenases: a decarboxylating enzyme (EC 1.3.8.6), and a nondecarboxylating enzyme (this entry).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The two enzymes cause different structural changes around the glutaconyl carboxylate group, primarily due to the presence of either a tyrosine or a valine residue, respectively, at the active site.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19395484"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20486657"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.3.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.3.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.99.32#SIPF95287B8021E2608">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>A + glutaryl-CoA = (2E)-glutaconyl-CoA + AH2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
