<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.3.99.41">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-(methylsulfanyl)propanoyl-CoA 2-dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.3.99.41#SIPC239FDE2137C8FF7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in marine bacteria, participates in a 3-(methylsulfanyl)propanoate degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Based on similar enzymes, the in vivo electron acceptor is likely electron-transfer flavoprotein (ETF).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21562561"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28469605"/>
