<replaces rdf:resource="1.4.3.9"/>
<skos:prefLabel>monoamine oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>adrenaline oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>amine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>amine oxidase (flavin-containing)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tyraminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tyramine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.4.3.4#SIP8E58D62A7B2F0691"/>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the oxidative deamination of neurotransmitters and biogenic amines.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Acts on primary amines, and also on some secondary and tertiary amines.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It differs from EC 1.4.3.21, as it can oxidize secondary and tertiary amines but not methylamine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Inhibited by acetylenic compounds such as chlorgyline, 1-deprenyl and pargyline but, unlike EC 1.4.3.21 and EC 1.4.3.22, it is not inhibited by semicarbazide.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2644497"/>
