<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.4.3.19">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glycine oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.4.3.19#SIP167B3AF47F4550D2"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.4.3.19#SIPFD87257234548AAF"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.4.3.19#SIPCDD7A91CD67364FE"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.4.3.19#SIP07DDC99B5D067A72"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Bacillus subtilis is active with glycine, sarcosine, N-ethylglycine, D-alanine, D-alpha-aminobutyrate, D-proline, D-pipecolate and N-methyl-D-alanine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It differs from EC 1.4.3.3 due to its activity on sarcosine and D-pipecolate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The intermediate 2-iminoacetate is used directly by EC 2.8.1.10.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9827558"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11744710"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.4.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.4.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
