<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.4.3.20">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-lysine 6-oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-lysine-epsilon-oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Lod</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>marinocine</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.4.3.20#SIPD394EA11E4DF89FB"/>
<rdfs:comment>Differs from EC 1.4.3.13 by using free L-lysine rather than the protein-bound form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>N(2)-acetyl-L-lysine is also a substrate, but N(6)-acetyl-L-lysine, which has an acetyl group at position 6, is not.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts on L-ornithine, D-lysine and 4-hydroxy-L-lysine, but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The amines cadaverine and putrescine are not substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16547036"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17030025"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.4.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.4.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.4.3.20#SIPD394EA11E4DF89FB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + L-lysine + O2 = (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate + H2O2 + NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
