<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.4.3.22">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.4.3.6"/>
<skos:prefLabel>diamine oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>amine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>amine oxidase (copper-containing)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CAO</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>copper amine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Cu-containing amine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>diamino oxhydrase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>histaminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>histamine deaminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>semicarbazide-sensitive amine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>SSAO</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.4.3.22#SIP694CF45EE692D5B3"/>
<rdfs:comment>A group of enzymes that oxidize diamines, such as histamine, and also some primary monoamines but have little or no activity toward secondary and tertiary amines.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They are copper quinoproteins (2,4,5-trihydroxyphenylalanine quinone) and, like EC 1.4.3.21 but unlike EC 1.4.3.4, they are sensitive to inhibition by carbonyl-group reagents, such as semicarbazide.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/182134"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8182053"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10668504"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12072962"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.4.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.4.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.4.3.22#SIP694CF45EE692D5B3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + histamine + O2 = H2O2 + imidazole-4-acetaldehyde + NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
