<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.5.1.39">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.5.1.29"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.6.8.1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>FMN reductase [NAD(P)H]</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.1.39#SIPAD05C3AE5B78A5AC"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.1.39#SIPA179038050CDCA67"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can utilize NADH and NADPH with similar reaction rates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Different from EC 1.5.1.42 and EC 1.5.1.38.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The luminescent bacterium Vibrio harveyi possesses all three enzymes, while the bacterium Aliivibrio fischeri contains only this non-specific type.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also reduces riboflavin and FAD, but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/222213"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6981058"/>
