<activity rdf:resource="1.5.3.5#SIPD3F4F3D30C772161"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which participates in nicotine degradation, is specific for the (S) isomer of 6-hydroxynicotine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The bacterium Arthrobacter nicotinovorans, in which this enzyme was originally discovered, has a different enzyme that catalyzes a similar reaction with the less common (R)-isomer (cf. EC 1.5.3.6).</rdfs:comment>
