<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.5.3.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(R)-6-hydroxynicotine oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>6-hydroxy-D-nicotine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-6-hydroxynicotine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.3.6#SIP0A85200F67DE6D70"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which participates in nicotine degradation, is specific for (R) isomer of 6-hydroxynicotine, derived from the uncommon (R)-nicotine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The bacterium Arthrobacter nicotinovorans, in which this enzyme was originally discovered, has a different enzyme that catalyzes a similar reaction with the (S)-isomer (cf. EC 1.5.3.5).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3622516"/>
