<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.5.3.10">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dimethylglycine oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.3.10#SIP2B80A05235665CCC"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.3.10#SIP40142604337F90E0"/>
<rdfs:comment>A flavoprotein (FAD).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Arthrobacter globiformis, contains two active sites connected by a large 'reaction chamber'.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>An imine intermediate is transferred between the sites, eliminating the production of toxic formaldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the absence of folate the enzyme does form formaldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Does not oxidize sarcosine. cf. EC 1.5.8.4.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11422368"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11926836"/>
