<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.5.5.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.5.99.8"/>
<skos:prefLabel>proline dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.5.2#SIP9DA54DA0DFA23DD3"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.5.2#SIP390860C17C15ABAE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The electrons from L-proline are transferred to the FAD cofactor, and from there to a quinone acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In many organisms, ranging from bacteria to mammals, proline is oxidized to glutamate in a two-step process involving this enzyme and EC 1.2.1.88.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Both activities are carried out by the same enzyme in enterobacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/355248"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1618807"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22040654"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.5.5.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.5.5.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
