<skos:prefLabel>methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase (ferredoxin)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.5.7.1#SIPEE9939B2ADF098E8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Clostridium formicoaceticum catalyzes the reduction of methylene blue, menadione, benzyl viologen, rubredoxin or FAD with 5-methyltetrahydrofolate and the oxidation of reduced ferredoxin or FADH2 with 5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However, unlike EC 1.5.1.20, EC 1.5.1.53, or EC 1.5.1.24, there is no activity with either NADH or NADP(+).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6381490"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.5.7.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.5.7.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.5.7.1#SIPEE9939B2ADF098E8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(6S)-5-methyl-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = (6R)-5,10-methylene-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + 2 H(+) + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6381490">
