<skos:prefLabel>NADPH dehydrogenase (quinone)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.6.5.10#SIPF182BFBDFF0FC27F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Escherichia coli is specific for NADPH and is most active with quinone derivatives and ferricyanide as electron acceptors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Menaquinone can act as acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from hog liver is inhibited by dicoumarol and folic acid derivatives but not by 2,4-dinitrophenol.</rdfs:comment>
