<skos:prefLabel>nitric oxide reductase [NAD(P)(+), nitrous oxide-forming]</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cytochrome P450nor</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>fungal nitric oxide reductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NOR</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.7.1.14#SIP17DD6113D1C50289"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.7.1.14#SIPA1650489834E9A44"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Fusarium oxysporum utilizes only NADH, but the isozyme from Trichosporon cutaneum utilizes both NADH and NADPH.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The electron transfer from NAD(P)H to heme occurs directly, not requiring flavin or other redox cofactors.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2040619"/>
