<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.7.2.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>hydrazine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.7.2.7#SIPD11EC580618FB11F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from anaerobic ammonia oxidizers (anammox bacteria), is one of only a few enzymes that are known to form an N-N bond (other examples include EC 1.7.1.14 and EC 4.8.1.1).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Candidatus Kuenenia stuttgartiensis is heterotrimeric and contains multiple c-type cytochromes.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21964329"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26479033"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.7.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.7.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.7.2.7#SIPD11EC580618FB11F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3 Fe(III)-[cytochrome c] + H2O + hydrazine = 3 Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] + 2 H(+) + NH4(+) + nitric oxide.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21964329">
