<skos:prefLabel>hydroxylamine oxidase (cytochrome)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>HAO</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>hydroxylamine oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>hydroxylamine oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.7.3.6#SIP6019CE19D610DD68"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the heterotrophic nitrifying bacterium Paracoccus denitrificans contains three to five non-heme, non-iron-sulfur iron atoms and interacts with cytochrome c556 and pseudoazurin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Under anaerobic conditions in vitro only nitrous oxide is formed.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Presumably nitroxyl is released and combines with a second nitroxyl to give nitrous oxide and water.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>When oxygen is present, nitrite is formed.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8253206"/>
