<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.8.1.16">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glutathione amide reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GAR</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.8.1.16#SIP45F933CD7F10080E"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme restores glutathione amide disulfide, which is produced during the reduction of peroxide by EC 1.11.1.17 back to glutathione amide (it catalyzes the reaction in the opposite direction to that shown).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme belongs to the family of flavoprotein disulfide oxidoreductases, but unlike other members of the family, which are specific for NADPH, it prefers NADH.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11399772"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11807270"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.8.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.8.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
