<activity rdf:resource="1.8.1.21#SIP384D359A050F84A9"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme's activity has been demonstrated in the bacterium Thiobacillus thioparus E6.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The methanethiol formed is eventually oxidized to sulfate and carbon dioxide, and the latter assimilated for autotrophic growth.</rdfs:comment>
