<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.8.4.16">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>thioredoxin:protein disulfide reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.8.4.16#SIP546FE8B2FEFEE45A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The DsbD protein is found in Gram-negative bacteria and transfers electrons from cytoplasmic thioredoxin to the periplasmic substrate proteins DsbC, DsbG and CcmG, reducing disulfide bonds in the target proteins to dithiols.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NrdH redoxins, which are found in Gram-positive bacteria, catalyze a similar reaction.</rdfs:comment>
