</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.8.5.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bacterial sulfide:quinone reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>sulfide:quinone reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.8.5.4#SIP473058CDDCE214F4"/>
<rdfs:comment>Ubiquinone, plastoquinone or menaquinone can act as acceptor in different species.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the formation of sulfur globules.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It repeats the catalytic cycle without releasing the product, producing a polysulfide of up to 10 sulfur atoms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction stops when the maximum length of the polysulfide that can be accommodated in the sulfide oxidation pocket is achieved.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also plays an important role in anoxygenic bacterial photosynthesis. cf. EC 1.8.5.8.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8119908"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9639604"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10816041"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19438211"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20303979"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20691146"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.8.5.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.8.5.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
