<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.8.5.9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>protein dithiol:quinone oxidoreductase DsbB</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.8.5.9#SIPAAADCB2C014D2176"/>
<rdfs:comment>DsbB is a protein found in Gram-negative bacteria that functions within a pathway for protein disulfide bond formation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of the DsbA protein by generating disulfide bonds de novo via the reduction of membrane quinones. cf. EC 1.8.4.15.</rdfs:comment>
