<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.8.7.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ferredoxin:CoB-CoM heterodisulfide reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.8.7.3#SIP1CDF9B460B1E5770"/>
<rdfs:comment>HdrABC is an enzyme complex that is found in most methanogens and catalyzes the reduction of the CoB-CoM heterodisulfide back to CoB and CoM.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>HdrA contains a FAD cofactor that acts as the entry point for electrons, which are transferred via HdrC to the HdrB catalytic subunit.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>One form of the enzyme from Methanosarcina acetivorans (HdrA2B2C2) can also catalyze EC 1.8.98.4. cf. EC 1.8.98.5, EC 1.8.98.6, and EC 1.8.98.1.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19968794"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28174314"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.8.7.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.8.7.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.8.7.3#SIP1CDF9B460B1E5770">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>coenzyme B + coenzyme M + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = coenzyme M-coenzyme B heterodisulfide + 2 H(+) + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19968794">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
