<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.11">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ubiquinol oxidase (non-electrogenic)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cyanide-insensitive oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>plant alternative oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ubiquinol oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.10.3.11#SIP059EE39684A97DE2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, described from the mitochondria of plants and some fungi and protists, is an alternative terminal oxidase that is not sensitive to cyanide inhibition and does not generate a proton motive force.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The function of this oxidase is believed to be dissipating excess reducing power, minimizing oxidative stress, and optimizing photosynthesis in response to changing conditions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7698344"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11106766"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16657603"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20169184"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22848123"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.10.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.10.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.11#SIP059EE39684A97DE2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 a ubiquinol + O2 = 2 a ubiquinone + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
