<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.16">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dihydrophenazinedicarboxylate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.10.3.16#SIP431A6F2E4C31568E"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.10.3.16#SIP12E4E69D4ED293EE"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.10.3.16#SIP5E22D8CE8851B9BE"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.10.3.16#SIPEA68940CC8630E02"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, isolated from the bacteria Pseudomonas fluorescens 2-79 and Burkholderia lata 383, is involved in biosynthesis of the reduced forms of phenazine, phenazine-1-carboxylate, and phenazine-1,6-dicarboxylate, where it catalyzes multiple reactions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23897464"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.10.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.10.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.16#SIP431A6F2E4C31568E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(1R,6R)-1,4,5,5a,6,9-hexahydrophenazine-1,6-dicarboxylate + O2 = (1R,10aS)-1,4,10,10a-tetrahydrophenazine-1,6-dicarboxylate + H2O2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.16#SIP12E4E69D4ED293EE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(1R,10aS)-1,4,10,10a-tetrahydrophenazine-1,6-dicarboxylate + O2 = (5aS)-5,5a-dihydrophenazine-1,6-dicarboxylate + H2O2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.16#SIP5E22D8CE8851B9BE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(1R,10aS)-1,4,10,10a-tetrahydrophenazine-1-carboxylate + O2 = (10aS)-10,10a-dihydrophenazine-1-carboxylate + H2O2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.16#SIPEA68940CC8630E02">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(1R)-1,4,5,10-tetrahydrophenazine-1-carboxylate + O2 = (10aS)-10,10a-dihydrophenazine-1-carboxylate + H2O2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23897464">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/23897464"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23897464"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.17">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>superoxide oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cytochrome b561</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.10.3.17#SIPD0750B10296092F4"/>
<rdfs:comment>This membrane-bound, di-heme containing enzyme, identified in the bacterium Escherichia coli, is responsible for the detoxification of superoxide in the periplasm.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In vivo the reaction proceeds in the opposite direction of that shown and produces oxygen.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Superoxide production was only observed when the enzyme was incubated in vitro with an excess of ubiquinol.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3510204"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6097799"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29915379"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.10.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.10.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.10.3.17#SIPD0750B10296092F4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a ubiquinol + 2 O2 = a ubiquinone + 2 H(+) + 2 superoxide.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3510204">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/3510204"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3510204"/>
</rdf:Description>
