<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.1.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>peroxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>lactoperoxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.11.1.7#SIP38177ECA7712E837"/>
<rdfs:comment>Heme proteins with histidine as proximal ligand.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The iron in the resting enzyme is Fe(III).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They also peroxidize non-phenolic substrates such as 3,3',5,5'-tetramethylbenzidine (TMB) and 2,2'-azinobis(3-ethylbenzthiazoline-6-sulfonic acid) (ABTS).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Certain peroxidases (e.g. lactoperoxidase, SBP) oxidize bromide, iodide and thiocyanate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8180190"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9622531"/>
