</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.1.18">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bromide peroxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>bromoperoxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>eosinophil peroxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.11.1.18#SIP9AA229278E8D1298"/>
<rdfs:comment>Bromoperoxidases of red and brown marine algae (Rhodophyta and Phaeophyta) contain vanadate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They catalyze the bromination of a range of organic molecules such as sesquiterpenes, forming stable C-Br bonds.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Bromoperoxidases also oxidize iodides.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2400770"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10843856"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15133166"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15548002"/>
