<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.1.21">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>catalase peroxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.11.1.21#SIPFA1B4A1E097BBEE4"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.11.1.21#SIP35AB45D7459000EB"/>
<rdfs:comment>Differs from EC 1.11.1.7, peroxidase, in having a relatively high catalase (EC 1.11.1.6) activity with H2O2 as donor, releasing O2; both activities use the same heme active site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Mycobacterium tuberculosis it is responsible for activation of the commonly used antitubercular drug, isoniazid.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2029529"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3886630"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8631329"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15231843"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20434429"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.11.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.11.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.1.21#SIPFA1B4A1E097BBEE4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>AH2 + H2O2 = A + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.1.21#SIP35AB45D7459000EB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H2O2 = 2 H2O + O2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
