<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.2.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>myeloperoxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MPO</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>verdoperoxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.11.2.2#SIP02670BEDC7D62B5D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Is present in phagosomes of neutrophils and monocytes, where the hypochlorite produced is strongly bactericidal.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It differs from EC 1.11.1.10 in its preference for formation of hypochlorite over the chlorination of organic substrates under physiological conditions (pH 5-8).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Hypochlorite in turn forms a number of antimicrobial products (Cl2, chloramines, hydroxyl radical, singlet oxygen).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>MPO also oxidizes bromide, iodide and thiocyanate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the absence of halides, it oxidizes phenols and has a moderate peroxygenase activity toward styrene.</rdfs:comment>
