</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.2.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-tyrosine peroxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.11.2.6#SIPA1D584769BE80DB3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Streptomyces lincolnensis participates in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic lincomycin A, while that from Streptomyces refuineus is involved in anthramycin biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which contains a heme b cofactor, is rapidly inactivated in the presence of hydrogen peroxide, but the presence of L-tyrosine protects it. cf. EC 1.11.2.5.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9531633"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21919439"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.11.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.11.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.11.2.6#SIPA1D584769BE80DB3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O2 + L-tyrosine = H2O + L-dopa.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
