<skos:altLabel>linoleate dioxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>manganese lipoxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.45#SIP6FE17EF2BAD268A3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The product (9Z,12Z)-(11S)-11-hydroperoxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate, is converted, more slowly, into (9Z,11E)-(13R)-13-hydroperoxyoctadeca-9,11-dienoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the fungus Gaeumannomyces graminis requires Mn(2+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It also acts on alpha-linolenate, whereas gamma-linolenate is a poor substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Oleate and arachidonate are not substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9582345"/>
