<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.48">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-hydroxy-2-methylquinolin-4-one 2,4-dioxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(1H)-3-hydroxy-4-oxoquinaldine 2,4-dioxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.48#SIP52604C4D229191E4"/>
<rdfs:comment>Does not contain a metal center or organic cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Fission of two C-C bonds: 2,4-dioxygenolytic cleavage with concomitant release of carbon monoxide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Arthrobacter sp. can also act on 3-hydroxy-4-oxoquinoline, forming N-formylanthranilate and CO (cf. EC 1.13.11.47), but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8856057"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10482514"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.48#SIP52604C4D229191E4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3-hydroxy-2-methyl-1H-quinolin-4-one + O2 = CO + H(+) + N-acetylanthranilate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
