<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.55">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sulfur oxygenase/reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>sulfur oxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>sulfur oxygenase reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.55#SIP8F3CE6FC74A71CD7"/>
<rdfs:comment>Elemental sulfur is both the electron donor and one of the two known acceptors, the other being oxygen.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Thiosulfate is also observed as a product, but is likely formed non-enzymically by a reaction between sulfite and sulfur.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme differs from EC 1.13.11.18 and EC 1.12.98.4 in that both activities occur simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1522063"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2493451"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12664265"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15030315"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.55#SIP8F3CE6FC74A71CD7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4 H2O + O2 + 4 sulfur = 6 H(+) + 2 hydrogen sulfide + 2 sulfite.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
