<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.64">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>5-nitrosalicylate dioxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.64#SIP957AA0C1793A2B37"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the soil bacterium Bradyrhizobium sp. JS329, is involved in the pathway of 5-nitroanthranilate degradation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is unusual in being able to catalyze the ring fission without the requirement for prior removal of the nitro group.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product undergoes spontaneous lactonization, with concurrent elimination of the nitro group.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20081004"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21498645"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.64#SIP957AA0C1793A2B37">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>5-nitrosalicylate + O2 = 2-oxo-3-(5-oxofuran-2-ylidene)propanoate + H(+) + nitrite.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20081004">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20081004"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20081004"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21498645">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21498645"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21498645"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.65">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.13.164"/>
<skos:prefLabel>carotenoid isomerooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.65#SIP26DAEB0BAE7873B3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the moth Galleria mellonella and the fruit fly Drosophila melanogaster, is involved in the synthesis of retinal from dietary caroteoids in insects.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme accepts different all-trans carotenoids, including beta-carotene, alpha-carotene and lutein, and catalyzes the symmetrical cleavage of the carotenoid and the simultaneous isomerization of only one of the products to a cis configuration.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>When the substrate is hydroxylated only in one side (as in cryptoxanthin), the enzyme preferentially isomerizes the hydroxylated part of the molecule.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19020100"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.65#SIP26DAEB0BAE7873B3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>all-trans-zeaxanthin + O2 = (3R)-11-cis-3-hydroxyretinal + (3R)-all-trans-3-hydroxyretinal.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19020100">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19020100"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19020100"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.66">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>hydroquinone 1,2-dioxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>hydroquinone dioxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.66#SIP78A388D19FEF7431"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is an extradiol-type dioxygenase, and is a member of the nonheme-iron(II)-dependent dioxygenase family.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes the ring cleavage of a wide range of hydroquinone substrates to produce the corresponding 4-hydroxymuconic semialdehydes.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10542173"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18502867"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20466541"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.66#SIP78A388D19FEF7431">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>hydroquinone + O2 = (2E,4Z)-4-hydroxy-6-oxohexa-2,4-dienoate + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10542173">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/10542173"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10542173"/>
</rdf:Description>
