<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.72">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-hydroxyethylphosphonate dioxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>HEPD</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.72#SIPDE154A967F015096"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from some bacteria including Streptomyces hygroscopicus and Streptomyces viridochromogenes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The pro-R hydrogen at C-2 of the ethyl group is retained by the formate ion.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Any stereochemistry at C-1 of the ethyl group is lost.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>One atom from dioxygen is present in each product.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in phosphinothricin biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
