<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.79">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.99.40"/>
<skos:prefLabel>aerobic 5,6-dimethylbenzimidazole synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>flavin reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.11.79#SIP8520F52DFB91F5D4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes a complex oxygen-dependent conversion of reduced flavin mononucleotide to form 5,6-dimethylbenzimidazole, the lower ligand of vitamin B12.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This conversion involves many sequential steps in two distinct stages, and an alloxan intermediate that acts as a proton donor, a proton acceptor, and a hydride acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The C-2 of 5,6-dimethylbenzimidazole is derived from C-1' of the ribityl group of FMNH2 and 2-H from the ribityl 1'-pro-S hydrogen.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While D-erythrose 4-phosphate has been shown to be one of the by-products, the nature of the other product(s) has not been verified yet.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17301238"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17377573"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17377583"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21344938"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23457476"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.13.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.11.79#SIP8520F52DFB91F5D4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>FMNH2 + O2 = 5,6-dimethylbenzimidazole + D-erythrose 4-phosphate + dialurate + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
