<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.12.19">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-oxoglutarate dioxygenase (ethylene-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ethylene-forming enzyme</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.13.12.19#SIP44891523B66EF240"/>
<rdfs:comment>This is one of two simultaneous reactions catalyzed by the enzyme, which is responsible for ethylene production in bacteria of the Pseudomonas syringae group.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the other reaction (EC 1.14.11.34) the enzyme catalyzes the mono-oxygenation of both 2-oxoglutarate and L-arginine, forming succinate, carbon dioxide and L-hydroxyarginine, which is subsequently cleaved into guanidine and (S)-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes catalyze two cycles of the ethylene-forming reaction for each cycle of the succinate-forming reaction, so that the stoichiometry of the products ethylene and succinate is 2:1.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1445291"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1445325"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1770346"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.13.12.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.13.12.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.13.12.19#SIP44891523B66EF240">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-oxoglutarate + 2 H(+) + O2 = 3 CO2 + ethene + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
