<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.11.33">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>DNA oxidative demethylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>alkylated DNA repair protein</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.33#SIP07A7AB432C78FA1B"/>
<rdfs:comment>Activity is slightly stimulated by ascorbate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes oxidative demethylation of the DNA base lesions N(1)-methyladenine, N(3)-methylcytosine, N(1)-methylguanine, and N(3)-methylthymine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It works better on single-stranded DNA (ssDNA) and is capable of repairing damaged bases in RNA.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12226668"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19852088"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21068844"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.11.33#SIP07A7AB432C78FA1B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-oxoglutarate + a methylated nucleobase within DNA + O2 = a nucleobase within DNA + CO2 + formaldehyde + succinate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
