<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.11.65">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-dimethyl-L-lysine(9) demethylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.65#SIP3295E4F5B64C1BCA"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires iron(II).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes a group of enzymes that demethylate N-methylated Lys-9 residues in the tail of the histone protein H3 (H3K9).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This lysine residue can exist in three methylation states (mono-, di- and trimethylated), but this group of enzymes only act on the the di- and mono-methylated forms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes are dioxygenases and act by hydroxylating the methyl group, forming an unstable hemiaminal that leaves as formaldehyde, cf. EC 1.14.11.66.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16603237"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17938240"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20208542"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24009392"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24334705"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.11.65#SIP3295E4F5B64C1BCA">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 2-oxoglutarate + N(6),N(6)-dimethyl-L-lysyl(9)-[histone H3] + 2 O2 = 2 CO2 + 2 formaldehyde + L-lysyl(9)-[histone H3] + 2 succinate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
