<rdfs:comment>This entry describes a group of enzymes that demethylate N-methylated Lys-9 residues in the tail of the histone protein H3 (H3K9).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This lysine residue can exist in three methylation states (mono-, di- and trimethylated), but this group of enzymes only act on the the tri- and di-methylated forms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes are dioxygenases and act by hydroxylating the methyl group, forming an unstable hemiaminal that leaves as formaldehyde, cf. EC 1.14.11.65.</rdfs:comment>
