<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-trimethyl-L-lysine(4) demethylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.67#SIP9EB921F37CF7CF2E"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires iron(II).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes a group of enzymes that demethylate N-methylated L-lysine residues at position 4 of histone H3 (H3K4).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes are dioxygenases and act by hydroxylating the methyl group, forming an unstable hemiaminal that leaves as formaldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They can act on tri-, di-, and mono-methylated forms.</rdfs:comment>
