<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-trimethyl-L-lysine(27) demethylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.68#SIP4A5B15B771588198"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires iron(II).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes a group of enzymes that demethylate N-methylated L-lysine residues at position 27 of histone H3 (H3K27).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes are dioxygenases and act by hydroxylating the methyl group, forming an unstable hemiaminal that leaves as formaldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They can act on tri- and di-methylated forms, but have no activity with the mono-methylated form.</rdfs:comment>
