<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.11.69">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-trimethyl-L-lysine(36) demethylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.69#SIPB6F1859CE29EA125"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires iron(II).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes a group of enzymes that demethylate N-methylated Lys(36) residues in the tail of the histone protein H3 (H3K36).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This lysine residue can exist in three methylation states (mono-, di- and trimethylated), but this group of enzymes only act on the the tri- and di-methylated forms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes are dioxygenases and act by hydroxylating the methyl group, forming an unstable hemiaminal that leaves as formaldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Since trimethylation of H3K36 enhances transcription, this enzyme acts as a transcription repressor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes that possess this activity often also catalyze the activity of EC 1.14.11.66, cf. EC 1.14.11.27.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16603238"/>
