<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.11.73">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[protein]-arginine 3-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.73#SIP19BB2BE78EB1A3D9"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from humans, catalyzes the stereoselective formation of the (2S,3R)-hydroxy-L-arginine stereoisomer.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>So far the enzyme has been shown to act on two substrates - the 40S ribosomal protein S6 (RPS6), which is hydroxylated at R137, and, at a lower activity, RCCD1, a protein involved in chromatin stability, which is hydroxylated at R141.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Even though the same stereoisomer is produced by the bacterial EC 1.14.11.47, the two enzymes do not exhibit any cross-reactivity on their respective ribosomal protein substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29563586"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
