</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.11.80">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.11.n2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>methylcytosine dioxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.80#SIP464643CB1BC3B121"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.80#SIP16F6666B6F0E7E58"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.11.80#SIP3E797381C9F3CB84"/>
<rdfs:comment>The TET proteins mediate iterative oxidation of 5-methylcytosine in DNA (5mc) to 5-hydroxymethylcytosine (5hmC), 5-formylcytosine (5fC), and 5-carboxylcytosine (5caC).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>5fC and 5caC are recognized by EC 3.2.2.29, which excises them, leaving an apyrimidinic site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Coupled with the base excision repair (BER) pathway, these activities result in a cytosine demethylation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
