<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.12.13">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-halobenzoate 1,2-dioxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-chlorobenzoate 1,2-dioxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.12.13#SIP9DFA4A08741E4269"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.12.13#SIPC4427E862F10E0E6"/>
<rdfs:comment>A multicomponent enzyme system composed of a dioxygenase component and an electron transfer component.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The latter contains FAD.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Burkholderia cepacia 2CBS, has a broad substrate specificity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Substrates include 2-fluorobenzoate, 2-chlorobenzoate, 2-bromobenzoate, and 2-iodobenzoate, which are processed in this order of preference.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1370284"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2610934"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7530709"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.12.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.12.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
