<rdfs:comment>Also acts on a number of analogs of 3-hydroxybenzoate substituted in the 2, 4, 5 and 6 positions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NADPH can act instead of NADH, more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4357436"/>
