<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>magnesium-protoporphyrin IX monomethyl ester (oxidative) cyclase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Mg-protoporphyrin IX monomethyl ester oxidative cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.81#SIP06B86DD64F443769"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of chlorophyllide a in aerobic organisms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The same transformation is achieved in anaerobic organisms by EC 1.21.98.3.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Some facultative phototrophic bacteria, such as Rubrivivax gelatinosus, possess both enzymes.</rdfs:comment>
