<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.84">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>4-hydroxyacetophenone monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>HAPMO</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.84#SIP8CFE4935329FC9AD"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Pseudomonas fluorescens ACB catalyzes the conversion of a wide range of acetophenone derivatives.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Highest activity occurs with compounds bearing an electron-donating substituent at the para position of the aromatic ring.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the absence of substrate, the enzyme can act as an NADPH oxidase (EC 1.6.3.1).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11322873"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12514023"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.84#SIP8CFE4935329FC9AD">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4'-hydroxyacetophenone + H(+) + NADPH + O2 = 4-acetoxyphenol + H2O + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
