<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.111">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.14.6"/>
<skos:prefLabel>methanesulfonate monooxygenase (NADH)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mesylate monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>methanesulfonic acid monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MSAMO</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MSA monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.111#SIP15075E8B9AB23F0A"/>
<rdfs:comment>Methanesulfonate is the simplest of the sulfonates and is a substrate for the growth of certain methylotrophic microorganisms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Compared with EC 1.14.14.5, this enzyme has a restricted substrate range that includes only the short-chain aliphatic sulfonates (methanesulfonate to butanesulfonate) and excludes all larger molecules, such as arylsulfonates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Methylosulfonomonas methylovora is a multicomponent system comprising an hydroxylase, a reductase (MsmD) and a ferredoxin (MsmC).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The hydroxylase has both large (MsmA) and small (MsmB) subunits, with each large subunit containing a Rieske-type [2Fe-2S] cluster.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8932698"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10094704"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.111#SIP15075E8B9AB23F0A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>methanesulfonate + NADH + O2 = formaldehyde + H2O + NAD(+) + sulfite.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
