<skos:prefLabel>4-nitrocatechol 4-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.166#SIP250F5FFDF073E63C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.166#SIP4DE019D38268EC92"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of 4-nitrocatechol with the concomitant removal of the nitro group as nitrite.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Forms a two-component system with a flavoprotein reductase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from the bacteria Lysinibacillus sphaericus JS905 and Rhodococcus sp. strain PN1 were shown to also catalyze EC 1.14.13.29, while the enzyme from Pseudomonas sp. WBC-3 was shown to also catalyze EC 1.14.13.167.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9647818"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15262926"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19218392"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.166#SIP250F5FFDF073E63C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4-nitrocatechol + NADPH + O2 = 2-hydroxy-1,4-benzoquinone + H2O + NADP(+) + nitrite.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.166#SIP4DE019D38268EC92">
