<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.187">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-evernosamine nitrososynthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.187#SIP05D021790E37F49A"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from the bacterium Micromonospora carbonacea var. africana.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The nitroso group is probably spontaneously oxidized to a nitro group giving dTDP-beta-L-evernitrose, which is involved in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic everninomycin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction was studied using dTDP-beta-L-4-epi-vancosamine (dTDP-4-O-desmethyl-beta-L-evernitrosamine).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18983146"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20866105"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.187#SIP05D021790E37F49A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dTDP-beta-L-evernosamine + H(+) + 2 NADPH + 2 O2 = dTDP-2,3,6-trideoxy-3-C-methyl-4-O-methyl-3-nitroso-beta-L-arabino-hexopyranose + 3 H2O + 2 NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
