<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.195">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-ornithine N(5)-monooxygenase (NADPH)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ornithine hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.195#SIP453EB8A78C03A9C0"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of N(5)-hydroxy-L-ornithine, N(5)-formyl-N(5)-hydroxy-L-ornithine or N(5)-acetyl-N(5)-hydroxy-L-ornithine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These nonproteinogenic amino acids are building blocks of siderophores produced by some bacteria (e.g. Streptomyces coelicolor, Saccharopolyspora erythraea and Pseudomonas aeruginosa).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is specific for NADPH. cf. EC 1.14.13.196.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17015659"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17900176"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18452021"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21650455"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
