<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.196">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-ornithine N(5)-monooxygenase [NAD(P)H]</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.196#SIP453EB8A78C03A9C0"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.196#SIP06CE11DD5C3244BB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the pathogenic fungus Aspergillus fumigatus catalyzes a step in the biosynthesis of the siderophores triacetylfusarinine and desferriferricrocin, while the enzyme from the bacterium Kutzneria sp. 744 is involved in the biosynthesis of piperazate, a building block of the kutzneride family of antifungal antibiotics.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity of the fungal enzyme is higher with NADPH, due to the fact that following the reduction of the flavin, NADP(+) (but not NAD(+)) stabilizes the C4a-hydroperoxyflavin intermediate that oxidizes the substrate. cf. EC 1.14.13.195.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20614882"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22465572"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22522643"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22928747"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
