<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.212">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>1,3,7-trimethyluric acid 5-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.212#SIP0AFFEC3129FD82DF"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp. CBB1, is part of the bacterial C-8 oxidation-based caffeine degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product decomposes spontaneously to a racemic mixture of 3,6,8-trimethylallantoin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme shows no acitivity with urate. cf. EC 1.14.13.113.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22609920"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25678373"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.212#SIP0AFFEC3129FD82DF">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>1,3,7-trimethylurate + H(+) + NADH + O2 = 1,3,7-trimethyl-5-hydroxyisourate + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
