<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.215">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>protoasukamycin 4-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.215#SIP79987A8F2B2C23F9"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces nodosus subsp. asukaensis, is involved in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic asukamycin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23890006"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.215#SIP79987A8F2B2C23F9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + NADH + O2 + protoasukamycin = 4-hydroxyprotoasukamycin + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23890006">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/23890006"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23890006"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.216">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>asperlicin C monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.216#SIP89DBB7A4E5B28C5E"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.216#SIP5AEB3D5CE0524B7F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the fungus Aspergillus alliaceus, contains an FAD cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme inserts a hydroxyl group, leading to formation of a N-C bond that creates an additional cycle between the bicyclic indole and the tetracyclic core moieties, resulting in the heptacyclic asperlicin E.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23030663"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.216#SIP89DBB7A4E5B28C5E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>asperlicin C + H(+) + NADH + O2 = asperlicin E + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.216#SIP5AEB3D5CE0524B7F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>asperlicin C + H(+) + NADPH + O2 = asperlicin E + H2O + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23030663">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/23030663"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23030663"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.217">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>protodeoxyviolaceinate monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>protoviolaceinate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.217#SIP6A73A5C16519EFD9"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.217#SIP4937D28C8D7E7F94"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.217#SIP6E68D05F41B41EFB"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.217#SIP342F57087DB0ADBD"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.217#SIP3CFBC912B88631C5"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Chromobacterium violaceum, participates in the biosynthesis of the violet pigment violacein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The immediate product, protoviolaceinate, can be acted upon by EC 1.14.13.224, leading to violacein production.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However, it is very labile, and in the presence of oxygen can be converted to the shunt product proviolacein.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17176066"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17925955"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.217#SIP6A73A5C16519EFD9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + NADPH + O2 + protodeoxyviolaceinate = H2O + NADP(+) + protoviolaceinate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.217#SIP4937D28C8D7E7F94">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + NADH + O2 + protodeoxyviolaceinate = H2O + NAD(+) + protoviolaceinate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.217#SIP6E68D05F41B41EFB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + NADPH + 2 O2 + protodeoxyviolaceinate = CO2 + 2 H2O + NADP(+) + proviolacein.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.217#SIP342F57087DB0ADBD">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + NADH + 2 O2 + protodeoxyviolaceinate = CO2 + 2 H2O + NAD(+) + proviolacein.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.217#SIP3CFBC912B88631C5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + O2 + protoviolaceinate = CO2 + H2O + proviolacein.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17176066">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17176066"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17176066"/>
</rdf:Description>
