<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.218">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>5-methylphenazine-1-carboxylate 1-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.218#SIP37431B50EA622113"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.218#SIPFBC1342597A8CA46"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa, is involved in the biosynthesis of pyocyanine, a toxin produced and secreted by the organism.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also act on phenazine-1-carboxylate, converting it into 1-hydroxyphenazine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11591691"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17253782"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18416536"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.218#SIP37431B50EA622113">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>5-methyl-phenazine-1-carboxylate + 2 H(+) + NADH + O2 = CO2 + H2O + NAD(+) + pyocyanin.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.218#SIPFBC1342597A8CA46">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + NADH + O2 + phenazine-1-carboxylate = 1-hydroxyphenazine + CO2 + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
