</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.222">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>aurachin C monooxygenase/isomerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>aurachin C monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.222#SIP71E7950FAFFFE0A5"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.222#SIP8D4E4E22F9C1CFF6"/>
<rdfs:comment>The aurachin C monooxygenase from the bacterium Stigmatella aurantiaca accepts both NADH and NADPH as cofactor, but has a preference for NADH.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes the initial steps in the conversion of aurachin C to aurachin B.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The FAD-dependent monooxygenase catalyzes the epoxidation of the C2-C3 double bond of aurachin C, which is followed by a semipinacol rearrangement, causing migration of the farnesyl group from C3 to C4.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22907798"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.222#SIP71E7950FAFFFE0A5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>aurachin C + H(+) + NADH + O2 = 4-hydroxy-2-methyl-3-oxo-[(2E,6E)-farnesyl]-3,4-dihydroquinoline 1-oxide + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.222#SIP8D4E4E22F9C1CFF6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>aurachin C + H(+) + NADPH + O2 = 4-hydroxy-2-methyl-3-oxo-[(2E,6E)-farnesyl]-3,4-dihydroquinoline 1-oxide + H2O + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22907798">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/22907798"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22907798"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.223">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-hydroxy-4-methyl-anthranilyl-[aryl-carrier protein] 5-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.223#SIPC5599DDBDE1285EA"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptosporangium sibiricum, is involved in the biosynthesis of the antitumor antibiotic sibiromycin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is not active with free 3-hydroxy-4-methylanthranilate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21612226"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.223#SIPC5599DDBDE1285EA">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3-hydroxy-4-methylanthranilyl-[aryl-carrier protein] + H(+) + NADH + O2 = 3,5-dihydroxy-4-methylanthranilyl-[aryl-carrier protein] + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
