</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.226">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acetone monooxygenase (methyl acetate-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.226#SIP514035464910AC5B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Gordonia sp. TY-5, is a Baeyer-Villiger type monooxygenase and participates in a propane utilization pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17071761"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.226#SIP514035464910AC5B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>acetone + H(+) + NADPH + O2 = H2O + methyl acetate + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17071761">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17071761"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17071761"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.227">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>propane 2-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.227#SIPBE5704607FAF2D9F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from several bacterial strains, is a multicomponent dinuclear iron monooxygenase that includes a hydroxylase, an NADH-dependent reductase, and a coupling protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme has several additional activities, including acetone monooxygenase (acetol-forming) and phenol 4-monooxygenase.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14645271"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17873074"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21183637"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.227#SIPBE5704607FAF2D9F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + NADH + O2 + propane = H2O + NAD(+) + propan-2-ol.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14645271">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/14645271"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14645271"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17873074">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17873074"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17873074"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21183637">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21183637"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21183637"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.228">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>jasmomic acid 12-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.228#SIP340B171B7987F923"/>
<rdfs:comment>Although believed to occur in plants, the enzyme has so far been characterized only from the rice blast fungus, Magnaporthe oryzae.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The fungus strategically deploys the enzyme to hydroxylate and inactivate endogenous jasmonate to evade the jasmonate-based innate immunity in rice plants.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26258762"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.228#SIP340B171B7987F923">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + jasmonate + NADPH + O2 = (1R,2R)-12-hydroxyjasmonate + H2O + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26258762">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26258762"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26258762"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.229">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tert-butanol monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tert-butyl alcohol monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.229#SIPE185EFEF2D820A35"/>
<rdfs:comment>Characterized from the bacterium Aquincola tertiaricarbonis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also act, with lower efficiency, on propan-2-ol, converting it to propane-1,2-diol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Depending on the substrate, the enzyme also catalyzes EC 1.14.19.48.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22194447"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.229#SIPE185EFEF2D820A35">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + NADPH + O2 + tert-butanol = 2-methylpropane-1,2-diol + H2O + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22194447">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/22194447"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22194447"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.230">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>butane monooxygenase (soluble)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.230#SIPA81DB56C561B74DC"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Thauera butanivorans, is similar to EC 1.14.13.25, but has a very low activity with methane.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also act on other C3-C6 linear and branched aliphatic alkanes with lower activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12427952"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17526838"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18281403"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19383682"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.230#SIPA81DB56C561B74DC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>butane + H(+) + NADH + O2 = butan-1-ol + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12427952">
