<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.240">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-polyprenylphenol 6-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.240#SIP8415F4471EA790C0"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.240#SIP9FC99F9A7DE20948"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli (UbiI) catalyzes the first hydroxylation during the aerobic biosynthesis of ubiquinone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Neisseria meningitidis (UbiM) can also catalyze the two additional hydroxylations that occur in the pathway (cf. EC 1.14.99.60).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23709220"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27822549"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
