<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.244">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phenol 2-monooxygenase (NADH)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.244#SIP8F0A899CB9B72DB7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Pseudomonas sp. CF600 and Acinetobacter radioresistens, consists of a multisubunit oxygenease component that contains the active site and a dinuclear iron center, a reductase component that contains FAD and one iron-sulfur cluster, and a regulatory component.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reductase component is responsible for transferring electrons from NADH to the dinuclear iron center.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2254258"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2254259"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8995386"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9012665"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12186554"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.244#SIP8F0A899CB9B72DB7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + NADH + O2 + phenol = catechol + H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
