<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.248">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-aspartate N-monooxygenase (nitrosuccinate-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.248#SIP6ACCEED48D0E41DE"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires FAD.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in some Actinobacteria, is involved in a pathway that forms nitrite, which is subsequently used to generate a diazo group in some secondary metabolites.</rdfs:comment>
