<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.13.251">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glycine betaine monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.13.251#SIPF9953C87E820B007"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Chromohalobacter salexigens, is involved in a degradation pathway of glycine betaine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is composed of two subunits - a ferredoxin reductase component that contains FAD, and a terminal oxygenase component that contains a [2Fe-2S] Rieske-type iron-sulfur cluster and a nonheme iron center.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17951379"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23524610"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29703733"/>
