<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.20">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phenol 2-monooxygenase (FADH2)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.20#SIP42AA120B13BB1446"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the ortho-hydroxylation of simple phenols into the corresponding catechols.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It accepts 4-methylphenol, 4-chlorophenol, and 4-fluorophenol as well as 4-nitrophenol, 3-nitrophenol, and resorcinol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is part of a two-component system that also includes an NADH-dependent flavin reductase. cf. EC 1.14.13.7.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is strictly dependent on FADH2 and does not accept FMNH2.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12968028"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14703520"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19787347"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.20#SIP42AA120B13BB1446">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>FADH2 + O2 + phenol = catechol + FAD + H(+) + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
