<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.24">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.13.159"/>
<skos:prefLabel>vitamin D 25-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP2R1</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>vitamin D2 25-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>vitamin D3 25-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.24#SIP183754EBACF022A1"/>
<rdfs:comment>A microsomal enzyme isolated from human and mouse liver that bioactivates vitamin D3.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While multiple isoforms (CYP27A1, CYP2J2/3, CYP3A4, CYP2D25 and CYP2C11) are able to catalyze the reaction in vitro, only CYP2R1 is thought to catalyze the reaction in humans in vivo.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The direct electron donor to the enzyme is EC 1.6.2.4.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12867411"/>
