<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.38">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.13.118"/>
<skos:prefLabel>valine N-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP79D1</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP79D2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.38#SIP170A8C4C7270779A"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes two successive N-hydroxylations of L-valine, the committed step in the biosynthesis of the cyanogenic glucoside linamarin in Manihot esculenta (cassava).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product of the two hydroxylations, N,N-dihydroxy-L-valine, is labile and undergoes dehydration and decarboxylation that produce the (E) isomer of the oxime.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is still not known whether the decarboxylation is spontaneous or catalyzed by the enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also accept L-isoleucine as substrate, with a lower activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is different from EC 1.14.14.39.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10636899"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15122013"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.38#SIP170A8C4C7270779A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-valine + 2 O2 + 2 reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = (E)-2-methylpropanal oxime + CO2 + 2 H(+) + 3 H2O + 2 oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
