<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.40">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.13.124"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.13.n1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phenylalanine N-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP79A2</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP79D16</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phenylalanine N-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.40#SIPABFE1D61381CA1DA"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, found in plants, catalyzes two successive N-hydroxylations of L-phenylalanine, a committed step in the biosynthesis of benzylglucosinolate and the cyanogenic glucosides (R)-prunasin and (R)-amygdalin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product of the two hydroxylations, N,N-dihydroxy-L-phenylalanine, is labile and undergoes dehydration followed by decarboxylation, producing an oxime.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is still not known whether the decarboxylation is spontaneous or catalyzed by the enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10799553"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25015725"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.40#SIPABFE1D61381CA1DA">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-phenylalanine + 2 O2 + 2 reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = (E)-phenylacetaldehyde oxime + CO2 + 2 H(+) + 3 H2O + 2 oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10799553">
