<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.47">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.13.165"/>
<skos:prefLabel>nitric-oxide synthase (flavodoxin)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>nitric oxide synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NO synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.47#SIPA25D82DD0D5FAFD5"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in bacteria and archaea, consist of only an oxygenase domain and functions together with bacterial ferredoxins or flavodoxins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The orthologous enzymes from plants and animals also contain a reductase domain and use only NADPH as the electron donor (cf. EC 1.14.13.39).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11856757"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12220171"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17127770"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19805284"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25194416"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
