</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.49">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>12-hydroxyjasmonoyl-L-amino acid 12-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP94C1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.49#SIPE7A709037A873A54"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in plants, acts on jasmonoyl-L-amino conjugates that have been hydroxylated at the C-12 position of the jasmonic acid chain by EC 1.14.14.48 further oxidizing that position to a carboxylate via an aldehyde intermediate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While the best studied substrate is (+)-7-iso-jasmonoyl-L-isoleucine, the enzyme was shown to be active with jasmonoyl-L-phenylalanine, and is likely to be active with other jasmonoyl-amino acid conjugates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22215670"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26164240"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27459369"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.49#SIPE7A709037A873A54">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 12-hydroxyjasmonyl-L-alpha-amino acid + 2 O2 + 2 reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = a 12-hydroxy-12-oxojasmonyl-L-alpha-amino acid + 3 H(+) + 3 H2O + 2 oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
