<skos:prefLabel>phenylacetonitrile alpha-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP3201B1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.77#SIP6EFA55EC790A04DA"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme has been characterized from the cyanogenic millipede Chamberlinius hualienensis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike plant enzymes that can catalyze this reaction (EC 1.14.14.44), this enzyme cannot act on phenylacetaldehyde oximes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can accept (4-hydroxyphenyl)acetonitrile, (2-methylphenyl)acetonitrile, and (3-methylphenyl)acetonitrile as substrates at a lower rate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28286729"/>
