<skos:prefLabel>2,5-diketocamphane 1,2-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2,5-diketocamphane 1,2-monooxygenase oxygenating component</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2,5-diketocamphane lactonizing enzyme</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>camphor 1,2-monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>camphor ketolactonase I</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.108#SIPCFD49184C7AEB308"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.108#SIPDF3B2E844356DDC7"/>
<rdfs:comment>A Baeyer-Villiger monooxygenase isolated from camphor-grown strains of Pseudomonas putida and encoded on the cam plasmid.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the degradation of (+)-camphor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Requires a dedicated NADH-FMN reductase (cf. EC 1.5.1.42).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Can accept several bicyclic ketones including (+)- and (-)-camphor and adamantanone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product spontaneously converts to [(1R)-2,2,3-trimethyl-5-oxocyclopent-3-enyl]acetate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1510672"/>
