<skos:prefLabel>(+)-abscisic acid 8'-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(+)-ABA 8'-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ABA 8'-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP707A1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.137#SIP7EBB0ABD94C411C4"/>
<rdfs:comment>A cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) protein found in plants.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the first step in the oxidative degradation of abscisic acid and is considered to be the pivotal enzyme in controlling the rate of degradation of this plant hormone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>CO inhibits the reaction, but its effects can be reversed by the presence of blue light.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The 8'-hydroxyabscisate formed can be converted into (-)-phaseic acid, most probably spontaneously.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9808729"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15064374"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
