<skos:altLabel>CYP90D1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.147#SIP85ADE1438933CDF4"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.147#SIP5568C6E7B2F418E5"/>
<rdfs:comment>A cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) protein involved in brassinosteroid biosynthesis in plants.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme has a relaxed substrate specificity, and C-23 hydroxylation can occur at different stages in the pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Arabidopsis thaliana two isozymes, encoded by the CYP90C1 and CYP90D1 genes, have redundant activities.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15703058"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17138693"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
