<skos:prefLabel>beta-amyrin 11-oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP88D6</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.152#SIP75A527ADB2594B59"/>
<rdfs:comment>A cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) protein from the plant Glycyrrhiza uralensis (Chinese licorice) that participates in the glycyrrhizin biosynthesis pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is also able to oxidize 30-hydroxy-beta-amyrin to 11alpha,30-dihydroxy-beta-amyrin but this is not thought to be part of glycyrrhizin biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18779566"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.152#SIP75A527ADB2594B59">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>beta-amyrin + 2 O2 + 2 reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = 11-oxo-beta-amyrin + 2 H(+) + 3 H2O + 2 oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
