<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.176">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.99.37"/>
<skos:prefLabel>taxadiene 5alpha-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.176#SIP66D2FE8B1B9F358B"/>
<rdfs:comment>This microsomal cytochrome-P450 (heme-thiolate) enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the diterpenoid antineoplastic drug taxol (paclitaxel).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction includes rearrangement of the 4(5)-double bond to a 4(20)-double bond, possibly through allylic oxidation.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8807878"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.176#SIP66D2FE8B1B9F358B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>O2 + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + taxa-4,11-diene = H(+) + H2O + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + taxa-4(20),11-dien-5alpha-ol.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8807878">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8807878"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8807878"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.177">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ultra-long-chain fatty acid omega-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP4F22</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.177#SIP73CAEDC6D3611A04"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.177#SIP6811B4AABD6FE371"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which is expressed in the epidermis of mammals, catalyzes the omega-hydroxylation of ultra-long-chain fatty acids (C28 to C36).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The products are incorporated into acylceramides, epidermis-specific ceramide species that are very important for skin barrier formation.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26056268"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.177#SIP73CAEDC6D3611A04">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an omega-methyl-ultra-long-chain fatty acid + O2 + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = an omega-hydroxy-ultra-long-chain fatty acid + H(+) + H2O + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.177#SIP6811B4AABD6FE371">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>O2 + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + triacontanoate = H(+) + H2O + omega-hydroxy-triacontanoate + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26056268">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26056268"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26056268"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.178">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>steroid 22S-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP90B1</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>steroid C-22 hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.178#SIPDDF496BD8C7F3B61"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.178#SIPB42E5558A025710F"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.14.178#SIPE464DA49BF2584D6"/>
<rdfs:comment>This plant cytochrome P450 (heme thiolate) enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of brassinosteroids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While in vivo substrates include C28-steroids such as campestanol, campesterol, and 6-oxocampestanol, the enzyme is able to catalyze the C-22 hydroxylation of a variety of C27, C28 and C29 steroids.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11319239"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11489171"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12350224"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16460510"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16960392"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.14.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.178#SIPDDF496BD8C7F3B61">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a C27-steroid + O2 + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = a (22S)-22-hydroxy C27-steroid + H(+) + H2O + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.178#SIPB42E5558A025710F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a C28-steroid + O2 + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = a (22S)-22-hydroxy C28-steroid + H(+) + H2O + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.14.178#SIPE464DA49BF2584D6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a C29-steroid + O2 + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = a (22S)-22-hydroxy C29-steroid + H(+) + H2O + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
