<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.20">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>heme oxygenase (biliverdin-producing, ferredoxin)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.15.20#SIP48FAC9C2938CBC4E"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in plants, algae, and cyanobacteria, participates in the biosynthesis of phytochromobilin and phytobilins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The terminal oxygen atoms that are incorporated into the carbonyl groups of pyrrole rings A and B of biliverdin are derived from two separate oxygen molecules.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The third oxygen molecule provides the oxygen atom that converts the alpha-carbon to CO.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike this enzyme, which uses ferredoxin as its electron donor, the electron source for the related mammalian enzyme (EC 1.14.14.18) is EC 1.6.2.4.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12167331"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15560792"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18846276"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.20#SIP48FAC9C2938CBC4E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>8 H(+) + heme b + 3 O2 + 6 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = biliverdin IXalpha + CO + Fe(2+) + 3 H2O + 6 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
