<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.23">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>chloroacetanilide N-alkylformylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.15.23#SIP8AF073C667A923CA"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Sphingomonas sp. DC-6, initiates the degradation of several chloroacetanilide herbicides, including alachlor, acetochlor, and butachlor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is a Rieske non-heme iron oxygenase, and requires a ferredoxin and EC 1.18.1.3 for activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24928877"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.23#SIP8AF073C667A923CA">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>butachlor + 2 H(+) + O2 + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = butyl formate + H2O + N-(2,6-diethylphenyl)-2-chloroacetamide + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
