<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.26">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>toluene methyl-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.15.26#SIP4C79E2E297BB04C7"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.15.26#SIP32134854D446827C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.15.26#SIP9806DE256C60A649"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from several Pseudomonas strains, catalyzes the first step in the degradation of toluenes and xylenes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has a broad substrate specificity and is also active with substituted compounds, such as chlorotoluenes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The electrons are provided by a reductase (EC 1.18.1.3) that transfers electrons from NADH via FAD and an [2Fe-2S] cluster.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also act on its products, producing gem-diols that spontaneously dehydrate to form aldehydes.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1327782"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1526468"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1999388"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9555884"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.26#SIP4C79E2E297BB04C7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + O2 + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + toluene = benzyl alcohol + H2O + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.26#SIP32134854D446827C">
