<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.15.29">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.13.141"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cholest-4-en-3-one 26-monooxygenase [(25S)-3-oxocholest-4-en-26-oate forming]</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cholest-4-en-3-one 26-monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cholest-4-en-3-one 27-monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP125</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CYP125A1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.15.29#SIP73A6B689193B9E9C"/>
<rdfs:comment>A cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) protein found in several bacterial pathogens.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in degradation of the host's cholesterol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes the hydroxylation of the C-26 carbon, followed by oxidation of the alcohol to the carboxylic acid via the aldehyde intermediate, initiating the degradation of the alkyl side-chain of cholesterol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The products are exclusively in the (25S) conformation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also accepts cholesterol as a substrate. cf. EC 1.14.15.28.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19843222"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19846551"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19846552"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20545858"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.15.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
