<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.16.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phenylalanine 3-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phenylalanine 3-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.16.7#SIP4D490558082ABB3F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces coeruleorubidus, forms 3-hydroxy-L-phenylalanine (i.e. m-L-tyrosine), which is one of the building blocks in the biosynthesis of the uridyl peptide antibiotics pacidamycins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The 4a-hydroxytetrahydropteridine formed can dehydrate to 6,7-dihydropteridine, both spontaneously and by the action of EC 4.2.1.96.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The 6,7-dihydropteridine must be enzymically reduced back to tetrahydropteridine, by EC 1.5.1.34, before it slowly rearranges into the more stable but inactive compound 7,8-dihydropteridine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21615132"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.16.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.16.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.16.7#SIP4D490558082ABB3F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(6R)-L-erythro-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrobiopterin + L-phenylalanine + O2 = (4aS,6R)-4a-hydroxy-L-erythro-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrobiopterin + 3-hydroxy-L-phenylalanine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
