<skos:prefLabel>peptidylglycine monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PAM</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptidyl alpha-amidating enzyme</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptidylglycine 2-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptidylglycine alpha-amidating monooxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.17.3#SIP51D388BC8417D021"/>
<rdfs:comment>A copper protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme binds two copper ions with distinct roles during catalysis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Peptidylglycines with a neutral amino acid residue in the penultimate position are the best substrates for the enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product is unstable and dismutates to glyoxylate and the corresponding desglycine peptide amide, a reaction catalyzed by EC 4.3.2.5.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In mammals, the two activities are part of a bifunctional protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the final step of biosynthesis of alpha-melanotropin and related biologically active peptides.</rdfs:comment>
