<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.18.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dihydroceramide fatty acyl 2-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>plant sphingolipid fatty acid 2-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.18.7#SIP1B1E0AFE25A04BC7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from plants, catalyzes the hydroxylation of carbon 2 of long- or very-long-chain fatty acids attached to sphinganine during de novo ceramide synthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme requires an external cytochrome b5 as the electron donor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The newly introduced 2-hydroxyl group has R-configuration. cf. EC 1.14.18.6.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19054355"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22635113"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22918503"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.18.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.18.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.18.7#SIP1B1E0AFE25A04BC7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an N-(1,2-saturated acyl)sphinganine + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H(+) + O2 = an N-[(2'R)-hydroxyacyl]sphinganine + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
