<skos:prefLabel>acyl-CoA (9+3)-desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Delta(12)(omega(6))-desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Delta(12) desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Delta(12) fatty acid desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Delta(12)-fatty-acid desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oleoyl-CoA 12-desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oleoyl-CoA Delta(12) desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.6#SIPBC77F98D3FE726ED"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.6#SIP11A1208292933B1F"/>
<rdfs:comment>This microsomal enzyme introduces a cis double bond at position 12 of fatty-acyl-CoAs that contain a cis double bond at position 9.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>When acting on 19:1Delta(10) fatty acyl-CoA the enzyme from the pathogenic protozoan Trypanosoma brucei introduces the new double bond at position 13, indicating that the new double bond is introduced three carbons from the existing cis double bond, toward the methyl-end of the fatty acid.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2248971"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8900454"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9829122"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15009186"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.6#SIPBC77F98D3FE726ED">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(9Z)-octadecenoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H(+) + O2 = (9Z,12Z)-octadecadienoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
