<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.10">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>icosanoyl-CoA 5-desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acyl-CoA Delta(5)-desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.10#SIP5AC15849DE687CD5"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Limnanthes douglasii (meadowfoam), is involved in the biosynthesis of (5Z)-icos-5-enoate, an unusual monounsaturated fatty acid that makes up to 60% of the total fatty acids in Limnanthes sp. seed oil.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme only acts on saturated fatty acids.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10982439"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.10#SIP5AC15849DE687CD5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>eicosanoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H(+) + O2 = (5Z)-eicosenoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10982439">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/10982439"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10982439"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.11">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] 4-desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Delta(4)-palmitoyl-[acyl carrier protein] desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.11#SIPDB40A66148B4081E"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from the plants Coriandrum sativum (coriander) and Hedera helix are involved in biosynthesis of petroselinate [(6Z)-octadec-6-enoate], which is formed by elongation of (4Z)-hexadec-4-enoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The ivy enzyme can also act on oleoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] and palmitoleoyl-[acyl-carrier protein], generating the corresponding 4,9-diene.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1454797"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12232129"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15939740"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.11#SIPDB40A66148B4081E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + hexadecanoyl-[ACP] + O2 + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = (4Z)-hexadecenoyl-[ACP] + 2 H2O + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1454797">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/1454797"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1454797"/>
</rdf:Description>
