</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.17">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sphingolipid 4-desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dehydroceramide desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.17#SIP9D864E0E946B75F1"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which has been characterized from plants, fungi, and mammals, generates a trans double bond at position 4 of sphinganine bases in sphingolipids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The preferred substrate is dihydroceramide, but the enzyme is also active with dihydroglucosylceramide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 1.14.19.29, this enzyme does not contain an integral cytochrome b5 domain and requires an external cytochrome b5.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product serves as an important signaling molecules in mammals and is required for spermatide differentiation.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5140816"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9312549"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11104018"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11937514"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18978071"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.17#SIP9D864E0E946B75F1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an N-acylsphinganine + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H(+) + O2 = an N-acylsphing-4-enine + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5140816">
