<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.18">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sphingolipid 8-(E)-desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>8 fatty acid desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>8-sphingolipid desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.18#SIP276E02EA8EFA5D82"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the yeasts Kluyveromyces lactis and Candida albicans and from the diatom Thalassiosira pseudonana, introduces a trans double bond at the 8-position of sphingoid bases in sphingolipids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme determines the position of the double bond by its distance from the alcohol end of the sphingoid base, and contains a cytochrome b5 domain that acts as the direct electron donor to the active site of the desaturase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The homologous enzymes from higher plants, EC 1.14.19.29, act on phytosphinganine (4-hydroxysphinganine) and produces a mixture of trans and cis isomers.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12402089"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15978045"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19047747"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.18#SIP276E02EA8EFA5D82">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an N-acylsphing-4-enine + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H(+) + O2 = a (4E,8E)-4-sphinga-4,8-dienine ceramide + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12402089">
