<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.21">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cholesterol 7-desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.21#SIP8AF83BB75ED59A9A"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.21#SIP4A82774544838002"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from several organisms including the worm Caenorhabditis elegans, the fly Drosophila melanogaster, and the ciliate Tetrahymena thermophila, is a Rieske oxygenase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In insects it participates in the the biosythesis of ecdysteroid hormones.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The electrons are transferred from NAD(P)H via an electron transfer chain likely to include ferredoxin reductase and ferredoxin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme differs from regular desaturases, such as EC 1.14.19.20, which are cytochrome b5-dependent and contain the three His-boxes that are typical to most desaturases.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21632547"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21749634"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23603937"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24244885"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.21#SIP8AF83BB75ED59A9A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>cholesterol + H(+) + NADPH + O2 = 7-dehydrocholesterol + 2 H2O + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.21#SIP4A82774544838002">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>cholesterol + H(+) + NADH + O2 = 7-dehydrocholesterol + 2 H2O + NAD(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
