<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.22">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.3.1.35"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acyl-lipid omega-6 desaturase (cytochrome b5)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>linoleate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oleate desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oleoyl-CoA desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphatidylcholine desaturase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.22#SIPD9014C1B98C96361"/>
<rdfs:comment>This microsomal enzyme introduces a cis double bond in fatty acids attached to lipid molecules at a location 6 carbons away from the methyl end of the fatty acid.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The distance from the carboxylic acid end of the molecule does not affect the location of the new double bond.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The most common substrates are oleoyl groups attached to either sn-1 or sn-2 position of the glycerol backbone in phosphatidylcholine. cf. EC 1.14.19.23.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/166662"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/475773"/>
