</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.40">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>hex-5-enoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] acetylenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.40#SIPC8F3099E9BA8590E"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.40#SIP8518C3E8627E9169"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the marine cyanobacterium Moorea producens, is involved in production of the ion channel blocker jamaicamide A.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is specific for hexanoate or hex-5-enoate loaded onto a dedicated acyl-carrier protein (JamC), which is encoded by a gene in the same operon.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25531891"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.40#SIPC8F3099E9BA8590E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>5-hexenoyl-[ACP] + 2 H(+) + O2 + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = 5-hexynoyl-[ACP] + 2 H2O + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.40#SIP8518C3E8627E9169">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + hexanoyl-[ACP] + O2 + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = 5-hexenoyl-[ACP] + 2 H2O + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25531891">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/25531891"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25531891"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.41">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sterol 22-desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.41#SIP052961A433F4DC01"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.41#SIP538C8F7A80A7FF41"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in yeast and plants, catalyzes the introduction of a double bond between the C-22 and C-23 carbons of certain sterols.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In yeast the enzyme acts on ergosta-5,7,24(28)-trien-3beta-ol, a step in the biosynthesis of ergosterol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana acts on sitosterol and 24-epi-campesterol, producing stigmasterol and brassicasterol, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8543054"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8635732"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16531502"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.41#SIP052961A433F4DC01">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>5-dehydroepisterol + H(+) + NADPH + O2 = ergosta-5,7,22,24(28)-tetraen-3beta-ol + 2 H2O + NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.41#SIP538C8F7A80A7FF41">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + NADPH + O2 + sitosterol = 2 H2O + NADP(+) + stigmasterol.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
