<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.60">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>7-chloro-L-tryptophan 6-halogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.60#SIPB386D4219E6840D0"/>
<rdfs:comment>An FAD-dependent halogenase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Kutzneria sp. 744, works in tandem with EC 1.14.19.9 to generate 6,7-dichloro-L-tryptophan, which is incorporated as a pyrroloindoline in the kutznerides family of natural products.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has a 120-fold preference for 7-chloro-L-tryptophan over L-tryptophan as substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18828589"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.60#SIPB386D4219E6840D0">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>7-chloro-L-tryptophan + chloride + FADH2 + O2 = 6,7-dichloro-L-tryptophan + FAD + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18828589">
