<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.19.75">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>very-long-chain acyl-lipid omega-9 desaturase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.75#SIP8A1493D783CB7CF4"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.19.75#SIP2C4A3643DEB2C81F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana, acts on both 24:0 and 26:0 fatty acids, introducing a cis double bond at a position 9 carbons from the methyl end.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These very-long-chain fatty acids are found as a minor component of seed lipids, but also in the membrane phosphatidylethanolamine and phosphatidylserine, in sphingolipids, as precursors and components of cuticular and epicuticular waxes, and in suberin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9559566"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23175755"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.19.-"/>
