<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.20.8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.11.50"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(-)-deoxypodophyllotoxin synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.20.8#SIP70ED4B0C9EDF652D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Sinopodophyllum hexandrum, is involved in the biosynthetic pathway of podophyllotoxin, a non-alkaloid toxin lignan whose derivatives are important anticancer drugs.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes the closure of the central six-membered ring in the aryltetralin scaffold.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26359402"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.20.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.20.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.20.8#SIP70ED4B0C9EDF652D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(-)-yatein + 2-oxoglutarate + O2 = (-)-deoxypodophyllotoxin + CO2 + H2O + succinate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
