</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.20.11">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-[(Z)-2-isocyanoethenyl]-1H-indole synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.20.11#SIP3387E15759186849"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the cyanobacterium Fischerella ambigua UTEX 1903, participates in the biosynthesis of hapalindole-type alkaloids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes an Fe(2+), 2-oxoglutarate-dependent monooxygenation at C-3, which is followed by decarboxylation and dehydration, resulting in the generation of a cis C-C double bond. cf. EC 1.14.20.12.</rdfs:comment>
