<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.99.38">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cholesterol 25-monooxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cholesterol 25-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.99.38#SIPFCE8E3CBC184A981"/>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike most other sterol hydroxylases, this enzyme is not a cytochrome P450.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Instead, it uses diiron cofactors to catalyze the hydroxylation of hydrophobic substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The diiron cofactor can be either Fe-O-Fe or Fe-OH-Fe and is bound to the enzyme through interactions with clustered histidine or glutamate residues.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In cell cultures, this enzyme down-regulates cholesterol synthesis and the processing of sterol regulatory element binding proteins (SREBPs). cf. EC 1.17.99.10.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7947683"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9852097"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11967195"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12390873"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12543708"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
