<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.99.63">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>beta-carotene 4-ketolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-C-4 oxygenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-carotene ketolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.99.63#SIP1BB807F16C16C278"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.99.63#SIPF33BE0984CDBF4E8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, studied from algae, plants, fungi, and bacteria, adds an oxo group at position 4 of a carotenoid beta ring.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is involved in the biosynthesis of carotenoids such as astaxanthin and flexixanthin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes does not act on beta rings that are hydroxylated at position 3, such as in zeaxanthin (cf. EC 1.14.99.64).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the yeast Xanthophyllomyces dendrorhous is bifuntional and also catalyzes the activity of EC 1.14.15.24.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7750556"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8764486"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15269553"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16416328"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16625353"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25612872"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
