</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.99.67">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>alpha-N-dichloroacetyl-p-aminophenylserinol N-oxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.99.67#SIP1C6D35AAF1A5547B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces venezuelae, is involved in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic chloramphenicol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It contains a carboxylate-bridged binuclear non-heme iron cluster.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The components of the native electron chain have not been identified, although the immediate donor is likely to be an iron-sulfur protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction mechanism involves formation of an extremely stable peroxo intermediate that catalyzes three individual two-electron oxidations via a hydroxylamine and a nitroso intermediates without releasing the intermediates. cf. EC 1.14.99.68.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24347692"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25564306"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28823151"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.99.67#SIP1C6D35AAF1A5547B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>AH2 + alpha-N-dichloroacetyl-p-aminophenylserinol + 2 O2 = A + chloramphenicol + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
