<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.99.68">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>4-aminobenzoate N-oxygenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.99.68#SIP495263B2EF4822E4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces thioluteus, catalyzes an early step in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic aureothin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It contains a carboxylate-bridged binuclear non-heme iron cluster.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The native electron donor has not been identified, but is likely an iron-sulfur protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction mechanism involves formation of an extremely stable peroxo intermediate that catalyzes three two-electron oxidations via a hydroxylamine and dihydroxylamine intermediates. cf. EC 1.14.99.67.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15038705"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16342311"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17765264"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18458342"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19731912"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20798054"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.14.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.99.68#SIP495263B2EF4822E4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4-aminobenzoate + AH2 + 2 O2 = 4-nitrobenzoate + A + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
