<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.14.99.69">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tRNA 2-(methylsulfanyl)-N(6)-isopentenyladenosine(37) hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tRNA 2-(methylsulfanyl)-N(6)-dimethylallyladenosine(37) hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tRNA 2-methylthio-N(6)-isopentenyl adenosine(37) hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.14.99.69#SIPDCABA141932389FE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found only within a small subset of facultative anaerobic bacteria, belongs to the nonheme diiron family.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Salmonella typhimurium was shown to catalyze a stereoselective (E) hydroxylation at the terminal C(4)-position of the prenyl group.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8253666"/>
