<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.16.3.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bacterial non-heme ferritin</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.16.3.2#SIPB1F9B4267AC7A2B3"/>
<rdfs:comment>Ferritins are intracellular iron-storage and detoxification proteins found in all kingdoms of life.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They are formed from two subunits that coassemble in various ratios to form a spherical protein shell.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Thousands of mineralized iron atoms are stored within the core of the structure.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product of dioxygen reduction by the bacterial non-heme ferritin is hydrogen peroxide, which is consumed in a subsequent reaction.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8281950"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11254384"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24380371"/>
