<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.16.3.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>manganese oxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.16.3.3#SIP3F0162A62F96DEAB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which belongs to the multicopper oxidase family, is found in many bacterial strains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It oxidizes soluble Mn(II) to insoluble manganese oxides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Since the enzyme is localized to the outer surface of the cell, its activity usually results in encrustation of the cells by the oxides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The physiological function of bacterial Mn(II) oxidation remains unclear.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12420165"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17359266"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23124227"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23577125"/>
