<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.1.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>leucoanthocyanidin reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>leucocyanidin reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.1.3#SIPC9C2C09CBD9F7A43"/>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the synthesis of catechin, catechin-4beta-ol (leucocyanidin) and the related flavan-3-ols afzelechin and gallocatechin, which are initiating monomers in the synthesis of plant polymeric proanthocyanidins or condensed tannins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While 2,3-trans-3,4-cis-leucocyanidin is the preferred flavan-3,4-diol substrate, 2,3-trans-3,4-cis-leucodelphinidin and 2,3-trans-3, 4-cis-leucopelargonidin can also act as substrates, but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NADH can replace NADPH but is oxidized more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8470799"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12788945"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.17.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.17.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.1.3#SIPC9C2C09CBD9F7A43">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2R,3S)-catechin + H2O + NADP(+) = (2R,3S,4S)-leucocyanidin + H(+) + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8470799">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8470799"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8470799"/>
</rdf:Description>
