<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.1.5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.5.1.13"/>
<skos:prefLabel>nicotinate dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>nicotinate hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>nicotinic acid hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.1.5#SIP0FECE815BF83CCA4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is capable of acting on a variety of nicotinate analogs to varying degrees, including pyrazine-2-carboxylate, pyrazine 2,3-dicarboxylate, trigonelline and 6-methylnicotinate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Clostridium barkeri also possesses a catalytically essential, labile selenium that can be removed by reaction with cyanide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Forms part of the nicotinate-fermentation catabolism pathway in Eubacterium barkeri.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Other enzymes involved in this pathway are EC 1.3.7.1, EC 3.5.2.18, EC 1.1.1.291, EC 5.4.99.4, EC 5.3.3.6, EC 4.2.1.85 and EC 4.1.3.32.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4388026"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6838209"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8278371"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8555176"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.17.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.17.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.1.5#SIP0FECE815BF83CCA4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + NADP(+) + nicotinate = 6-hydroxynicotinate + H(+) + NADPH.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
