<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.3.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>6-hydroxynicotinate dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>6-hydroxynicotinate hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>6-hydroxynicotinic acid dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>6-hydroxynicotinic acid hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.3.3#SIP0FEC19F554B6522E"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also has a catalytically essential, labile selenium that can be removed by reaction with cyanide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Bacillus niacini, this enzyme is required for growth on nicotinic acid.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.17.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.17.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.3.3#SIP0FEC19F554B6522E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>6-hydroxynicotinate + H2O + O2 = 2,6-dihydroxynicotinate + H2O2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.3.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.14.99.27"/>
<skos:prefLabel>juglone 3-hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>naphthoquinone hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.3.4#SIP257D87E25695A1F0"/>
<rdfs:comment>Even though oxygen is consumed, molecular oxygen is not incorporated into the product.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Catalysis starts by incorporation of an oxygen atom from a water molecule into the substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The naphthalene-1,2,4,8-tetrol intermediate is then oxidized by molecular oxygen, which is reduced to water.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts on 1,4-naphthoquinone, naphthazarin and 2-chloro-1,4-naphthoquinone.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4041238"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.17.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.17.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.3.4#SIP257D87E25695A1F0">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 juglone + O2 = 2 3,5-dihydroxy-1,4-naphthoquinone + 2 H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4041238">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/4041238"/>
