<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.4.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.1.4.1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>vitamin-K-epoxide reductase (warfarin-sensitive)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phylloquinone epoxide reductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>vitamin K1 epoxide reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.4.4#SIPB21F74981B24CDAD"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.4.4#SIPB83444E91401628E"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the reduction of vitamin K 2,3-epoxide, which is formed by the activity of EC 4.1.1.90, back to its phylloquinol active form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme forms a tight complex with EC 5.3.4.1, which transfers the required electrons from newly-synthesized proteins by catalyzing the formation of disulfide bridges.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme acts on the epoxide forms of both phylloquinone (vitamin K1) and menaquinone (vitamin K2).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Inhibited strongly by (S)-warfarin and ferulenol.</rdfs:comment>
