<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.9.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(+)-pinoresinol hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pinoresinol alpha-hydroxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.9.2#SIP7FD987AD951DE7FD"/>
<rdfs:comment>Contains FAD.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp SG-MS2, catalyzes the incorporation of an oxygen atom originating from a water molecule into position C-6 of the lignan (+)-pinoresinol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme consists of a flavoprotein subunit and a c-type cytochrome subunit.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Electrons that originate in the substrate are transferred via the FAD cofactor and the cytochrome subunit to the blue-copper protein azurin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/32198167"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.17.9.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.17.9.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.9.2#SIP7FD987AD951DE7FD">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(+)-pinoresinol + H2O + 2 oxidized [azurin] = (+)-6-hydroxypinoresinol + 2 H(+) + 2 reduced [azurin].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
