<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.99.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>epoxyqueuosine reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oQ reductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.99.6#SIP57271F56E108501C"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the last step in the bacterial biosynthetic pathway to queuosine, the modified guanosine base in the wobble position in tRNAs specific for Tyr, His, Asp or Asn.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Two types of enzymes are known to catalyze this activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>QueG enzymes are cobalamin-dependent, while QueH enzymes contain a [4Fe-4S] metallocluster along with an adjacent coordinated iron metal.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21502530"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28128549"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/34652139"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.17.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.17.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.99.6#SIP57271F56E108501C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>AH2 + epoxyqueuosine(34) in tRNA = A + H2O + queuosine(34) in tRNA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
