<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.17.99.10">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>steroid C-25 hydroxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cholesterol C-25 dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>steroid C-25 dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.99.10#SIP45C4A29A076D0125"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.99.10#SIP3471429D42012631"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.99.10#SIP1E1CA669CB9A3DA7"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.99.10#SIP0E8766882BF5CDBA"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.99.10#SIPD63EED13F055ACAB"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.17.99.10#SIPBDB6DAD98C9B4E19"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Sterolibacterium denitrificans, participates in the anaerobic degradation of cholesterol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can accept several substrates including vitamin D3.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme contains a bis(guanylyl molybdopterin) cofactor, five [Fe-S] clusters, and one heme b. cf. EC 1.14.99.38.</rdfs:comment>
