<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.19.1.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>flavodoxin--NADP(+) reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>FPR</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.19.1.1#SIP273722F013962B3A"/>
<rdfs:comment>This activity occurs in some prokaryotes and algae that possess flavodoxin, and provides low-potential electrons for a variety of reactions such as nitrogen fixation, sulfur assimilation and amino acid biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In photosynthetic organisms it is involved in the photosynthetic electron transport chain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also catalyzes EC 1.18.1.2.</rdfs:comment>
