<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.20.4.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>mycoredoxin</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.20.4.3#SIP90AB2285911CAC17"/>
<rdfs:comment>Reduction of arsenate is part of a defense mechanism of the cell against toxic arsenate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrate arseno-mycothiol is formed by EC 2.8.4.2.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A second mycothiol recycles mycoredoxin and forms mycothione.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19286650"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.20.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.20.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.20.4.3#SIP90AB2285911CAC17">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>[mycoredoxin]-L-cysteine + arseno-mycothiol + H(+) = [mycoredoxin]-S-mycothiol-L-cysteine + arsenite.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19286650">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19286650"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19286650"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.20.4.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>arsenate reductase (thioredoxin)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.20.4.4#SIP29B09F9B2F4CA06F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized in bacteria of the Firmicutes phylum, is specific for thioredoxin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has no activity with glutaredoxin (cf. EC 1.20.4.1).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Although the arsenite formed is more toxic than arsenate, it can be extruded from some bacteria by EC 7.3.2.7; in other organisms, arsenite can be methylated by EC 2.1.1.137 in a pathway that produces non-toxic organoarsenical compounds.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also has the activity of EC 3.1.3.48.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8003493"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10606519"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11573087"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12072565"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.20.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.20.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.20.4.4#SIP29B09F9B2F4CA06F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>[thioredoxin]-dithiol + arsenate + H(+) = [thioredoxin]-disulfide + arsenite + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
