<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.21.3.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>aureusidin synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.21.3.6#SIP875D3128EF0A9DE5"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.21.3.6#SIP954123D5DA1BDA9E"/>
<activity rdf:resource="1.21.3.6#SIP03D95729532721E9"/>
<rdfs:comment>Plays a key role in the yellow coloration of flowers such as Antirrhinum majus (snapdragon).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is a homolog of plant polyphenol oxidase and catalyzes two separate chemical transformations, i.e. 3-hydroxylation and oxidative cyclization (2',-dehydrogenation).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>H2O2 activates reaction (1) but inhibits reaction (2).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Originally considered to act on the phenol but now thought to mainly act on the 4'-O-beta-glucoside in vivo.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11073455"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11164594"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11418122"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16832053"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="1.21.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="1.21.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.21.3.6#SIP875D3128EF0A9DE5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2',4,4',6'-tetrahydroxychalcone 4'-O-beta-D-glucoside + H(+) + O2 = aureusidin 6-O-beta-glucoside + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.21.3.6#SIP954123D5DA1BDA9E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 2',3,4,4',6'-pentahydroxychalcone 4'-O-beta-D-glucoside + 2 H(+) + O2 = 2 aureusidin 6-O-beta-glucoside + 2 H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.21.3.6#SIP03D95729532721E9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2',3,4,4',6'-pentahydroxychalcone 4'-O-beta-D-glucoside + H(+) + O2 = bracteatin 6-O-beta-glucoside + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
