<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.21.98.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>PqqA peptide cyclase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.21.98.4#SIP0F0728711BCA79E8"/>
<rdfs:comment>This bacterial enzyme, which is a member of the radical SAM protein family, catalyzes the formation of a C-C bond between C-4 of glutamate and C-3 of tyrosine residues of the PqqA protein (which are separated by three amino acid residues).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This is the first enzymic step in the biosynthesis of the bacterial enzyme cofactor pyrroloquinoline quinone (PQQ).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction is dependent on the presence of flavodoxin and the accessory protein PqqD.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20737074"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25817994"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26961875"/>
