<skos:prefLabel>thyroxine 5'-deiodinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>diiodothyronine 5'-deiodinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>iodothyronine 5'-deiodinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>iodothyronine outer ring monodeiodinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-thyroxine iodohydrolase (reducing)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>thyroxine 5-deiodinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>type II iodothyronine deiodinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>type I iodothyronine deiodinase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.21.99.4#SIP9F49E11B45497B69"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme activity has only been demonstrated in the direction of 5'-deiodination, which renders the thyroid hormone more active.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme consists of type I and type II enzymes, both containing selenocysteine, but with different kinetics.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>For the type I enzyme the first reaction is a reductive deiodination converting the -Se-H group of the enzyme into an -Se-I group; the reductant then reconverts this into -Se-H, releasing iodide.</rdfs:comment>
