<rdf:Description rdf:about="1.23.5.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.10.99.3"/>
<skos:prefLabel>violaxanthin de-epoxidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>VDE</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="1.23.5.1#SIPACEF74D2D70A973C"/>
<rdfs:comment>Along with EC 1.14.15.21, this enzyme forms part of the xanthophyll (or violaxanthin) cycle for controlling the concentration of zeaxanthin in chloroplasts.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is activated by a low pH of the thylakoid lumen (produced by high light intensity).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Zeaxanthin induces the dissipation of excitation energy in the chlorophyll of the light-harvesting protein complex of photosystem II.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In higher plants the enzyme reacts with all-trans-diepoxides, such as violaxanthin, and all-trans-monoepoxides, but in the alga Mantoniella squamata, only the diepoxides are good substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/102251"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8742341"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9624110"/>
