<skos:prefLabel>methyltransferase cap1</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cap1-MTase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>messenger RNA (nucleoside-2'-)-methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mRNA (nucleoside-2'-O)-methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.57#SIPD3599F3622591418"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the methylation of the ribose on the first transcribed nucleotide of mRNA or snRNA molecules.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This methylation event is known as cap1, and occurs in all mRNAs and snRNAs of higher eukaryotes, including insects, vertebrates and their viruses.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human enzyme can also methylate mRNA molecules that lack methylation on the capping 5'-triphosphoguanosine.</rdfs:comment>
