<skos:prefLabel>macrocin O-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MOMT</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.101#SIP054BC751088FF902"/>
<rdfs:comment>The 3-hydroxyl group of a 2-O-methyl-6-deoxy-D-allose residue in the macrolide antibiotic macrocin acts as methyl acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from Streptomyces fradiae.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Tylosin is a macrolide antibiotic.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Not identical with EC 2.1.1.102.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3170601"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3170602"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
