<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.114">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>polyprenyldihydroxybenzoate methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3,4-dihydroxy-5-hexaprenylbenzoate methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DHHB methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DHHB-Mt</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DHHB O-methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dihydroxyhexaprenylbenzoate methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.114#SIPC99F32E87B758CBB"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.114#SIP5A0BEE7CE4BEC209"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.114#SIPC8755018E5D3D5B5"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.114#SIPBA5B1EEF444EAAAB"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.114#SIP645F1929795D6649"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.114#SIPEE8EEF57E55F9C81"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is involved in ubiquinone biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Ubiquinones from different organisms have a different number of prenyl units (for example, ubiquinone-6 in Saccharomyces, ubiquinone-9 in rat and ubiquinone-10 in human), and thus the natural substrate for the enzymes from different organisms has a different number of prenyl units.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However, the enzyme usually shows a low degree of specificity regarding the number of prenyl units.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>For example, the human COQ3 enzyme can restore biosynthesis of ubiquinone-6 in coq3 deletion mutants of yeast.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from yeast and rat also catalyze the methylation of 3-demethylubiquinol-6 and 3-demethylubiquinol-9, respectively (this activity is classified as EC 2.1.1.64).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1885593"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10419476"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10777520"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21636923"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.114#SIPC99F32E87B758CBB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3,4-dihydroxy-5-all-trans-polyprenylbenzoate + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3-methoxy,4-hydroxy-5-all-trans-polyprenylbenzoate + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
