<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.127">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[ribulose-bisphosphate carboxylase]-lysine N-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ribulose-bisphosphate-carboxylase/oxygenase N-methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RuBisCO LSMT</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RuBisCO methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.127#SIP6D3F42702443BF11"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes three successive methylations of Lys-14 in the large subunits of hexadecameric higher plant ribulose-bisphosphate-carboxylase (EC 4.1.1.39).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Only the three methylated form is observed.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from pea (Pisum sativum) also three-methylates a specific lysine in the chloroplastic isoforms of fructose-bisphosphate aldolase (EC 4.1.2.13).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8527940"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17338551"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17635932"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22547063"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.127#SIP6D3F42702443BF11">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-lysyl-[ribulose-1,5-bisphosphate carboxylase] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3 H(+) + N(6),N(6),N(6)-trimethyl-L-lysyl-[ribulose-1,5-bisphosphate carboxylase] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
