<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.152">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>precorrin-6A synthase (deacetylating)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>precorrin-6X synthase (deacetylating)</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.152#SIP7EDBC634E6DFC0F2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which participates in the aerobic (late cobalt insertion) cobalamin biosythesis pathway, catalyzes two reactions - the methylation of carbon C(1) of precorrin-5, and its deacetylation, forming precorrin-6A.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>See EC 2.1.1.195 for the C(1)-methyltransferase that participates in the anaerobic cobalamin biosynthesis pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8226690"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12195810"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.152#SIP7EDBC634E6DFC0F2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + precorrin-5 + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = acetate + 2 H(+) + precorrin-6A + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
