<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.164">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>demethylrebeccamycin-D-glucose O-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.164#SIP3CD71D88C3E5D1A4"/>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the last step in the biosynthesis of rebeccamycin, an indolocarbazole alkaloid produced by the bacterium Lechevalieria aerocolonigenes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is able to use a wide variety substrates, tolerating variation on the imide heterocycle, deoxygenation of the sugar moiety, and even indolocarbazole glycoside anomers.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16575939"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18502766"/>
