<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.167">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>27S pre-rRNA (guanosine(2922)-2'-O)-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.167#SIP17945FBE1BAA6F33"/>
<rdfs:comment>Spb1p is a site-specific 2'-O-ribose RNA methyltransferase that catalyzes the formation of 2'-O-methylguanosine(2922), a universally conserved position of the catalytic center of the ribosome that is essential for translation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>2'-O-methylguanosine(2922) is formed at a later stage of the processing, during the maturation of of the 27S pre-rRNA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In absence of snR52, Spb1p can also catalyze the formation of uridine(2921).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14636587"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15546625"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.167#SIP17945FBE1BAA6F33">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>guanosine(2922) in 27S pre-rRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2'-O-methylguanosine(2922) in 27S pre-rRNA + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
