<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.197">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>malonyl-[acyl-carrier protein] O-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.197#SIP55C4116799385930"/>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in an early step of biotin biosynthesis in Gram-negative bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group to the omega-carboxyl group of malonyl-[acyl-carrier protein] forming a methyl ester.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The methyl ester is recognized by the fatty acid synthetic enzymes, which process it via the fatty acid elongation cycle to give pimelyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] methyl ester.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While the enzyme can also accept malonyl-CoA, it has a much higher activity with malonyl-[acyl-carrier protein].</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3058702"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4563978"/>
