<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.222">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-polyprenyl-6-hydroxyphenol methylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-octaprenyl-6-hydroxyphenol methylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.222#SIP814EABA339793A95"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.222#SIP48D532EF0CBC9BC3"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.222#SIP18C12BCA9435D6B8"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.222#SIP6ECB3BFF5B02CDFA"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.222#SIPCA583A99308560F7"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.222#SIP7FFB9FA99B5A998D"/>
<rdfs:comment>UbiG catalyzes both methylation steps in ubiquinone biosynthesis in Escherichia coli.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The second methylation is classified as EC 2.1.1.64.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In eukaryotes Coq3 catalyzes the two methylation steps in ubiquinone biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However, while the second methylation is common to both enzymes, the first methylation by Coq3 occurs at a different position within the pathway, and thus involves a different substrate and is classified as EC 2.1.1.114.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrate of the eukaryotic enzyme (3,4-dihydroxy-5-all-trans-polyprenylbenzoate) differs by an additional carboxylate moiety.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8703953"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10419476"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.222#SIP814EABA339793A95">
