<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.226#SIPE30331B688F61A14"/>
<rdfs:comment>The bifunctional enzyme from Mycobacterium tuberculosis 2'-O-methylates cytidine(1920) in helix 69 of 23S rRNA and cytidine(1409) in helix 44 of 16S rRNA (cf. EC 2.1.1.227).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These methylations result in increased susceptibility to the antibiotics capreomycin and viomycin.</rdfs:comment>
