<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.247">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[methyl-Co(III) methylamine-specific corrinoid protein]:coenzyme M methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MT2-A</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.247#SIPF9829BDC73D25D8C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.247#SIPCF3B22A22B13AF6C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.247#SIPB8871E5A3D288FF0"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which is involved in methanogenesis from mono-, di-, and trimethylamine, catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group bound to the cobalt cofactor of several corrinoid proteins (mono-, di-, and trimethylamine-specific corrinoid proteins, cf. EC 2.1.1.248, EC 2.1.1.249 and EC 2.1.1.250) to coenzyme M, forming the substrate for EC 2.8.4.1, the enzyme that catalyzes the final step in methanogenesis.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7635826"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8702528"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9006042"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9642198"/>
