<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/9371433"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9371433"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11073950">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/11073950"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11073950"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.252">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tetramethylammonium--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tetramethylammonium methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.252#SIP2D3F2C947E3FEB01"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from tetramethylammonium to a tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein (MtqC), is involved in methanogenesis from tetramethylammonium.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Methylation of the corrinoid protein requires the central cobalt to be in the Co(I) state.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>During methylation the cobalt is oxidized to the Co(III) state.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The methylated corrinoid protein is substrate for EC 2.1.1.253.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9732435"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.252#SIP2D3F2C947E3FEB01">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Co(I)-[tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein] + H(+) + tetramethylammonium = methyl-Co(III)-[tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein] + trimethylamine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9732435">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/9732435"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9732435"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.253">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[methyl-Co(III) tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein]:coenzyme M methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.253#SIPDB80F27296112703"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which is involved in methanogenesis from tetramethylammonium, catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from a corrinoid protein (see EC 2.1.1.252), where it is bound to the cobalt cofactor, to coenzyme M, forming the substrate for EC 2.8.4.1, the enzyme that catalyzes the final step in methanogenesis.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9732435"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.253#SIPDB80F27296112703">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>coenzyme M + methyl-Co(III)-[tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein] = Co(I)-[tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein] + H(+) + methyl-coenzyme M.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9732435">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/9732435"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9732435"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.254">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>erythromycin 3''-O-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.254#SIP4A4C26844E2E3366"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.254#SIPB8D218CF342A7C89"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme methylates the 3 position of the mycarosyl moiety of erythromycin C, forming the most active form of the antibiotic, erythromycin A.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also methylate the precursor erythromycin D, forming erythromycin B, which is then converted to erythromycin A by EC 1.14.13.154.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2185226"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9353926"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.254#SIP4A4C26844E2E3366">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>erythromycin C + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = erythromycin A + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.254#SIPB8D218CF342A7C89">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>erythromycin D + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = erythromycin B + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2185226">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/2185226"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2185226"/>
</rdf:Description>
