<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.272">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cobalt-factor III methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.272#SIP27C37D233A7F7956"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from the bacterium Bacillus megaterium.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which participates in the anaerobic (early cobalt insertion) pathway of adenosylcobalamin biosynthesis, catalyzes a crucial reaction where the tetrapyrrole ring contracts as a result of methylation of C-17.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Contains a [4Fe-4S] cluster.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also convert cobalt-precorrin-3 to cobalt-precorrin-4.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reductant may be thioredoxin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>See EC 2.1.1.131 for the corresponding enzyme that participates in the aerobic cobalamin biosynthesis pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23155054"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.272#SIP27C37D233A7F7956">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>AH2 + Co(II)-factor III + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = A + Co-precorrin-4 + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23155054">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/23155054"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23155054"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.273">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>benzoate O-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.273#SIP90AFBF2203293A6B"/>
<rdfs:comment>While the enzyme from the plant Zea mays is specific for benzoate, the enzymes from Arabidopsis species and Clarkia breweri also catalyze the reaction of EC 2.1.1.274.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In snapdragon (Antirrhinum majus) two isoforms are found, one specific for benzoate and one that is also active toward salicylate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The volatile product is an important scent compound in some flowering species.</rdfs:comment>
