</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.290">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tRNA(Phe) [7-(3-amino-3-carboxypropyl)wyosine(37)-O]-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tRNA-yW synthesizing enzyme-4</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.290#SIP2FF00D5FF1DD7892"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is found only in eukaryotes, where it is involved in the biosynthesis of wybutosine, a hypermodified tricyclic base found at position 37 of certain tRNAs.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The modification is important for translational reading-frame maintenance.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In some species that produce hydroxywybutosine the enzyme uses 7-(2-hydroxy-3-amino-3-carboxypropyl)wyosine(37) in tRNA(Phe) as substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also has the activity of EC 2.3.1.231.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16642040"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19287006"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20972222"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.290#SIP2FF00D5FF1DD7892">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>7-[(3S)-3-amino-3-carboxypropyl]wyosine(37) in tRNA(Phe) + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 7-[(3S)-(3-amino-3-methoxycarbonyl)propyl]wyosine(37) in tRNA(Phe) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
