<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.296">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>methyltransferase cap2</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cap2-MTase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mRNA (nucleoside-2'-O)-methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.296#SIP53E9F2CD7A88CB9A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in higher eukaryotes including insects and vertebrates, and their viruses, methylates the ribose of the nucleoside at the second transcribed position of mRNAs and snRNAs.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This methylation is known as cap2.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human enzyme can also methylate mRNA molecules where the upstream ribonucleotide is not methylated (see EC 2.1.1.57), but with lower efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16516986"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21310715"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.296#SIP53E9F2CD7A88CB9A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 5'-end (N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-(2'-O-methyl-ribonucleoside)-(ribonucleotide) in mRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a 5'-end (N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-(2'-O-methyl-ribonucleoside)-(2'-O-methyl-ribonucleotide) in mRNA + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
