<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.303">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2,7-dihydroxy-5-methyl-1-naphthoate 7-O-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>neocarzinostatin O-methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.303#SIPFFAE1482E2DA6C12"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Streptomyces carzinostaticus is involved in the biosynthesis of 2-hydroxy-7-methoxy-5-methyl-1-naphthoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This compound is part of the enediyne chromophore of the antitumor antibiotic neocarzinostatin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In vivo the enzyme catalyzes the regiospecific methylation at the 7-hydroxy group of its native substrate 2,7-dihydroxy-5-methyl-1-naphthoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In vitro it also recognizes other dihydroxynaphthoic acids and catalyzes their regiospecific O-methylation.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18387946"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19702337"/>
