<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.319">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.23"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.124"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.125"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.126"/>
<skos:prefLabel>type I protein arginine methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.319#SIP72A056168B233779"/>
<rdfs:comment>This eukaryotic enzyme catalyzes the sequential dimethylation of one of the terminal guanidino nitrogen atoms in arginine residues, resulting in formation of asymmetric dimethylarginine residues.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Some forms (e.g. PRMT1) have a very wide substrate specificity, while others (e.g. PRMT4 and PRMT6) are rather specific.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme has a preference for methylating arginine residues that are flanked by one or more glycine residues.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>PRMT1 is responsible for the bulk (about 85%) of total protein arginine methylation activity in mammalian cells. cf. EC 2.1.1.320, EC 2.1.1.321 and EC 2.1.1.322.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9642256"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9752719"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10713084"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11724789"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
