<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.321">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.23"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.124"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.125"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.126"/>
<skos:prefLabel>type III protein arginine methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.321#SIPB5D124FE87D1390C"/>
<rdfs:comment>Type III protein arginine methyltransferases catalyze the single methylation of one of the terminal nitrogen atoms of the guanidino group in an L-arginine residue within a protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike type I and type II protein arginine methyltransferases, which also catalyze this reaction, type III enzymes do not methylate the substrate any further. cf. EC 2.1.1.319, EC 2.1.1.320 and EC 2.1.1.322.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15044439"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17709427"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25294873"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
