<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.329">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.1.1.n12"/>
<skos:prefLabel>demethylphylloquinol methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-phytyl-1,4-naphthoquinol methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.329#SIP4F47A11CBE354F0B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in plants and cyanobacteria, catalyzes the final step in the biosynthesis of phylloquinone (vitamin K1), an electron carrier associated with photosystem I.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is specific for the quinol form of the substrate, and does not act on the quinone form.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11772039"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17082184"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26023160"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
