<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(-)-5'-demethylyatein + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (-)-yatein + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26359402">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26359402"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26359402"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.331">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bacteriochlorophyllide d C-12(1)-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.331#SIPAC6F210DDAB3A5D8"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, found in green sulfur bacteria (Chlorobiaceae) and green flimentous bacteria (Chloroflexaceae), is a radical S-adenosyl-L-methionine (AdoMet) enzyme and contains a [4Fe-4S] cluster.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It adds a methyl group at the C-12(1) position of bacteriochlorophylls of the c, d and e types.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This methylation plays a role in fine-tuning the structural arrangement of the bacteriochlorophyll aggregates in chlorosomes and therefore directly influences the chlorosomes absorption properties.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17586634"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.331#SIPAC6F210DDAB3A5D8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>8-ethyl-12-methyl-3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 8,12-diethyl-3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17586634">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17586634"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17586634"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.332">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bacteriochlorophyllide d C-8(2)-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.332#SIPCC8596D736EAC97E"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.332#SIP27241A7D44A12A2E"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, found in green sulfur bacteria (Chlorobiaceae) and green flimentous bacteria (Chloroflexaceae), is a radical S-adenosyl-L-methionine (AdoMet) enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It adds one or two methyl groups at the C-8(2) position of bacteriochlorophylls of the c, d and e types.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These methylations play a role in fine-tuning the structural arrangement of the bacteriochlorophyll aggregates in chlorosomes and therefore directly influence chlorosomal absorption properties.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17586634"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.332#SIPCC8596D736EAC97E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>8,12-diethyl-3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 12-ethyl-8-propyl-3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.332#SIP27241A7D44A12A2E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>12-ethyl-8-propyl-3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 12-ethyl-8-isobutyl-3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17586634">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17586634"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17586634"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.333">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bacteriochlorophyllide d C-20 methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.333#SIP83A3FBC82956E952"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in green sulfur bacteria (Chlorobiaceae) and green flimentous bacteria (Chloroflexaceae), catalyzes the methylation of the C-20 methine bridge position in bacteriochlorophyllide d, forming bacteriochlorophyllide c.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15090495"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.333#SIP83A3FBC82956E952">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a bacteriochlorophyllide d + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a bacteriochlorophyllide c + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15090495">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/15090495"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15090495"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.334">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>methanethiol S-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.334#SIP6E3A8A0A17D45E29"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in many bacterial taxa, is involved in a pathway that converts L-methionine to dimethyl sulfide.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25807229"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.334#SIP6E3A8A0A17D45E29">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
