<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.346">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>U6 snRNA m(6)A methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.346#SIP5944B2302DBB6472"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, found in vertebrates, methylates a specific adenine in a hairpin structure of snRNA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The effects of the binding of the methyltransferase to its substrate is important for the regulation of the activity of an isoform of EC 2.5.1.6, that produces S-adenosyl-L-methionine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also binds (and maybe methylates) the lncRNAs XIST and MALAT1 as well as a number of pre-mRNAs at specific positions often found in the intronic regions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28525753"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29051200"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.346#SIP5944B2302DBB6472">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>adenosine in U6 snRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = H(+) + N(6)-methyladenosine in U6 snRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
