<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.355">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(9) N-trimethyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.355#SIPAF81998A4592B73F"/>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes several enzymes that successively methylate the L-lysine(9) residue of histone H3 (H3K9), ultimately generating a trimethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These modifications influence the binding of chromatin-associated proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In general, the methylation of H3K9 leads to transcriptional repression of the affected target genes. cf. EC 2.1.1.366, EC 2.1.1.367 and EC 2.1.1.368.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11094092"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11867540"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11959841"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12130538"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14633678"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20084102"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.355#SIPAF81998A4592B73F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-lysyl(9)-[histone H3] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3 H(+) + N(6),N(6),N(6)-trimethyl-L-lysyl(9)-[histone H3] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
