<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.357">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(36) N-dimethyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.357#SIPCB1F4557DA34710C"/>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes a group of metazoan enzymes that catalyze two successive methylations of lysine(36) of histone H3 (H3K36), forming mono- and dimethylated forms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These modifications influence the binding of chromatin-associated proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product can be further methylated to the trimethyl form by EC 2.1.1.358.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The yeast SET2 enzyme can catalyze all three methylations (see EC 2.1.1.359).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21187428"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21196496"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22099308"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22266761"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.357#SIPCB1F4557DA34710C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-lysyl(36)-[histone H3] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2 H(+) + N(6),N(6)-dimethyl-L-lysyl(36)-[histone H3] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
