<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.359">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(36) N-trimethyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.359#SIP30C8B8FB976FEAF2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from yeast, catalyzes the successive methylation of lysine(36) of histone H3 (H3K36), forming the trimethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These modifications influence the binding of chromatin-associated proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme couples the methylation reactions with transcriptional elongation through an interaction with the large subunit of RNA polymerase II.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In mammals this activity is catalyzed by two different enzymes, EC 2.1.1.357 and EC 2.1.1.358.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11839797"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12917322"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16087749"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20048053"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.359#SIP30C8B8FB976FEAF2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-lysyl(36)-[histone H3] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3 H(+) + N(6),N(6),N(6)-trimethyl-L-lysyl(36)-[histone H3] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
