<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.361">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H4]-lysine(20) N-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.361#SIP4054912C1D37D4D3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the monomethylation of the L-lysine(20) residue of histone H4 (H4K20).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This event is usually followed by further methylation by EC 2.1.1.362, [histone H4]-N-methyl-L-lysine(20) N-methyltransferase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme plays a pivotal role in DNA replication.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity is high during the G2 and M phases, but declines significantly during G1 and S phases.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Mutations in the enzyme have severe consequences, including DNA double-strand breaks, activation of DNA damage checkpoints, defective cell cycle progression, and reduced cell proliferation.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12086618"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12121615"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18166648"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19223465"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23345616"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
