<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.364">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(4) N-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.364#SIPC5E42BB01B2E4FEE"/>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes enzymes that catalyze a single methylation of the L-lysine(4) residue of histone H3 (H3K4), generating a monomethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This modifications influence the binding of chromatin-associated proteins and result in gene activation or suppression.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Some enzymes that catalyze this reaction continue to generate a trimethylated form; these enzymes are classified under EC 2.1.1.354.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11779497"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11850410"/>
