<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.365">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>MMP 1-O-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3-O-methylmannose polysaccharide 1-O-methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.365#SIP23029D40F91891EB"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires Mg(2+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Mycolicibacterium hassiacum, participates in the biosynthesis of 3-O-methylmannose polysaccharides (MMP), which are intracellular polymethylated polysaccharides implicated in the modulation of fatty acid metabolism in non-tuberculous mycobacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The methylation catalyzed by this enzyme was shown to block the reducing end of 3,3'-di-O-methyl-alpha-mannobiose, a probable early precursor of the 3-O-methylmannose polysaccharides.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30606802"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.365#SIP23029D40F91891EB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3,3'-di-O-methyl-4alpha-mannobiose + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 1,3,3'-tri-O-methyl-4alpha-mannobiose + H(+) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30606802">
