</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.366">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-N(6),N(6)-dimethyl-lysine(9) N-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.366#SIPC7E6AA1F8506B0D8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme methylates only dimethylated lysine(9) of histone H3 (H3K9), forming the trimethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This modification influences the binding of chromatin-associated proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In general, the methylation of H3K9 leads to transcriptional repression of the affected target genes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is highly up-regulated in Huntington disease patients. cf. EC 2.1.1.355, EC 2.1.1.367, and EC 2.1.1.368.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11791185"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14536086"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22939622"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.366#SIPC7E6AA1F8506B0D8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>N(6),N(6)-dimethyl-L-lysyl(9)-[histone H3] + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = H(+) + N(6),N(6),N(6)-trimethyl-L-lysyl(9)-[histone H3] + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
