<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.367">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(9) N-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.367#SIPD7D2AC5DDD6BD4DA"/>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes several enzymes that methylate the L-lysine-9 residue of histone H3 (H3K9) only once, generating a monomethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These modifications influence the binding of chromatin-associated proteins. cf. EC 2.1.1.355, EC 2.1.1.366, and EC 2.1.1.368.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22939622"/>
