<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.369">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(27) N-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.369#SIP930C76716C40E349"/>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes enzymes that methylate the L-lysine-27 residue of histone H3 only once, generating a monomethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This modification influences the binding of chromatin-associated proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The methylation of lysine-27 leads to transcriptional repression of the affected target genes. cf. EC 2.1.1.356 and EC 2.1.1.371.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19503079"/>
