</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.370">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(4) N-dimethyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.370#SIP00E4DD5AA30B02FF"/>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes enzymes that successively methylate the L-lysine(4) residue of histone H3 (H3K4) twice, ultimately generating a dimethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These modifications influence the binding of chromatin-associated proteins.The human NSD3 protein also catalyzes the activity of EC 2.1.1.371. cf. EC 2.1.1.354 and EC 2.1.1.364.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16682010"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
