<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.371">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[histone H3]-lysine(27) N-dimethyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.371#SIP327FCFA429A5FD1A"/>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes enzymes that successively methylate the L-lysine(27) residue of histone H3 (H3K27) twice, ultimately generating a dimethylated form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>These modifications influence the binding of chromatin-associated proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human NSD3 protein also catalyzes the activity of EC 2.1.1.370. Cf. EC 2.1.1.356 and EC 2.1.1.369.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16682010"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
