<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.373">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-hydroxy-4-(methylsulfanyl)butanoate S-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>methylthiohydroxybutyrate methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MTHB methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.373#SIPAF4DC76A757A27A4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the marine bacterium Labrenzia aggregata, participates in the biosynthesis of dimethylsulfoniopropanoate (DMSP).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A eukaryotic enzyme that shares little sequence similarity with the bacterial enzyme was identified in many marine phytoplankton species.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28191900"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29483657"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29574051"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.373#SIPAF4DC76A757A27A4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2R)-2-hydroxy-4-(methylsulfanyl)butanoate + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (2R)-4-(dimethylsulfaniumyl)-2-hydroxybutanoate + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
