<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/33064871"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33064871"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.375">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>NNS virus cap methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.375#SIPA2D67495166C9396"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from non-segmented negative strain (NNS) viruses (e.g. rhabdoviruses) catalyzes two successive methylations.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In higher eukaryotes the two methylations occur in the reverse order and are catalyzed by two different enzymes (cf. EC 2.1.1.56 and EC 2.1.1.57) that do not required a specific motif.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19710136"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.375#SIPA2D67495166C9396">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 5'-end (5'-triphosphoguanosine)-adenylyl-adenylyl-cytidylyl-adenosine in mRNA + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a 5'-end (N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-(2'-O-methyladenylyl)-adenylyl-cytidylyl-adenosine in mRNA + H(+) + 2 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19710136">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19710136"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19710136"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.376">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glycine betaine--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>glycine betaine methyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.376#SIPBA1C83D3328A47B4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from glycine betaine to a glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein (MtgC), is involved in methanogenesis from glycine betaine in some methanogenic archaea, and in glycine betaine degradation in some bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike similar enzymes involved in methanogenesis from methylated C1 compounds, this enzyme does not contain the unusual amino acid L-pyrrolysine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25313086"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31787957"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.376#SIPBA1C83D3328A47B4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Co(I)-[glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein] + glycine betaine + H(+) = methyl-Co(III)-[glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein] + N,N-dimethylglycine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25313086">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/25313086"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25313086"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31787957">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/31787957"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31787957"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.377">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[methyl-Co(III) glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein]--coenzyme M methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.377#SIP5510C1E7E74B93D2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which is involved in methanogenesis from glycine betaine, catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group bound to the cobalt cofactor of glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein to coenzyme M, forming the substrate for EC 2.8.4.1, which catalyzes the final step in methanogenesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the methanogenic archaeon Methanolobus vulcani B1d can also catalyze the activity of EC 2.1.1.246.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31787957"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.377#SIP5510C1E7E74B93D2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>coenzyme M + methyl-Co(III)-[glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein] = Co(I)-[glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein] + H(+) + methyl-coenzyme M.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31787957">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/31787957"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31787957"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.378">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[methyl-Co(III) glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein]--tetrahydrofolate methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.378#SIPDB6AD40CD9D78A21"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, characterized from the anaerobic bacterium Desulfitobacterium hafniense Y51, catalyzes a similar reaction to that of EC 2.1.1.258, but in the opposite direction, transferring a methyl group from a methylated corrinoid protein to tetrahydrofolate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The corrinoid protein is specifically methylated by EC 2.1.1.376.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25313086"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.378#SIPDB6AD40CD9D78A21">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + methyl-Co(III)-[glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein] = (6S)-5-methyl-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + Co(I)-[glycine betaine-specific corrinoid protein] + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25313086">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/25313086"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25313086"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.379">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[methyl coenzyme M reductase]-L-arginine C-5-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>methanogenesis marker protein 10</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.379#SIP95A0EEF5808EED91"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, present in methanogenic archaea, catalyzes a modification of an L-arginine residue at the active site of EC 2.8.4.1, which catalyzes the last and methane-releasing step of methanogenesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is a radical AdoMet (radical SAM) enzyme and contains an [4Fe-4S] cluster and a Coalpha-[alpha-(5-hydroxybenzimidazolyl)]-cobamide cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The methyl group, which is derived from S-adenosyl-L-methionine, is transferred to the cob(I)amide cofactor, forming methylcob(III)amide as an intermediate carrier, before being transferred to the arginine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29743535"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31113866"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31740491"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.379#SIP95A0EEF5808EED91">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>AH2 + L-arginyl-[methyl-coenzyme M reductase] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (5S)-C-methyl-L-arginyl-[methyl-coenzyme M reductase] + 5'-deoxyadenosine + A + 2 H(+) + L-methionine + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29743535">
