<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.388">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>proline betaine--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.1.388#SIPBA748CFF84FDFC32"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Eubacterium limosum, is a component of a system that transfers a methyl group from L-proline betaine to tetrahydrofolate, as part of an L-proline betaine degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The resulting 5-methyltetrahydrofolate is processed to acetyl-CoA via the Wood--Ljungdahl pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31341018"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.1.1.388#SIPBA748CFF84FDFC32">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Co(I)-[quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein] + H(+) + L-proline betaine = methyl-Co(III)-[quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein] + N-methyl-L-proline.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31341018">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
