<skos:prefLabel>methylmalonyl-CoA carboxytransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>methylmalonyl-CoA carboxyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>transcarboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.1.3.1#SIP5549604D31C1ED3E"/>
<rdfs:comment>A biotinyl-protein, containing cobalt and zinc.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, described from the bacterium Propionibacterium shermanii, is unique among the biotin-dependent enzymes in that it catalyzes carboxyl transfer between two organic molecules, utilizing two separate carboxyltransferase domains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is a very large complex, consisting of a hexameric central core of 12S subunits surrounded by six 5S subunit dimers, each connected to the central core by twelve 1.3S biotin carrier subunits.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3893281"/>
