<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.2.1.14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-fructose transaldolase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.2.1.14#SIPD323E981564E81E1"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.2.1.14#SIP7ED5211A3704D37A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacillus aryabhattai SOS1, is involved in a degradation pathway for 6-sulfo-D-quinovose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also use D-erythrose 4-phosphate as the acceptor, forming D-sedoheptulose 7-phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/32919372"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
