<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.97">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glycylpeptide N-tetradecanoyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptide N-myristoyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptide N-tetradecanoyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.97#SIP2D7B6DF25F6180F6"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of myristic acid from myristoyl-CoA to the amino group of the N-terminal glycine residue in a variety of eukaryotic proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It uses an ordered Bi Bi reaction in which myristoyl-CoA binds to the enzyme prior to the binding of the peptide substrate, and CoA release precedes the release of the myristoylated peptide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from yeast is profoundly affected by amino acids further from the N-terminus, and is particularly stimulated by a serine residue at position 5.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3106975"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3123489"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3566958"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9677304"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11371195"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.97#SIP2D7B6DF25F6180F6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>N-terminal glycyl-[protein] + tetradecanoyl-CoA = CoA + H(+) + N-tetradecanoylglycyl-[protein].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
