<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.135">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phosphatidylcholine--retinol O-acyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>lecithin retinol acyl transferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>lecithin-retinol acyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>lecithin--retinol acyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>retinyl ester synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.135#SIPE7591E9DB42D4749"/>
<rdfs:comment>A key enzyme in retinoid metabolism, catalyzing the transfer of an acyl group from the sn-1 position of phosphatidylcholine to retinol, forming retinyl esters which are then stored.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Recognizes the substrate both in free form and when bound to cellular-retinol-binding-protein, but has higher affinity for the bound form.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Can also esterify 11-cis-retinol.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2722792"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3410848"/>
