<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.177">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3,5-dihydroxybiphenyl synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>biphenyl synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>BIS</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.177#SIPC8403CD586AFEEF3"/>
<rdfs:comment>A polyketide synthase that is involved in the production of the phytoalexin aucuparin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>2-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA can also act as substrate but it leads to the derailment product 4-hydroxycoumarin (cf. EC 2.3.1.208).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme uses the same starter substrate as EC 2.3.1.151.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14595561"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17109150"/>
