<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.185">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tropine acyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TAT</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tropine acetyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tropine tigloyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.185#SIP0E8AB1B0344AAF41"/>
<rdfs:comment>Exhibits absolute specificity for the endo/3alpha configuration found in tropine as pseudotropine (tropan-3beta-ol; see EC 2.3.1.186) is not a substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Acts on a wide range of aliphatic acyl-CoA derivatives, with tigloyl-CoA and acetyl-CoA being the best substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is probably involved in the formation of the tropane alkaloid littorine, which is a precursor of hyoscyamine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1959620"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10626376"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16720272"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.185#SIP0E8AB1B0344AAF41">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an acyl-CoA + tropine = CoA + H(+) + O-acyltropine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
