<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.191">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.3.1.n1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>UDP-3-O-(3-hydroxymyristoyl)glucosamine N-acyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UDP-3-O-[3-hydroxymyristoyl]-D-glucosamine N-acyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UDP-3-O-acyl-glucosamine N-acyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.191#SIPBB431E3E1DC1E3EE"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.191#SIP3B7CA8D58567E463"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes a step of lipid A biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>LpxD from Escherichia coli prefers (3R)-3-hydroxytetradecanoyl-[acyl-carrier protein], but it does not an absolute specificity for 14-carbon hydroxy fatty acids, as it can transfer other fatty acids, including odd-chain fatty acids, if they are available to the organism.</rdfs:comment>
