<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.250">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[Wnt protein] O-palmitoleoyl transferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>porcupine</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.250#SIPB0410F73DF6AD67A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in animals, modifies a specific serine residue in Wnt proteins, e.g. Ser(209) in human Wnt3a and Ser(224) in chicken WNT1.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can accept C13 to C16 fatty acids in vitro, but only (9Z)-hexadecenoate modification is observed in vivo. cf. EC 3.1.1.98.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17141155"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24292069"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25451226"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
