<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.272">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-acetylphloroglucinol acetyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MAPG ATase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.272#SIPACA47AF8ECECCC82"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp. YGJ3 is composed of three subunits named PhlA, PhlB and PhlC.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Production of 2,4-diacetylphloroglucinol, which has antibiotic activity, is strongly inhibited by chloride ions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22451400"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.272#SIPACA47AF8ECECCC82">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 2-acetylphloroglucinol = 1,3,5-trihydroxybenzene + 2,4-diacetylphloroglucinol + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22451400">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/22451400"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22451400"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.273">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>diglucosylglycerate octanoyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DGG octanoyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.273#SIP9417F7DBFEAC8D10"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from mycobacteria, is involved in the biosynthesis of methylglucose lipopolysaccharide (MGLP).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also act on 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate, but with lower activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26324178"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.273#SIP9417F7DBFEAC8D10">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2R)-2-O-[alpha-D-glucopyranosyl-(1->6)-alpha-D-glucopyranosyl]-glycerate + octanoyl-CoA = (2R)-2-O-[6-O-octanoyl-alpha-D-glucopyranosyl-(1->6)-alpha-D-glucopyranosyl]-glycerate + CoA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26324178">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26324178"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26324178"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.274">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.3.1.n2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phosphate acyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acyl-[acyl-carrier-protein]--phosphate acyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acyl-ACP phosphotransacylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphate-acyl-ACP acyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.274#SIP8A53211398ADC7AC"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in bacteria, catalyzes the synthesis of fatty acyl-phosphate from acyl-[acyl carrier protein], a step in the most widely distributed bacterial pathway for the initiation of phospholipid formation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While the activity is modestly enhanced by Mg(2+), the enzyme does not require a divalent cation.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16949372"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17645809"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19058030"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29199103"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.274#SIP8A53211398ADC7AC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a fatty acyl-[ACP] + phosphate = an acyl phosphate + holo-[ACP].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
