<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.278">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>mycolipenoyl-CoA--2-(long-chain-fatty acyl)-trehalose mycolipenoyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.278#SIPB14119E3A5BFFE1D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Mycobacterium tuberculosis, participates in the biosynthesis of polyacyltrehalose (PAT), a pentaacylated, trehalose-based glycolipid found in the cell wall of pathogenic strains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes two successive activities - it first transfers an acyl (often palmitoyl) group to position 2 (see EC 2.3.1.279), followed by the transfer of a mycolipenyl group to position 3.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19276083"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.278#SIPB14119E3A5BFFE1D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-O-(long-chain fatty acyl)-alpha,alpha-trehalose + a mycolipenoyl-CoA = 2-O-(long-chain fatty acyl)-3-O-mycolipenoyl-trehalose + CoA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19276083">
