<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>long-chain-acyl-CoA--trehalose acyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.279#SIP576A923F00EE921B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Mycobacterium tuberculosis, participates in the biosynthesis of polyacyltrehalose (PAT), a pentaacylated, trehalose-based glycolipid found in the cell wall of pathogenic strains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes two successive activities - it first transfers an acyl (often palmitoyl) group to position 2, followed by the transfer of a mycolipenyl group to position 3 (see EC 2.3.1.278).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19276083"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.279#SIP576A923F00EE921B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a long-chain fatty acyl-CoA + alpha,alpha-trehalose = 2-O-(long-chain fatty acyl)-alpha,alpha-trehalose + CoA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
