<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.281">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>coelimycin P1 polyketide synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.281#SIP76AB577E7E456E2B"/>
<rdfs:comment>This polyketide synthase enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces coelicolor A3(2), catalyzes the first reaction in the biosynthesis of coelimycin P1.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is made of three proteins which together comprise six modules that contain a total of 28 domains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>An NADH-dependent terminal reductase domain at the C-terminus of the enzyme catalyzes the reductive release of the product.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17009021"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28451186"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.281#SIP76AB577E7E456E2B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>12 H(+) + 6 malonyl-CoA + NADH + 5 NADPH = (2E,5S,6E,8E,10E)-5-hydroxydodeca-2,6,8,10-tetraenal + 6 CO2 + 6 CoA + 4 H2O + NAD(+) + 5 NADP(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
