<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.299">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sphingoid base N-stearoyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mammalian ceramide synthase 1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.299#SIPACD30EE87A7E4EF7"/>
<rdfs:comment>Mammals have six ceramide synthases that exhibit relatively strict specificity regarding the chain-length of their acyl-CoA substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Ceramide synthase 1 (CERS1) is structurally and functionally distinctive from all other CERS enzymes, and is specific for stearoyl-CoA as the acyl donor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can use multiple sphingoid bases including sphinganine, sphingosine, and phytosphingosine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12105227"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22661289"/>
