<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.305">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acyl-[acyl-carrier protein]--UDP-2-acetamido-3-amino-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranose N-acyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.305#SIP815587495896D032"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is found in bacterial species whose lipid A contains 2,3-diamino-2,3-dideoxy-D-glucopyranose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Some enzymes, such as that from Leptospira interrogans, are highly specific for 2,3-diamino-2,3-dideoxy-D-glucopyranose, while others, such as the enzyme from Acidithiobacillus ferrooxidans, are also able to accept UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine (cf. EC 2.3.1.129).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from different organisms also differ in their specificity for the acyl donor. The enzyme from L. interrogans is highly specific for (3R)-3-hydroxydodecanoyl-[acyl-carrier protein], while that from Mesorhizobium loti functions almost equally well with 10-, 12-, and 14-carbon 3-hydroxyacyl-[acyl-carrier protein]s.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15044493"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19456129"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.305#SIP815587495896D032">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a (3R)-hydroxyacyl-[ACP] + UDP-2-acetamido-3-amino-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranose = a UDP-2-acetamido-3-{[(3R)-3-hydroxyacyl]amino}-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranose + H(+) + holo-[ACP].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
