<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.311">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tRNA carboxymethyluridine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.311#SIPF4836EEA2C23F853"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in eukaryotes, most archaea, and some bacteria, catalyzes the first step in modification of the wobble uridine base of certain tRNAs.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In eukaryotes the enzyme is a complex of six conserved subunits, with ELP3 being the catalytic subunit.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In archaea and bacteria the enzyme consists of a single subunit, homologous to ELP3.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme contains an [4Fe-4S] cluster and uses radical chemistry. A 5'-deoxyadenosyl radical generated in the radical AdoMet (SAM) domain attacks the acetyl-CoA donor, activating its methyl group, which forms a C-C bond with C5 of the uridine moiety.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16420352"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25151136"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30733442"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.311#SIPF4836EEA2C23F853">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>acetyl-CoA + H2O + S-adenosyl-L-methionine + uridine(34) in tRNA = 5'-deoxyadenosine + 5-(carboxymethyl)uridine(34) in tRNA + CoA + 2 H(+) + L-methionine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
