<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.313">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>NAD-dependent lipoamidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.1.313#SIP5A7BEA6A3D83E89E"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, a member of the sirtuin family, removes the lipoyl group from the dihydrolipoamide acyltransferase (E2) component of 2-oxo acid dehydrogenase complexes such as EC 1.2.1.104.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme often has additional activities and can remove other modifications of lysine residues such as acetyl and biotinyl groups. cf. EC 3.5.1.138.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25525879"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28900027"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30913880"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.1.313#SIP5A7BEA6A3D83E89E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + N(6)-[(R)-lipoyl]-L-lysyl-[protein] + NAD(+) = 2''-O-lipoyl-ADP-D-ribose + L-lysyl-[protein] + nicotinamide.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
