<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>gamma-glutamyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>gamma-glutamyltranspeptidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>gamma-glutamyl transpeptidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>glutamyl transpeptidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.2#SIPFB26CE63B1EABA3C"/>
<rdfs:comment>The mammlian enzyme is part of the cell antioxidant defense mechanism.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It initiates extracellular glutathione (GSH) breakdown, provides cells with a local cysteine supply and contributes to maintain intracelular GSH levels.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The protein also has EC 3.4.19.13 activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme consists of two chains that are created by the proteolytic cleavage of a single precursor polypeptide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The N-terminal L-threonine of the C-terminal subunit functions as the active site for both the cleavage and the hydrolysis reactions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5698023"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6030345"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16618936"/>
