<skos:altLabel>leucyl/phenylalanyl-tRNA--protein transferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>leucyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>leucyl-tRNA--protein transferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.6#SIP3C8CABEFD3658F55"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.6#SIP5952744DCC778925"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.6#SIPD766A0B37218BA87"/>
<rdfs:comment>Participates in the N-end rule protein degradation pathway in certain bacteria, by attaching the primary destabilizing residue L-leucine to the N-termini of proteins that have an N-terminal L-arginine or L-lysine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Once modified, the proteins are recognized by EC 3.4.21.92.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also transfers L-phenylalanine in vitro, but this has not been observed in vivo. cf. EC 2.3.2.8 and EC 2.3.2.29.</rdfs:comment>
