<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.18">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-L-lysyl-(N(6)-triglycine)-D-alanyl-D-alanine-diphosphoundecaprenyl-N-acetylglucosamine:glycine glycyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.18#SIPA6041ACB52A36F91"/>
<rdfs:comment>This Staphylococcus aureus enzyme catalyzes the successive transfer of two glycine moieties from charged tRNAs to MurNAc-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-(N(6)-tri-Gly)-D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc, attaching them to the three glycine molecules that were previously attached to the N(6) of the L-lysine at position 3 of the pentapeptide by EC 2.3.2.16 (FemX) and EC 2.3.2.17 (FemA).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This is the last step in the synthesis of the pentaglycine interpeptide bridge that is used in this organism for the cross-linking of different glycan strands to each other.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9393725"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14523106"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15228543"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.18#SIPA6041ACB52A36F91">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 glycyl-tRNA(Gly) + MurNAc-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-(N(6)-tri-Gly)-D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc = 2 H(+) + MurNAc-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-(N(6)-penta-Gly)-D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc + 2 tRNA(Gly).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
