<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.20">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cyclo(L-leucyl-L-phenylalanyl) synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.20#SIP00FB366BBA727670"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction proceeds following a ping-pong mechanism forming a covalent intermediate between an active site serine and the L-phenylalanine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The protein, found in the bacterium Streptomyces noursei, also forms cyclo(L-phenylalanyl-L-phenylalanyl), cyclo(L-methionyl-L-phenylalanyl), cyclo(L-phenylalanyl-L-tyrosyl) and cyclo(L-methionyl-L-tyrosyl).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19430487"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21296757"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.20#SIP00FB366BBA727670">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-leucyl-tRNA(Leu) + L-phenylalanyl-tRNA(Phe) = cyclo(L-phenylalanyl-L-leucyl) + H(+) + tRNA(Leu) + tRNA(Phe).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
