<skos:altLabel>ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme E2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.23#SIP5E219FEB61733FA7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme acquires the activated ubquitin from the E1 ubiquitin-activating enzyme (EC 6.2.1.45) and binds it via a transthioesterification reaction to itself.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the human enzyme the catalytic center is located at Cys-87 where ubiquitin is bound via its C-terminal glycine in a thioester linkage.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19940261"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20061386"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22563859"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22815819"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23385757"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
