<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.29">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>aspartate/glutamate leucyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.29#SIP95642A8F5D490CDA"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.29#SIPC0F2C7100934FB16"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in the N-end rule protein degradation pathway in certain bacteria, by attaching the primary destabilizing residue L-leucine to the N-termini of proteins that have an N-terminal L-aspartate or L-glutamate residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Once modified, the proteins are recognized by EC 3.4.21.92. cf. EC 2.3.2.6 and EC 2.3.2.8.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16492767"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
