<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.33">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>RCR-type E3 ubiquitin transferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MYCBP2</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PHR1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.33#SIPF96C1E3A4518BA83"/>
<rdfs:comment>RCR-type E3 ubiquitin transferases is a class of RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferase (see EC 2.3.2.27) that mediates ubiquitination of acceptor proteins via an internal cysteine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The RING1 domain binds an EC 2.3.2.23 and transfers the ubiquitin that is bound to it to an internal cysteine residue on a mediator loop of the RCR-type ligase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The ubiquitin may be transferred to a second internal cysteine before the transfer of the ubiquitin from the RCR-type ligase to the substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29643511"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.33#SIPF96C1E3A4518BA83">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>[E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme]-S-ubiquitinyl-L-cysteine + [acceptor protein]-L-threonine = [E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme]-L-cysteine + [acceptor protein]-3-O-ubiquitinyl-L-threonine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29643511">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/29643511"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29643511"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.34">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>E2 NEDD8-conjugating enzyme</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NEDD8-carrier-protein E2</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NEDD8-conjugating enzyme E2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.34#SIP837C31DCDF54B2F0"/>
<rdfs:comment>Some RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferases (EC 2.3.2.27) are not able to bind a substrate protein directly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Instead, they form complexes with a cullin scaffold protein and a substrate recognition module, which are known as CRL (Cullin-RING-Ligase) complexes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The cullin protein needs to be activated by the ubiquitin-like protein NEDD8 in a process known as neddylation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Like ubiquitin, the NEDD8 protein ends with two glycine residues.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>EC 6.2.1.64 activates NEDD8 in an ATP-dependent reaction by forming a high-energy thioester intermediate between NEDD8 and one of its cysteine residues.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The activated NEDD8 is subsequently transferred to a cysteine residue of an E2 NEDD8-conjugating enzyme, and is eventually conjugated to a lysine residue of specific substrates in the presence of the appropriate E3 transferase (EC 2.3.2.32).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9694792"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10207026"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15361859"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19250909"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.34#SIP837C31DCDF54B2F0">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>[E1 NEDD8-activating enzyme]-S-[NEDD8 protein]-yl-L-cysteine + [E2 NEDD8-conjugating enzyme]-L-cysteine = [E1 NEDD8-activating enzyme]-L-cysteine + [E2 NEDD8-conjugating enzyme]-S-[NEDD8-protein]-yl-L-cysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
