<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.35">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>capsaicin synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.35#SIP89031AD58FD9CFD4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found only in plants that belong to the Capsicum genus, catalyzes the last step in the biosynthesis of capsaicinoids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the acylation of vanillylamine by a branched-chain fatty acid.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The exact structure of the fatty acid determines the type of capsaicinoid formed.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12175073"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15918882"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24441736"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.35#SIP89031AD58FD9CFD4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(6E)-8-methylnon-6-enoyl-CoA + vanillylamine = capsaicin + CoA + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
