<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.37">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ergosteryl-3beta-O-L-aspartate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.2.37#SIPE4E74CAA89DF6338"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, detected in fungal species that belong to the Ascomycota and Basidiomycota phyla and characterized from Aspergillus fumigatus, is bifunctional.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The AspRS domain catalyzes the transfer of L-aspartate to tRNA(Asp) (EC 6.1.1.12), while the second domain carries out the transfer of L-aspartate to the 3beta-hydroxyl of ergosterol.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/32541034"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.2.37#SIPE4E74CAA89DF6338">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ergosterol + L-aspartyl-tRNA(Asp) = 1-(ergostan-3beta-yl)-L-aspartate + tRNA(Asp).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
