<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.3.20">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acyl-CoA:acyl-CoA alkyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.3.20#SIP1CF2AB8EE1C46456"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in certain bacterial species, catalyzes a head-to-head non-decarboxylative Claisen condensation of two acyl-CoA molecules, resulting in formation of a 2-alkyl-3-oxoalkanoic acid.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is part of a pathway for the production of olefins.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20418444"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21266575"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22524624"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27815501"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.3.20#SIP1CF2AB8EE1C46456">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 1,2-saturated acyl-CoA + an acyl-CoA + H2O = an (R)-2-alkyl-3-oxoalkanoate + 2 CoA + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
