<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.3.21">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.3.1.182"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(R)-citramalate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.3.3.21#SIP04945116996F0364"/>
<rdfs:comment>One of the enzymes involved in a pyruvate-derived pathway for isoleucine biosynthesis that is found in some bacterial and archaeal species.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can be inhibited by isoleucine, the end-product of the pathway, but not by leucine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is highly specific for pyruvate as substrate, as the 2-oxo acids 3-methyl-2-oxobutanoate, 2-oxobutanoate, 4-methyl-2-oxopentanoate, 2-oxohexanoate and 2-oxoglutarate cannot act as substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9864346"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15292141"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.3.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.3.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.3.3.21#SIP04945116996F0364">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>acetyl-CoA + H2O + pyruvate = (3R)-citramalate + CoA + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
