<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.11">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glycogen(starch) synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UDP-glucose--glycogen glucosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.11#SIPBBF4B83BE4B9B898"/>
<rdfs:comment>The description (official name) varies according to the source of the enzyme and the nature of its synthetic product.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Glycogen synthase from animal tissues is a complex of a catalytic subunit and the protein glycogenin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme requires glucosylated glycogenin as a primer; this is the reaction product of EC 2.4.1.186.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A similar enzyme utilizes ADP-glucose (cf. EC 2.4.1.21).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2970965"/>
