<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.60#SIPFEA768C9EFBCE068"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.60#SIP80C002CD4C525781"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Salmonella participates in the biosynthesis of the repeat unit of O antigens produced by strains that belong to the A, B and D1-D3 groups.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is able to transfer abequose, paratose, or tyvelose, depending on the availability of the specific dideoxyhexose in a particular strain.</rdfs:comment>
