<skos:altLabel>uridine diphosphoacetylgalactosamine-galactosylgalactosylglucosylceramide acetylgalactosaminyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.79#SIPC41176C394A81F7D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Globoside is a neutral glycosphingolipid in human erythrocytes and has blood-group-P-antigen activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>UDP-GalNAc is the only sugar donor that is used efficiently by the enzyme: UDP-Gal and UDP-GlcNAc result in very low enzyme activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Lactosylceramide, globoside and gangliosides GM3 and GD3 are not substrates.</rdfs:comment>
