<skos:altLabel>uridine diphosphoglucose-cyanohydrin glucosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>uridine diphosphoglucose-p-hydroxymandelonitrile glucosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.85#SIPBD29C8AD4FFEC734"/>
<rdfs:comment>Acts on a wide range of substrates in vitro, including cyanohydrins, terpenoids, phenolics, hexanol derivatives and plant hormones, in a regiospecific manner.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the biosynthesis of the cyanogenic glucoside dhurrin in sorghum, along with EC 1.14.14.36 and EC 1.14.14.37.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This reaction prevents the disocciation and release of toxic hydrogen cyanide.</rdfs:comment>
