<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>scopoletin + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = H(+) + scopolin + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.129">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>peptidoglycan glycosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>bactoprenyldiphospho-N-acetylmuramoyl-(N-acetyl-D-glucosaminyl)-pentapeptide:peptidoglycan N-acetylmuramoyl-N-acetyl-D-glucosaminyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>penicillin binding protein (3 or 1B)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptidoglycan TGase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptidoglycan transglycosylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PG-II</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.129#SIPEC836C642218B394"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also works when the lysine residue is replaced by meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioate (meso-2,6-diaminopimelate, A2pm) combined with adjacent residues through its L-center, as it is in Gram-negative and some Gram-positive organisms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The undecaprenol involved is ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the synthesis of cell-wall peptidoglycan.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6802846"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9841666"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11320055"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.129#SIPEC836C642218B394">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>[GlcNAc-(1->4)-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)](n)-di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + beta-D-GlcNAc-(1->4)-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)-di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate = [GlcNAc-(1->4)-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)](n+1)-di-trans-octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
