</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.132">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>GDP-Man:Man1GlcNAc2-PP-dolichol alpha-1,3-mannosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GDP-Man:Man1GlcNAc2-PP-Dol alpha-1,3-mannosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mannosyltransferase II</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.132#SIP27B945D851AFDBE4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The biosynthesis of asparagine-linked glycoproteins utilizes a dolichyl diphosphate-linked glycosyl donor, which is assembled by the series of membrane-bound glycosyltransferases that comprise the dolichol pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Alg2 mannosyltransferase from Saccharomyces cerevisiae carries out an alpha1,3-mannosylation of D-Man-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcNAc-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcNAc-diphosphodolichol, followed by an alpha1,6-mannosylation (cf. EC 2.4.1.257), to form the first branched pentasaccharide intermediate of the dolichol pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16878994"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19282279"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.132#SIP27B945D851AFDBE4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>beta-D-Man-(1->4)-beta-D-GlcNAc-(1->4)-alpha-D-GlcNAc-diphosphodolichol + GDP-alpha-D-mannose = alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-beta-D-Man-(1->4)-beta-D-GlcNAc-(1->4)-alpha-D-GlcNAc-diphosphodolichol + GDP + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
