<skos:prefLabel>N-acetyllactosaminide beta-1,6-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>I-branching beta1,6-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.150#SIP879653C84DDFF6C2"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.150#SIP1CC7B201B368E289"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme acts on poly-N-acetyllactosamine [glycan chains of beta-D-galactosyl-(1->4)-N-acetyl-D-glucosamine units connected by beta(1,3) linkages] attached to proteins or lipids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It transfers a GlcNAc residue by beta(1,6) linkage to galactosyl residues close to non-reducing terminals, introducing a branching pattern known as I branching.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6219989"/>
