<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.202">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2,4-dihydroxy-7-methoxy-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-3(4H)-one 2-D-glucosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DIMBOA glucosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.202#SIPD974FFC39ED30C80"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.202#SIPE50BFADA56E7B638"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in the detoxification of the benzoxazinoids DIBOA (2,4-dihydroxy-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-3(4H)-one) and DIMBOA (2,4-dihydroxy-7-methoxy-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-3(4H)-one) which are stored as the respective non-toxic glucosides in the vacuoles in some plants, most commonly from the family of Poaceae (grasses).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Benzoxazinoids are known to exhibit antimicrobial, antifeedant, and antiinsecticidal effects and are involved in the interaction of plants with other plants, insects, or microorganisms.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11851909"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16666853"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.202#SIPD974FFC39ED30C80">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>DIMBOA + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = DIMBOA beta-D-glucoside + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.202#SIPE50BFADA56E7B638">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>DIBOA + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = DIBOA beta-D-glucoside + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
