<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.226">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>N-acetylgalactosaminyl-proteoglycan 3-beta-glucuronosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>chondroitin glucuronyltransferase II</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.226#SIPECBC4A40994409B8"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.226#SIP8E13FE5AC717AC67"/>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the biosynthesis of chondroitin and dermatan sulfate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human chondroitin synthetase is a bifunctional glycosyltransferase, which also has the EC 2.4.1.175 activity required for the synthesis of the chondroitin sulfate disaccharide repeats.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Similar chondroitin synthase 'copolymerases' can be found in Pasteurella multocida and Escherichia coli.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>There is also another human protein with apparently only the 3-beta-glucuronosyltransferase activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10818104"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11514575"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11943778"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12145278"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
