</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.246">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>mannosylfructose-phosphate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mannosylfructose-6-phosphate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MFPS</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.246#SIP83CE6589197B4A14"/>
<rdfs:comment>GDP-mannose can be replaced by ADP-mannose but with a concomitant decrease in activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product of this reaction is dephosphorylated by EC 3.1.3.79 to form the non-reducing disaccharide mannosylfructose, which is the major endogenous osmolyte produced by several alpha-proteobacteria in response to osmotic stress.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The F in the product name is used to indicate that the fructose residue of sucrose carries the substituent.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17728402"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.246#SIP83CE6589197B4A14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>beta-D-fructose 6-phosphate + GDP-alpha-D-mannose = beta-D-fructofuranosyl alpha-D-mannopyranoside 6(F)-phosphate + GDP + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17728402">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17728402"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17728402"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.247">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>beta-D-galactosyl-(1->4)-L-rhamnose phosphorylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-galactosyl-beta1->4-L-rhamnose phosphorylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GalRhaP</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.247#SIP4BF2527EBC0A3411"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Clostridium phytofermentans is also active toward toward beta-D-galactosyl derivatives of L-mannose, L-lyxose, D-glucose, 2-deoxy-D-glucose, and D-galactose in this order.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Differs from 1,3-beta-galactosyl-N-acetylhexosamine phosphorylase (EC 2.4.1.211) in being active toward L-rhamnose and inactive toward N-acetyl hexosamine derivatives.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19491100"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.247#SIP4BF2527EBC0A3411">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>beta-D-galactosyl-(1->4)-L-rhamnose + phosphate = alpha-D-galactose 1-phosphate + L-rhamnopyranose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19491100">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19491100"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19491100"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.248">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cycloisomaltooligosaccharide glucanotransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.248#SIP5F691A64571A5322"/>
<rdfs:comment>Specific for (1->6)-alpha-D-glucans (dextrans) and, unlike cyclomaltodextrin glucanotransferase (EC 2.4.1.19), without activity toward (1->4)-alpha-D-glucans, such as amylose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It also has no activity on oligosaccharides, such as amylopectin and pullulan, containing (1->6)-alpha-D-glucosidic linkages at branch points.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Bacillus circulans T-3040 has been shown to form cycloisomalto-oligosaccharides of three sizes (7, 8 and 9 glucose units).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It will also catalyze the disproportionation of two isomalto-oligosaccharides molecules to yield a series of isomalto-oligosachharides and the addition of D-glucose to cycloisomalto-oligosaccharides with ring opening to form isomalto-oligosaccharides.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7515357"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16926507"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.248#SIP5F691A64571A5322">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>cyclizes part of a (1->6)-alpha-D-glucan chain by formation of a (1->6)-alpha-D-glucosidic bond.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7515357">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/7515357"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7515357"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16926507">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/16926507"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16926507"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.249">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>delphinidin 3',5'-O-glucosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UDP-glucose:anthocyanin 3',5'-O-glucosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.249#SIP34AB80B2C9543BDF"/>
<rdfs:comment>Ternatins are a group of polyacetylated delphinidin glucosides that confer blue color to the petals of butterfly pea (Clitoria ternatea).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes two reactions in the biosynthesis of ternatin C5: the conversion of delphinidin 3-O-(6''-O-malonyl)-beta-D-glucoside to delphinidin 3-O-(6''-O-malonyl)-beta-D-glucoside-3'-O-beta-D-glucoside, followed by the conversion of the later to ternatin C5, by transferring two glucosyl groups in a stepwise manner.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17668234"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.249#SIP34AB80B2C9543BDF">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>delphinidin 3-O-(6''-O-malonyl)-beta-D-glucoside + 2 UDP-alpha-D-glucose = 2 H(+) + ternatin C5 + 2 UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17668234">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17668234"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17668234"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.250">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.4.1.n3"/>
<skos:prefLabel>D-inositol-3-phosphate glycosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mycothiol glycosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N-acetylglucosamine-inositol-phosphate N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.250#SIP60FEC8B7A6EE36A3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which belongs to the GT-B fold superfamily, catalyzes the first dedicated reaction in the biosynthesis of mycothiol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrate was initially believed to be inositol, but eventually shown to be D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A substantial conformational change occurs upon UDP binding, which generates the binding site for D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12754249"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16940050"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18390549"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.250#SIP60FEC8B7A6EE36A3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>1D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = 1D-myo-inositol 2-acetamido-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranoside 3-phosphate + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12754249">
