<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.268">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glucosylglycerate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.268#SIP0E945206583B03C0"/>
<rdfs:comment>Persephonella marina possesses two enzymatic systems for the synthesis of glucosylglycerate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The first one is a single-step pathway in which glucosylglycerate synthase catalyzes the synthesis of 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate in one-step from ADP-glucose and D-glycerate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The second system is a two-step pathway in which EC 2.4.1.266 catalyzes the conversion of NDP-glucose and 3-phospho-D-glycerate into 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-3-phospho-D-glycerate, which is then converted to 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate by EC 3.1.3.85.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17369297"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20061481"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.268#SIP0E945206583B03C0">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(R)-glycerate + ADP-alpha-D-glucose = (2R)-2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-glycerate + ADP + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17369297">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17369297"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17369297"/>
</rdf:Description>
