<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>rhamnogalacturonan I rhamnosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RG I rhamnosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.351#SIP1C38AE13763B65B6"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from Vigna angularis (azuki beans), participates in the biosynthesis of rhamnogalacturonan type I.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It does not require any metal ions, and prefers substrates with a degree of polymerization larger than 7.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28283389"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
