<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.361">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>GDP-mannose:di-myo-inositol-1,3'-phosphate beta-1,2-mannosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MDIP synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.361#SIP184E2AA3AE390A26"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the hyperthermophilic bacterium Thermotoga maritima is involved in the synthesis of the solutes 2-O-(beta-D-mannosyl)-bis(myo-inositol) 1,3'-phosphate and 2-O-(beta-D-mannosyl-(1->2)-beta-D-mannosyl)-bis(myo-inositol) 1,3'-phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19648237"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.361#SIP184E2AA3AE390A26">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>bis(myo-inositol) 1,3'-phosphate + 2 GDP-alpha-D-mannose = 2-O-(beta-D-mannosyl-(1->2)-beta-D-mannosyl)-bis(myo-inositol) 1,3'-phosphate + 2 GDP + 2 H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19648237">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19648237"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19648237"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.362">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>alpha-(1->3) branching sucrase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>branching sucrase A</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>BRS-A</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.362#SIP2CCC4BF35DB27294"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Leuconostoc spp. is responsible for producing alpha-(1->3) branches in alpha-(1->6) glucans by transferring the glucose residue from fructose to a 3-hydroxyl group of a glucan.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26763236"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27141938"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.362#SIP2CCC4BF35DB27294">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>sucrose + a (1->6)-alpha-D-glucan = D-fructose + a (1->6)-alpha-D-glucan containing a (1->3)-alpha-D-glucose branch.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26763236">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26763236"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26763236"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27141938">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/27141938"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27141938"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.363">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ginsenoside 20-O-glucosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UGT71A27</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.363#SIPBF3187DF0A9FC080"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.363#SIP81F4D90BE8F72A99"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.363#SIP712F0D7AD140A499"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.363#SIPFD1FC1B435298733"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.363#SIPBDE7AD6F3675268B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Panax ginseng, transfers a glucosyl moiety to the free C20(S)-OH group of dammarane derivative substrates, including protopanaxatriol, dammarenediol II, (20S)-ginsenoside Rh2, and (20S)-ginsenoside Rg3.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It does not act on the 20R epimer of protopanaxadiol, or on ginsenosides that are glucosylated at the C-6 position, such as ginsenoside Rh1 or ginsenoside Rg2.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24603359"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26032089"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.363#SIPBF3187DF0A9FC080">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-protopanaxadiol + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside C-K + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.363#SIP81F4D90BE8F72A99">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-protopanaxatriol + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside F1 + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.363#SIP712F0D7AD140A499">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside Rg3 + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside Rd + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.363#SIPFD1FC1B435298733">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside Rh2 + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside F2 + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.363#SIPBDE7AD6F3675268B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dammarenediol-II + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-20-O-(beta-D-glucosyl)-3-hydroxydammarene + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24603359">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/24603359"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24603359"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26032089">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26032089"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26032089"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.364">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>protopanaxadiol-type ginsenoside 3-O-glucosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UGT74AE2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.364#SIP3F3BEB03702771D8"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.364#SIP00E3AC5600350207"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Panax ginseng, transfers a glucosyl moiety to the free C-3-OH group of (20S)-protopanaxadiol and ginsenoside C-K.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25320211"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.364#SIP3F3BEB03702771D8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-protopanaxadiol + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside Rh2 + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.364#SIP00E3AC5600350207">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside C-K + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside F2 + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25320211">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/25320211"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25320211"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.365">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>protopanaxadiol-type ginsenoside-3-O-glucoside 2''-O-glucosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UGT94Q2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.365#SIPF93C81EB4FE723A5"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.365#SIPF5E96DC66E350E1F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Panax ginseng, transfers a glucosyl moiety to the 2'' position of the glucose moiety in the protopanaxadiol-type ginsenoside-3-O-glucosides (20S)-ginsenoside Rh2 and ginsenoside F2.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25320211"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.365#SIPF93C81EB4FE723A5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside Rh2 + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside Rg3 + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.365#SIPF5E96DC66E350E1F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside F2 + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = (20S)-ginsenoside Rd + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25320211">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/25320211"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25320211"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.366">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ginsenoside F1 6-O-glucosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UGTPg101</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.366#SIP3545F9A3F38CE7D1"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Panax ginseng, glucosylates the C-6 position of ginsenoside F1.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also glucosylates the C-20 position of protopanaxatriol, which forms ginsenoside F1 (cf. EC 2.4.1.363).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However, unlike EC 2.4.1.367, it is not able to glucosylate the C-6 position of protopanaxatriol when position C-20 is not glucosylated.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26032089"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
