<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.370">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>inositol phosphorylceramide mannosyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.1.370#SIPA5E3EDFF0FA33A47"/>
<rdfs:comment>The simplest complex sphingolipid of yeast, inositol-phospho-alpha-hydroxyphytoceramide (IPC), is usually mannosylated to yield mannosyl-inositol-phospho-alpha hydroxyphytoceramide (MIPC).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is located in the Golgi apparatus, and utilizes GDP-alpha-D-mannose as the mannosyl group donor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It consists of a catalytic subunit (SUR1 or CSH1) and a regulatory subunit (CSG2).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9323360"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9395539"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12954640"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.4.1.370#SIPA5E3EDFF0FA33A47">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 1D-myo-inositol-1-phospho-N-[(R)-2-hydroxy-very-long-chain fatty acyl]-(R)-4-hydroxysphingoid base + GDP-alpha-D-mannose = an alpha-D-mannosyl-(1&lt;->6)-1D-myo-inositol-1-phospho-N-[(R)-2-hydroxy-very-long-chain fatty acyl]-(R)-4-hydroxysphingoid base + GDP + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
