<skos:prefLabel>tRNA-guanosine(34) queuine transglycosylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>guanine insertion enzyme</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Q-insertase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>queuine(34) transfer ribonucleate ribosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>queuine tRNA-ribosyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TGT</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tRNA transglycosylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.4.2.64#SIP57E990FCB56644AC"/>
<rdfs:comment>Certain prokaryotic and eukaryotic tRNAs contain the modified base queuine at position 34.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In eukaryotes and a small number of prokaryotes queuine is salvaged and incorporated into tRNA directly via a base-exchange reaction, replacing guanine. cf. EC 2.4.2.29.</rdfs:comment>
