<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15356000"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.43">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>nicotianamine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.43#SIP4EDA8461C8516420"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.43#SIP4EDA8461C8516420">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3 H(+) + nicotianamine + 3 S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.44">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>homospermidine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.44#SIP90FCA8DAF0D73F6D"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.44#SIPC8A362AC2000B3D3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction of this bacterial enzyme occurs in three steps, with some of the intermediates presumably remaining enzyme-bound: (1) NAD(+)-dependent dehydrogenation of either putrescine or spermidine. (2) Attack by water forming 4-aminobutanal (and releasing ammonia or propane-1,3-diamine, respectively). (3) Condensation of 4-aminobutanal with putrescine, which forms homospermidine and restores NAD(+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Differs from the eukaryotic enzyme EC 2.5.1.45, which cannot use putrescine as donor of the aminobutyl group.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/437275"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8407874"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26776105"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.44#SIP90FCA8DAF0D73F6D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 putrescine = NH4(+) + sym-homospermidine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.44#SIPC8A362AC2000B3D3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>putrescine + spermidine = propane-1,3-diamine + sym-homospermidine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/437275">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/437275"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/437275"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8407874">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8407874"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8407874"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26776105">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26776105"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26776105"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.45">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>homospermidine synthase (spermidine-specific)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.45#SIPC8A362AC2000B3D3"/>
<rdfs:comment>A eukaryotic enzyme found in plants.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction occurs in three steps, with some of the intermediates presumably remaining enzyme-bound: (1) NAD(+)-dependent dehydrogenation of spermidine to dehydrospermidine. (2) Attack by water forming 4-aminobutanal (and releasing propane-1,3-diamine). (3) Condensation of 4-aminobutanal with purescine, which forms homospermidine and restores NAD(+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is more specific than EC 2.5.1.44, which is found in bacteria, as it cannot use putrescine as donor of the 4-aminobutyl group.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Forms part of the biosynthetic pathway of the poisonous pyrrolizidine alkaloids of the ragworts (Senecio).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10611289"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11117877"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.45#SIPC8A362AC2000B3D3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>putrescine + spermidine = propane-1,3-diamine + sym-homospermidine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
