<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.46">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.1.1.249"/>
<skos:prefLabel>deoxyhypusine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(4-aminobutyl)lysine synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>[eIF-5A]-deoxyhypusine synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>spermidine dehydrogenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.46#SIP27C5227A978CE143"/>
<rdfs:comment>The eukaryotic initiation factor eIF5A contains a hypusine residue that is essential for activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the first reaction of hypusine formation from one specific lysine residue of the eIF5A precursor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction occurs in four steps: NAD(+)-dependent dehydrogenation of spermidine (1a), formation of an enzyme-imine intermediate by transfer of the 4-aminobutylidene group from dehydrospermidine to the active site lysine residue (1b), transfer of the same 4-aminobutylidene group from the enzyme intermediate to the e1F5A precursor (1c), reduction of the e1F5A-imine intermediate to form a deoxyhypusine residue (1d).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Hence the overall reaction is transfer of a 4-aminobutyl group.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>For the plant enzyme, homospermidine can substitute for spermidine and putrescine can substitute for the lysine residue of the eIF5A precursor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Hypusine is formed from deoxyhypusine by the action of EC 1.14.99.29.</rdfs:comment>
