<skos:prefLabel>1,4-dihydroxy-2-naphthoate polyprenyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIP1D070E0A80F3E4AF"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIPD72403868124C578"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIP45DF989D711DBBEA"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIP2CB6EC1869AC2EB2"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIPBDCF972958BD8D2F"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIP1FBE56353520CBFF"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIP938BB8FBCC473DDD"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIP8DB977CE6C361630"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.74#SIP0CF69BB6B50BCE70"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes a step in the synthesis of menaquinone, in which the prenyl chain synthesized by polyprenyl diphosphate synthase is transferred to 1,4-dihydroxy-2-naphthoate (DHNA).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The bacterial enzyme is an inner membrane protein, with the C-terminus located in the periplasm.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is highly specific for DHNA but not for a specific length of the prenyl chain.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/949474"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7275947"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9573170"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15919996"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.74#SIP1D070E0A80F3E4AF">
