<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.141">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>heme o synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.141#SIP08FD51CEB66EF9E3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in many archaea, bacteria, and eukaryotes, produces heme o, which in many cases is further modified into heme a.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In organisms that produce heme a, the enzyme forms a complex with heme a synthase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In some archaeal species the enzyme transfers a geranylgeranyl group instead of a farnesyl group.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1336371"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7968515"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8063781"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8078902"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15491161"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19204012"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.141#SIP08FD51CEB66EF9E3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H2O + heme b = diphosphate + Fe(II)-heme o.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
