</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.144">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>S-sulfo-L-cysteine synthase (O-acetyl-L-serine-dependent)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cysteine synthase B</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.5.1.144#SIP9DC6D16A7B5F9666"/>
<rdfs:comment>In plants, the activity is catalyzed by a chloroplastic enzyme that plays an important role in chloroplast function and is essential for light-dependent redox regulation within the chloroplast.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The bacterial enzyme also catalyzes the activity of EC 2.5.1.47. cf. EC 2.8.5.1.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6373737"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6615127"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20179139"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22829322"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23333972"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.5.1.144#SIP9DC6D16A7B5F9666">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>O-acetyl-L-serine + thiosulfate = acetate + H(+) + S-sulfo-L-cysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
