<skos:altLabel>D-alanine aminotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-alanine-D-glutamate transaminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-alanine transaminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-amino acid aminotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-amino acid transaminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-aspartate aminotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-aspartate transaminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-aspartic aminotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.21#SIPA07EDC5EEC24C3B4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from thermophilic Bacillus species acts on many D-amino acids with D-alanine and D-2-aminobutyrate as the best amino donors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can similarly use any of several 2-oxo acids as amino acceptor, with 2-oxoglutarate and 2-oxobutyrate among the best.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from some other sources has a broader specificity.</rdfs:comment>
