<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.77">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>taurine--pyruvate aminotransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.77#SIPA2F148DA41D9363C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.77#SIPAB44EFFE6F0D617B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Bilophila wadsworthia catalyzes a reversible reaction that starts an anaerobic taurine degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>beta-alanine is also a significant amino group donor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas denitrificans PD1222 can also use hypotaurine, producing 2-sulfinoacetaldehyde, which spontaneously hydrolyzes to sulfite and acetaldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 2.6.1.55, 2-oxoglutarate cannot serve as an acceptor for the amino group.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11082195"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11728723"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12471498"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23603744"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.77#SIPA2F148DA41D9363C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>pyruvate + taurine = L-alanine + sulfoacetaldehyde.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.77#SIPAB44EFFE6F0D617B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>hypotaurine + pyruvate = 2-sulfinoacetaldehyde + L-alanine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
