<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.86">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-amino-4-deoxychorismate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-amino-2-deoxyisochorismate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ADIC synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.86#SIP654195836E3BE071"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction occurs in the reverse direction to that shown above.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In contrast to most anthranilate-synthase I (ASI) homologs, this enzyme is not inhibited by tryptophan.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Streptomyces globisporus, the sequential action of this enzyme and EC 1.3.99.24, 2-amino-4-deoxychorismate dehydrogenase, leads to the formation of the benzoxazolinate moiety of the enediyne antitumor antibiotic C-1027.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In certain Pseudomonads the enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of phenazine, a precursor for several compounds with antibiotic activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11562236"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15008629"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18182490"/>
