<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.97">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>archaeosine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.97#SIPA07BA8A4356D5D29"/>
<rdfs:comment>In Euryarchaeota the reaction is catalyzed by ArcS.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Crenarchaeota, which do not have an ArcS homolog, the reaction is catalyzed either by a homolog of EC 6.3.4.20 that includes a glutaminase domain (cf. EC 3.5.1.2), or by a homolog of EC 1.7.1.13.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the Euryarchaeon Methanocaldococcus jannaschii can also use arginine and ammonium as amino donors.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20129918"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22032275"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.97#SIPA07BA8A4356D5D29">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>7-cyano-7-carbaguanosine(15) in tRNA + H2O + L-glutamine = archaeosine(15) in tRNA + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20129918">
