<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/23586652"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23586652"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.105">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.6.1.n2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>lysine--8-amino-7-oxononanoate transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DAPA aminotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.105#SIPF4F7DFAA8B01D39D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Participates in the pathway for biotin biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Bacillus subtilis cannot use S-adenosyl-L-methionine as amino donor and catalyzes an alternative reaction for the conversion of 8-amino-7-oxononanoate to 7,8-diaminononanoate (cf. EC 2.6.1.62).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15880481"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20565114"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.105#SIPF4F7DFAA8B01D39D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(8S)-8-amino-7-oxononanoate + L-lysine = (7R,8S)-7,8-diammoniononanoate + (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15880481">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/15880481"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15880481"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20565114">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20565114"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20565114"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.106">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dTDP-3-amino-3,4,6-trideoxy-alpha-D-glucose transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.106#SIP98FD5310A993BBC3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of dTDP-alpha-D-desosamine, a sugar found in several bacterial macrolide antibiotics including erythromycin, megalomicin A, mycinamicin II, and oleandomycin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction occurs in the reverse direction.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17456741"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.106#SIP98FD5310A993BBC3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-oxoglutarate + dTDP-3-amino-3,4,6-trideoxy-alpha-D-glucose = dTDP-3-dehydro-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucose + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17456741">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17456741"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17456741"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.107">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>beta-methylphenylalanine transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.107#SIPF78991BE8BAAB7E3"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces hygroscopicus NRRL3085.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is involved in the biosynthesis of the glycopeptide antibiotic mannopeptimycin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19731276"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.107#SIPF78991BE8BAAB7E3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2S,3S)-3-methylphenylalanine + 2-oxoglutarate = (3S)-2-oxo-3-phenylbutanoate + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19731276">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19731276"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19731276"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.108">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(5-formylfuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>[5-(hydroxymethyl)furan-3-yl]methyl phosphate transaminase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.108#SIPB6DDC172DAE09E80"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the archaebacterium Methanocaldococcus jannaschii, participates in the biosynthesis of the cofactor methanofuran.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24977328"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.108#SIPB6DDC172DAE09E80">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4-(hydroxymethyl)-2-furancarboxaldehyde phosphate + L-alanine = [5-(aminomethyl)-3-furyl]methyl phosphate + pyruvate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24977328">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/24977328"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24977328"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.109">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>8-amino-3,8-dideoxy-alpha-D-manno-octulosonate transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.109#SIPBAC5CCC48ABF5FB2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Shewanella oneidensis, forms 8-amino-3,8-dideoxy-alpha-D-manno-octulosonate, an aminated form of Kdo found in lipopolysaccharides of members of the Shewanella genus. cf. EC 1.1.3.48.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23413030"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.109#SIPBAC5CCC48ABF5FB2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-oxoglutarate + 8-amino-3,8-dideoxy-alpha-D-manno-octulosonate = 3,8-dideoxy-8-oxo-alpha-D-manno-octulosonate + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23413030">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/23413030"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23413030"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1074/jbc.m113.453324</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.110">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dTDP-4-dehydro-2,3,6-trideoxy-D-glucose 4-aminotransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TDP-4-keto-2,3,6-trideoxy-D-glucose 4-aminotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.110#SIP03BEB711C2F1F234"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Saccharopolyspora spinosa, participates in the biosynthesis of forosamine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18345667"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.110#SIP03BEB711C2F1F234">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-oxoglutarate + dTDP-4-amino-2,3,4,6-tetradeoxy-alpha-D-erythro-hexopyranose = dTDP-4-dehydro-2,3,6-trideoxy-alpha-D-hexopyranose + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18345667">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/18345667"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18345667"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.111">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-aminobutanoyl-CoA transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acyl-CoA beta-transaminase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.111#SIP140FEBB4E6A18550"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in bacteria, is part of a L-lysine degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is also active with other beta-amino compounds such as 3-amino-5-methylhexanoyl-CoA and 3-amino-3-phenylpropanoyl-CoA.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21826218"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.111#SIP140FEBB4E6A18550">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(3S)-3-aminobutanoyl-CoA + 2-oxoglutarate = acetoacetyl-CoA + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21826218">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21826218"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21826218"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.112">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(S)-ureidoglycine--glyoxylate transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(S)-ureidoglycine--glyoxylate aminotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UGXT</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.112#SIPECBB9ECB7DD827AF"/>
<rdfs:comment>The protein, found in bacteria, can use other amino-group acceptors, but is specific for (S)-ureidoglycine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20852637"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.112#SIPECBB9ECB7DD827AF">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(S)-2-ureidoglycine + glyoxylate = glycine + N-carbamoyl-2-oxoglycine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20852637">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20852637"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20852637"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.113">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>putrescine--pyruvate transaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.113#SIP2D116448ECA33FBE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, studied in the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa, participates in a putrescine degradation pathway. cf. EC 2.6.1.82.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12081945"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.113#SIP2D116448ECA33FBE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>putrescine + pyruvate = 4-aminobutanal + L-alanine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12081945">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/12081945"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12081945"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1128/jb.184.14.3765-3773.2002</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.114">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>8-demethyl-8-aminoriboflavin-5'-phosphate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.114#SIP71676A3F9B7FD8FF"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces davawensis, has the activities of an oxidoreductase, a decarboxylase, and an aminotransferase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Its combined actions result in the replacement of a methyl substituent of one of the aromatic rings of FMN by an amino group, a step in the biosynthetic pathway of roseoflavin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction requires thiamine for completion.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27062037"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27331868"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27981706"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.114#SIP71676A3F9B7FD8FF">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3 A + FMN + H2O + L-glutamate + O2 = 2-oxoglutarate + 8-amino-8-demethylriboflavin 5'-phosphate + 3 AH2 + CO2 + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27062037">
