<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31455636"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1074/jbc.ra119.010406</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.121">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>8-amino-7-oxononanoate carboxylating dehydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.121#SIP54936B3B51D18CC3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which participates in biotin biosynthesis, is found in haloarchaea and some cyanobacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It forms a conjugant between (7R,8S)-8-amino-7-oxononanoate and an internal lysine residue and catalyzes multiple reactions, including a reduction, a carboxylation of the epsilon-amino group of the lysine residue, and an oxidative cleavage of the conjugate to release (7R,8S)-8-amino-7-(carboxyamino)nonanoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>During this process the lysine residue serves as an amino donor and is converted to (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate, resulting in inactivation of the enzyme following a single turnover. cf. EC 2.6.1.105.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/32042199"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.121#SIP54936B3B51D18CC3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(8S)-8-amino-7-oxononanoate + CO2 + L-lysyl-[protein] = (7R,8S)-8-amino-7-(carboxyamino)nonanoate + (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoyl-[protein] + 2 H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/32042199">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/32042199"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32042199"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41589-019-0461-9</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.122">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>UDP-N-acetyl-3-dehydro-alpha-D-glucosamine 3-aminotranferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.122#SIP4FB9A2B1471A3CDD"/>
<rdfs:comment>This bacterial enzyme participates, together with EC 1.1.1.374, in the synthesis of 2,3-diamino-2,3-dideoxy-D-glucopyranose, a component of lipid A in some species.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15044494"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.122#SIP4FB9A2B1471A3CDD">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-oxoglutarate + UDP-2-acetamido-3-amino-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranose = L-glutamate + UDP-2-acetamido-3-dehydro-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15044494">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/15044494"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15044494"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1074/jbc.m400596200</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.123">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>4-amino-4-deoxychorismate synthase (2-amino-4-deoxychorismate-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ADCS</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ADC synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.6.1.123#SIP36D2FC9F4DB40111"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacillus subtilis, is a heterodimer.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The PabA subunit acts successively on two molecules of L-glutamine, hydrolyzing each to L-glutamate and ammonia (cf. EC 3.5.1.2, glutaminase).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The ammonia molecules are channeled to the active site of PabB, which catalyzes the formation of 4-amino-4-deoxychorismate from chorismate in two steps, via the intermediate 2-amino-4-deoxychorismate. cf. EC 2.6.1.85.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19275258"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23230967"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.6.1.123#SIP36D2FC9F4DB40111">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>chorismate + H2O + 2 L-glutamine = 4-amino-4-deoxychorismate + 2 L-glutamate + NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19275258">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19275258"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19275258"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1021/ja809283u</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
