</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.26">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>riboflavin kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>flavokinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RFK</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.26#SIPDAE30F846972BD80"/>
<rdfs:comment>The cofactors FMN and FAD participate in numerous processes in all organisms, including mitochondrial electron transport, photosynthesis, fatty-acid oxidation, and metabolism of vitamin B6, vitamin B12 and folates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While monofunctional riboflavin kinase is found in eukaryotes, some bacteria have a bifunctional enzyme that exhibits both this activity and that of EC 2.7.7.2.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Bacillus subtilis, ATP can be replaced by other phosphate donors but with decreasing enzyme activity in the order ATP > dATP > CTP > UTP.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10206712"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12693963"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13584303"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14284745"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14927668"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16183635"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
