<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.48">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>uridine/cytidine kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>uridine-cytidine kinase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.48#SIP7AC2253BCF666AAB"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.48#SIPA946DBCB374D0F15"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.48#SIPB5A2E691965F50C3"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.48#SIPBA31FBE7442B5C21"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in prokaryotes and eukaryotes, phosphorylates both uridine and cytidine to their monophosphate forms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Escherichia coli prefers GTP to ATP.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human enzyme also catalyzes the phosphorylation of several cytotoxic ribonucleoside analogs. cf. EC 2.7.1.213.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/211379"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5782006"/>
