<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.158">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>inositol-pentakisphosphate 2-kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>inositol 1,3,4,5,6-pentakisphosphate 2-kinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>inositol polyphosphate kinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Ins(1,3,4,5,6)P5 2-kinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>IP5 2-kinase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.158#SIP5F89C4AF944909E3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also use Ins(1,4,5,6)P4 and Ins(1,4,5)P3 as substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Inositol hexakisphosphate (phytate) accumulates in storage protein bodies during seed development and, when hydrolyzed, releases stored nutrients to the developing seedling before the plant is capable of absorbing nutrients from its environment.</rdfs:comment>
