<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.225#SIPBC24AA0DA554C311"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Staphylococcus aureus, is involved in the biosynthesis of L-2,3-diaminopropanoate, which is used by that organism as a precursor for the biosynthesis of the siderophore staphyloferrin B.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29483190"/>
