<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.227">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>inositol phosphorylceramide synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.227#SIP8460F38B517F78EE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from yeast, attaches a phosphoinositol headgroup to alpha-hydroxyphytoceramides, generating a very-long-chain inositol phospho-alpha hydroxyphytoceramide (IPC), the simplest of the three complex sphingolipids produced by yeast.</rdfs:comment>
