<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.234">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>D-tagatose-1-phosphate kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.234#SIP6CCC772B74E96742"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which has been purified from the bacteria Klebsiella oxytoca and Bacillus licheniformis, is part of a D-tagatose catabolic pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrate, which occurs in a pyranose form in solution, undergoes a change to the furanose conformation after binding to the enzyme, in order to permit phosphorylation at C-6.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15257457"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23524682"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26159072"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.234#SIP6CCC772B74E96742">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>alpha-D-tagatopyranose 1-phosphate + ATP = ADP + D-tagatofuranose 1,6-bisphosphate + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
