<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.238">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phenol phosphorylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phenylphosphate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.1.238#SIPB67A225CA8F4F243"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Thauera aromatica, catalyzes the first step in an anaerobic phenol degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, composed of three subunits, transfers the beta-phosphoryl from ATP to phenol, forming phenyl phosphate, AMP, and phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>During catalysis a diphosphoryl group is transferred from ATP to a histidine residue in one of the enzyme's subunits, from which phosphate is cleaved to render the reaction unidirectional.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The remaining histidine phosphate subsequently serves as the actual phosphorylation agent.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15547277"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16980461"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.1.238#SIPB67A225CA8F4F243">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + H2O + phenol = AMP + 2 H(+) + phenyl phosphate + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
