<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.2.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acetate kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acetate kinase (phosphorylating)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acetic kinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acetokinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>AK</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.2.1#SIPED8CCF57889088BB"/>
<rdfs:comment>While purified enzyme from Escherichia coli is specific for acetate, others have found that the enzyme can also use propanoate as a substrate, but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Acetate can be converted into the key metabolic intermediate acetyl-CoA by coupling acetate kinase with EC 2.3.1.8.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Both this enzyme and EC 2.7.2.15 play important roles in the production of propanoate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3020034"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6956338"/>
