<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.4.34">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>GDP-polyphosphate phosphotransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>polyphosphate kinase 2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.4.34#SIPEBBFD446081CEC83"/>
<rdfs:comment>Polyphosphate kinase 2, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa, uses inorganic polyphosphate as a donor to convert GDP to GTP.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also act on ADP (cf. EC 2.7.4.1), but with lower activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme has only a trivial activity in the opposite direction (synthesizing polyphosphate from GTP).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The GTP that is produced is believed to be consumed by EC 2.7.7.13.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12482933"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12486232"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.4.34#SIPEBBFD446081CEC83">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>[phosphate](n) + GTP = [phosphate](n+1) + GDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
