<skos:altLabel>UDP-N-acetylglucosamine pyrophosphorylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.23#SIPC9758E31A0D86E2E"/>
<rdfs:comment>Part of the pathway for acetamido sugar biosynthesis in bacteria and archaea.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from several bacteria (e.g., Escherichia coli, Bacillus subtilis and Haemophilus influenzae) has been shown to be bifunctional and also to possess the activity of EC 2.3.1.157.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from plants and animals is also active toward N-acetyl-alpha-D-galactosamine 1-phosphate (cf. EC 2.7.7.83), while the bacterial enzyme shows low activity toward that substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8083170"/>
