<skos:prefLabel>gentamicin 2''-nucleotidyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2''-aminoglycoside nucleotidyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.46#SIPDAB66EBB7B48A08F"/>
<rdfs:comment>ATP, dATP, CTP, ITP and GTP can act as donors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Kanamycin, tobramycin and sisomicin can also act as acceptors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The nucleotidyl residue is transferred to the 2-hydroxy group of the 3-amino-3-deoxy-D-glucose moiety in the antibiotic.</rdfs:comment>
