<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.65">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>diguanylate cyclase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DGC</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.65#SIP2CC6140EF58F4829"/>
<rdfs:comment>Can be activated by BeF3, a phosphoryl mimic, which results in dimerization.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Dimerization is required but is not sufficient for diguanylate-cyclase activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Cyclic di-3',5'-guanylate is an intracellular signaling molecule that controls motility and adhesion in bacterial cells; it was first identified as having a positive allosteric effect on EC 2.4.1.12.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15716451"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16418169"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17640875"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.7.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.7.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
