<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.66">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>malonate decarboxylase holo-[acyl-carrier protein] synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>holo ACP synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>holo-malonate-decarboxylase synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.66#SIPA3D22491925DC128"/>
<rdfs:comment>The delta subunit of malonate decarboxylase serves as an an acyl-carrier protein (ACP) and contains the cofactor 2'-(5-triphosphoribosyl)-3'-dephospho-CoA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Two reactions are involved in the production of the holo-ACP form of this enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The first reaction is catalyzed by EC 2.4.2.52.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The resulting prosthetic group is then attached to the ACP subunit via a phosphodiester linkage to a serine residue, thus forming the holo form of the enzyme, in a manner analogous to that of EC 2.7.7.61.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11052675"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11052676"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.7.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.7.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.66#SIPA3D22491925DC128">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2'-(5''-triphospho-alpha-D-ribosyl)-3'-dephospho-CoA + apo-[malonate decarboxylase ACP] = diphosphate + holo-[malonate decarboxylase ACP].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
