<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.79">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tRNA(His) guanylyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>histidine tRNA guanylyltransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.79#SIPE03E0F74CA324105"/>
<rdfs:comment>In eukarya an additional guanosine residue is added post-transcriptionally to the 5'-end of tRNA(His) molecules.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The addition occurs opposite a universally conserved adenosine(73) and is thus the result of a non-templated 3'-5' addition reaction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The additional guanosine residue is an important determinant for aminoacylation by EC 6.1.1.21.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme requires a divalent cation for activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>ATP activation is not required when the substrate contains a 5'-triphosphate (ppp-tRNA(His)).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1660461"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1660462"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14633974"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18366186"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20660484"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21059936"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.7.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.7.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.79#SIPE03E0F74CA324105">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 5'-end ribonucleotide-tRNA(His) + ATP + GTP + H2O = a 5'-end phospho-guanosine-ribonucleotide-tRNA(His) + AMP + 2 diphosphate + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
