<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.84">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2'-5' oligoadenylate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.84#SIPCCA296B64396D372"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is activated by binding to double-stranded RNA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The resulting product binds to and activates RNase L, which subsequently degrades the RNA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Oligoadenylates of chain lengths 2, 4 and 5 are also produced.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The dimer does not have any known biological activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/272640"/>
