<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.85">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>diadenylate cyclase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cyclic-di-AMP synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.85#SIP27D487F6FB17353B"/>
<rdfs:comment>Cyclic di-3',5'-adenylate is a bioactive molecule produced by some bacteria and archaea, which may function as a secondary signaling molecule.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The intracellular bacterial pathogen Listeria monocytogenes secretes it into the host's cytosol, where it triggers a cytosolic pathway of innate immunity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18439896"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20508090"/>
