<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.7.92">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-nononate cytidylyltransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.7.92#SIP8060B77ECA1DEDB3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is part of the biosynthesis pathway of the sialic acid 3-deoxy-D-glycero-beta-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate (Kdn).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Kdn is abundant in extracellular glycoconjugates of lower vertebrates such as fish and amphibians, but is also found in the capsular polysaccharides of bacteria that belong to the Bacteroides genus.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8381411"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8665905"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11479279"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17580313"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18804026"/>
