<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.8.48">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.7.8.n3"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ceramide phosphoethanolamine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CPE synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.8.48#SIP6B4A597277822D3E"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.8.48#SIP4A8AFA186E7D8AB7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, studied from the fly Drosophila melanogaster, has homologs among the invertebrates, but not in other animal phyla.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Its product, ceramide phosphoethanolamine, is synthesized as the main sphingolipid in cell membranes of arthropods, such as Drosophila and Musca, and is common in worms, bees, spiders, and scorpions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has also been reported in deep-sea mussels and some sea snails, as well as protozoans and oomycetes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme requires a Mn(II) cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19506037"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23449981"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.8.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.8.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.8.48#SIP6B4A597277822D3E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an N-acyl-sphingoid base + CDP-ethanolamine = an N-acyl-sphingoid 1-phosphoethanolamine + CMP + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.8.48#SIP4A8AFA186E7D8AB7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an N-acylsphing-4-enine + CDP-ethanolamine = an N-acylsphing-4-enine 1-phosphoethanolamine + CMP + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
