<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.9.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>rifampicin phosphotransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.9.6#SIP3750773BB9632DA7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from a diverse collection of Gram-positive bacteria, inactivates the antibiotic rifampicin by phosphorylating it at position 21.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme comprises three domains: two substrate-binding domains (ATP-grasp and rifampicin-binding domains) and a smaller phosphate-carrying L-histidine swivel domain that transits between the spatially distinct substrate-binding sites during catalysis.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24778229"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27103605"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.9.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.9.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
