<skos:altLabel>myosin II heavy-chain kinase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.11.7#SIP3344522272AE36F2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Dictyostelium sp. (slime molds) brings about phosphorylation of the heavy chains of Dictyostelium myosin, inhibiting the actin-activated ATPase activity of the myosin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>One threonine residue in each heavy chain acts as acceptor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While the enzyme from some species is activated by actin, in other cases Ca(2+)/calmodulin are required for activity.</rdfs:comment>
