<activity rdf:resource="2.7.11.9#SIP70AE06AAE29D99B0"/>
<rdfs:comment>This serine/threonine kinase specifically binds to and phosphorylates the N-terminal region of the human Goodpasture antigen, which is located on the alpha3 chain of collagen IV and is involved in autoimmune disease.</rdfs:comment>
