<skos:prefLabel>cGMP-dependent protein kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3':5'-cyclic GMP-dependent protein kinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cGMP-dependent protein kinase Ibeta</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>guanosine 3':5'-cyclic monophosphate-dependent protein kinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PKG</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PKG 1alpha</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PKG 1beta</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PKG II</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.11.12#SIPABF32A1AD40E58B2"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.11.12#SIP81BD4F43BC20BF5F"/>
<rdfs:comment>cGMP is required to activate this enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme occurs as a dimer in higher eukaryotes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The C-terminal region of each polypeptide chain contains the catalytic domain that includes the ATP and protein substrate binding sites.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This domain catalyzes the phosphorylation by ATP to specific serine or threonine residues in protein substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also has two allosteric cGMP-binding sites (sites A and B).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Binding of cGMP causes a conformational change that is associated with activation of the kinase.</rdfs:comment>
