<rdfs:comment>Activated by AMP.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>EC 1.1.1.34 is inactivated by the phosphorylation of the enzyme protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Histones can also act as acceptors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Can also phosphorylate EC 6.4.1.2 and EC 3.1.1.79.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Thr-172 within the catalytic subunit (alpha-subunit) is the major site phosphorylated by the AMP-activated protein kinase kinase.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>GTP can act instead of ATP.</rdfs:comment>
