<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.11.33">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.7.11.n2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[pyruvate, water dikinase] kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PEPS kinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PSRP</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.11.33#SIPD622F9591A7D8430"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli is bifunctional and catalyzes both the phosphorylation and dephosphorylation of EC 2.7.9.2; cf. EC 2.7.4.28.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is specific for a reaction intermediate form of EC 2.7.9.2, where it phosphorylates an active site histidine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has no activity toward EC 2.7.9.1, (cf. EC 2.7.11.32).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20044937"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.7.11.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.7.11.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
