</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.7.11.34">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>NEK6-subfamily protein kinase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.11.34#SIPABF32A1AD40E58B2"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.7.11.34#SIP81BD4F43BC20BF5F"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires Mg(2+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>NEK6 subfamily kinases are present in animals, though lost in insects, and include human NEK6 and NEK7 and C. elegans nekl-3.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They are activated in mitosis by phosphorylation by NEK9, and phosphorylate cytoskeletal proteins including EML4, KIF11A and KIF14. In C. elegans, nekl-3 is involved in clathrin-mediated endocytosis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In peptide arrays, NEK6 prefers to phosphorylate Ser residues, with hydrophobic residues at -2 and +1 and charged residues at -1, -2 and +2.</rdfs:comment>
