<skos:altLabel>thiosulfate cyanide transsulfurase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>thiosulfate thiotransferase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.8.1.1#SIP8717130C02E5CF5B"/>
<rdfs:comment>A few other sulfur compounds can act as donors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.8.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.8.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.8.1.1#SIP8717130C02E5CF5B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>hydrogen cyanide + thiosulfate = 2 H(+) + sulfite + thiocyanate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.8.1.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-mercaptopyruvate sulfurtransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.8.1.2#SIP30930E9B6F245865"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes a transsulfuration reaction from 3-mercaptopyruvate to an internal cysteine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the presence of a dithiol such as reduced thioredoxin or dihydrolipoate, the sulfanyl sulfur is released as hydrogen sulfide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in a sulfur relay process that leads to the 2-thiolation of some tRNAs and to protein urmylation by transferring sulfur between the NFS1 cysteine desulfurase (EC 2.8.1.7) and the MOCS3 sulfurtransferase (EC 2.8.1.11).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4550801"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6026243"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13367011"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13436433"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13673028"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16107337"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18855522"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21732914"/>
