<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.8.1.11">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.8.1.n1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>molybdopterin synthase sulfurtransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>molybdopterin synthase sulfurylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.8.1.11#SIP4085D8FC94DD633D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme transfers sulfur to form a thiocarboxylate moiety on the C-terminal glycine of the small subunit of EC 2.8.1.12.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the human, the reaction is catalyzed by the rhodanese-like C-terminal domain (cf. EC 2.8.1.1) of the MOCS3 protein, a bifunctional protein that also contains EC 2.7.7.80 at the N-terminal domain.</rdfs:comment>
