</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.8.5.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-cysteine S-thiosulfotransferase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="2.8.5.2#SIP1B251D9BDED9D1E3"/>
<activity rdf:resource="2.8.5.2#SIP5199E1AD3A42B998"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is part of the Sox enzyme system, which participates in a bacterial thiosulfate oxidation pathway that produces sulfate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes two reactions in the pathway - early in the pathway it attaches a thiosulfate molecule to the sulfur atom of an L-cysteine of a SoxY protein; later it transfers a second thiosulfate molecule to a sulfane group that is already attached to the same cysteine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10940005"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11523998"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12147345"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12411478"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16297640"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16995898"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28257465"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="2.8.5.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="2.8.5.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.8.5.2#SIP1B251D9BDED9D1E3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome c] + L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein] + thiosulfate = 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] + 2 H(+) + S-sulfosulfanyl-L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="2.8.5.2#SIP5199E1AD3A42B998">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome c] + S-sulfanyl-L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein] + thiosulfate = 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] + 2 H(+) + S-(2-sulfodisulfanyl)-L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
