<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.2#SIP711031E8364F523D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Acts on many phenolic esters.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is likely that the three forms of human paraoxonase are lactonases rather than aromatic esterases.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The natural substrates of the paraoxonases are lactones, with (+-)-5-hydroxy-6E,8Z,11Z,4Z-eicostetraenoic-acid 1,5-lactone being the best substrate.</rdfs:comment>
