<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.67">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>fatty-acyl-ethyl-ester synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>FAEES</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>FAEE synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.67#SIPB06026C6BAB847AD"/>
<rdfs:comment>In the reverse reaction, forms ethyl esters from fatty acids and ethanol in the absence of coenzyme A or ATP.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Best substrates are unsaturated octadecanoic acids; palmitate, stearate and arachidonate also act, more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6487591"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
