</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.73">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>feruloyl esterase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cinnamoyl ester hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ferulic acid esterase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>hydroxycinnamoyl esterase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.73#SIP4954B8B51609CEE8"/>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the hydrolysis of the 4-hydroxy-3-methoxycinnamoyl (feruloyl) group from an esterified sugar, which is usually arabinose in 'natural' substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>p-Nitrophenol acetate and methyl ferulate are poorer substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>All microbial ferulate esterases are secreted into the culture medium.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They are sometimes called hemicellulase accessory enzymes, since they help xylanases and pectinases to break down plant cell wall hemicellulose.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1663152"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8679110"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9406381"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.73#SIP4954B8B51609CEE8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>feruloyl-polysaccharide + H2O = ferulate + polysaccharide.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
