<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.74">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cutinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cutin hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.74#SIP2F9BF15CC2D55EE1"/>
<rdfs:comment>Cutin, a polymeric structural component of plant cuticles, is an hydroxy fatty acid polymer, usually C16 or C18 and that contains one to three hydroxyl groups.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from several fungal sources also hydrolyzes the p-nitrophenyl esters of hexadecanoic acid.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is however inactive toward several esters that are substrates for non-specific esterases.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/239740"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1156575"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9281862"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.74#SIP2F9BF15CC2D55EE1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>cutin + H2O = cutin monomers.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
