<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.85">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>pimeloyl-[acyl-carrier protein] methyl ester esterase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.85#SIPA6A572A02E9046D0"/>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in biotin biosynthesis in Gram-negative bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme exhibits carboxylesterase activity, particularly toward substrates with short acyl chains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Even though the enzyme can interact with coenzyme A thioesters, the in vivo role of the enzyme is to hydrolyze the methyl ester of pimeloyl-[acyl carrier protein], terminating the part of the biotin biosynthesis pathway that is catalyzed by the fatty acid elongation enzymes.</rdfs:comment>
