</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.106">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>O-acetyl-ADP-ribose deacetylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.106#SIPB4353E8B28521B6A"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.106#SIPCD6B5A3748A45BED"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli and from human cells, removes the acetyl group from either the 2'' or 3'' position of O-acetyl-ADP-ribose, which are formed by the action of EC 2.3.1.286.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human enzyme can also remove ADP-D-ribose from phosphorylated double stranded DNA adducts.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21257746"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26481419"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29410655"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.106#SIPB4353E8B28521B6A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3''-O-acetyl-ADP-D-ribose + H2O = acetate + ADP-D-ribose + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.106#SIPCD6B5A3748A45BED">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2''-O-acetyl-ADP-D-ribose + H2O = acetate + ADP-D-ribose + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
