<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/26481419"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26481419"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29410655">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/29410655"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29410655"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.107">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>apo-salmochelin esterase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.107#SIPC815215D9AEE2E78"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.107#SIPBCC19EFBF89CDBF3"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.107#SIPF30C7779C5E6A284"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.107#SIP408B11117B55F078"/>
<rdfs:comment>This bacterial enzyme is present in pathogenic Salmonella species, uropathogenic and avian pathogenic Escherichia coli strains, and certain Klebsiella strains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 3.1.1.108, which acts only on enterobactin, this enzyme can also act on the C-glucosylated forms known as salmochelins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 3.1.1.109, (IroD), IroE prefers apo siderophores as substrates, and is assumed to act before the siderophores are exported out of the cell.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It hydrolyzes the trilactone only once, producing linearized trimers.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16076215"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.107#SIPC815215D9AEE2E78">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>enterobactin + H2O = N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine trimer.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.107#SIPBCC19EFBF89CDBF3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + triglucosyl-enterobactin = [N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]3 + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.107#SIPF30C7779C5E6A284">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>diglucosyl-enterobactin + H2O = H(+) + N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl-[N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.107#SIP408B11117B55F078">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + monoglucosyl-enterobactin = [N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl]2-N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16076215">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/16076215"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16076215"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.108">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>iron(III) enterobactin esterase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.1.108#SIP247C102FBD659E74"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Escherichia coli, allows the bacterium to grow in limited iron conditions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also act on enterobactin (with no complexed iron) and the aluminum(III) analog of iron(III) enterobactin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The trimer formed is further hydrolyzed to form the dimer and the monomer.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/150859"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1534808"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3040679"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4330269"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8148617"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30086222"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.1.108#SIP247C102FBD659E74">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Fe(III)-enterobactin + H(+) + 3 H2O = Fe(III)-[N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine] + 2 N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
