<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.4#SIP8A06B8A82CB5F582"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.4#SIP930CCC34041D3CD6"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the Mg(2+)-dependent dephosphorylation of a 1,2-diacylglycerol-3-phosphate, yielding a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol (DAG), the substrate for de novo lipid synthesis via the Kennedy pathway and for the synthesis of triacylglycerol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In lipid signaling, the enzyme generates a pool of DAG to be used for protein kinase C activation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The mammalian enzymes are known as lipins.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3475370"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18812320"/>
