<skos:altLabel>sucrose phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.24#SIP853125915354050C"/>
<rdfs:comment>This is the final step in the sucrose-biosynthesis pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Highly specific for sucrose 6-phosphate, with fructose 6-phosphate unable to act as a substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The F in sucrose 6(F)-phosphate is used to indicate that the fructose residue of sucrose carries the substituent.</rdfs:comment>
