<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.3.36">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phosphoinositide 5-phosphatase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>diphosphoinositide phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>inositol 1,4,5-triphosphate 5-phosphomonoesterase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>inositol triphosphate 5-phosphomonoesterase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>IP3 phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphatidylinositol-bisphosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphatidyl-inositol-bisphosphate phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphatidyl-myo-inositol-4,5-bisphosphate phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>polyphosphoinositol lipid 5-phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PtdIns(4,5)P2 phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>triphosphoinositide phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>triphosphoinositide phosphomonoesterase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>type II inositol-1,4,5-trisphosphate 5-phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>type II inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.36#SIP8BDA8632B4A0865E"/>
<rdfs:comment>These enzymes can also remove the 5-phosphate from Ins(1,4,5)P3 and/or Ins(1,3,4,5)P4.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They are a diverse family of enzymes, with differing abilities to catalyze two or more of the four reactions listed.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They are thought to use inositol lipids rather than inositol phosphates as substrates in vivo.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>All of them can use either or both of PtdIns(4,5)P2 and PtdIns(3,4,5)P3 as substrates; this is the main property that distinguishes them from EC 3.1.3.56.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4284485"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6271223"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
