<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.3.71">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-phosphosulfolactate phosphatase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(2R)-phosphosulfolactate phosphohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ComB phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.71#SIPFBE9D9AFE8E8D8AB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Methanococcus jannaschii acts on both stereoisoimers of the substrate and also hydrolyzes a number of phosphate monoesters of (S)-2-hydroxycarboxylic acids, including 2-phosphomalate, 2-phospholactate and 2-phosphoglycolate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme can also hydrolyze phosphate monoesters of (R)-2-hydroxycarboxylic acids such as (S)-2-phospho-3-sulfolactate and (R)-2-phosphomalate, which, presumably, bind to the enzyme in opposite orientations.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11589710"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
