<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.3.74">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>pyridoxal phosphatase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PLP phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PNP phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>vitamin B6 (pyridoxine) phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>vitamin B6-phosphate phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.74#SIP82F1347C622147F6"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.74#SIPD6BCCE349F27A0CE"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.74#SIPE42B0EFF5CCC194B"/>
<rdfs:comment>Specific for phosphorylated vitamin B6 compounds: it acts not only on pyridoxal phosphate (PLP), but also on pyridoxine phosphate (PNP), pyridoxamine phosphate (PMP), 4-pyridoxic acid phosphate and 4-deoxypyridoxine phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This reaction can also be carried out by EC 3.1.3.1 and EC 3.1.3.2, but these enzymes have very broad substrate specificities.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1322411"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7625842"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14522954"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
