<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.3.77">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acireductone synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>E-1 enolase-phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.77#SIP5C305A02E16670E6"/>
<rdfs:comment>This bifunctional enzyme first enolizes the substrate to form the intermediate 2-hydroxy-5-(methylsulfanyl)-3-oxopent-1-enyl phosphate, which is then dephosphorylated to form the acireductone 1,2-dihydroxy-5-(methylsulfanyl)pent-1-en-3-one.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The acireductone represents a branch point in the methione salvage pathway as it is used in the formation of formate, CO and 3-(methylsulfanyl)propanoate by EC 1.13.11.53 and of formate and 4-(methylsulfanyl)-2-oxobutanoate either by a spontaneous reaction under aerobic conditions or by EC 1.13.11.54.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7852397"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8227039"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15843022"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
