<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.3.102">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>FMN hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>FMN phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.102#SIPA691104595DEA1E0"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in many isoforms purified from both bacteria and plants, is a member of the haloacid dehalogenase superfamily.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Most of the isoforms have a wide substrate specificity, but isoforms specific for FMN also exist.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16183635"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16990279"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22002057"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
