<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.3.103">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-nonulopyranosonate 9-phosphatase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-keto-3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate-9-phosphate phosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.3.103#SIP861DA7808CEF2D00"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron, is part of the biosynthesis pathway of the sialic acid 3-deoxy-D-glycero-beta-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate (Kdn).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Kdn is abundant in extracellular glycoconjugates of lower vertebrates such as fish and amphibians, but is also found in the capsular polysaccharides of bacteria that belong to the Bacteroides genus.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18804026"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18986982"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
