<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.4.59">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cyclic-di-AMP phosphodiesterase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.4.59#SIP5D83F06C46267E71"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, described from Gram-positive bacteria, degrades the second messenger cyclic di-3',5'-adenylate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is a membrane-bound protein that contains a cytoplasmic facing Per-Arnt-Sim (PAS) domain, a modified GGDEF domain, and a DHH/DHHA1 domain, which confers the phosphodiesterase activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity requires Mn(2+) and is inhibited by pApA.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19901023"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21909268"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21986827"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27834680"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.1.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.1.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.4.59#SIP5D83F06C46267E71">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3',3'-c-di-AMP + H2O = 5'-O-phosphonoadenylyl-(3'->5')-adenosine + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19901023">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
