</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.4.60">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>pApA phosphodiesterase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pApA hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.4.60#SIP8E67441CBE11FF2D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the Gram-positive bacterium Staphylococcus aureus, is a cytoplasmic protein that contains a DHH/DHHA1 domain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can act on cyclic di-3',5'-adenylate with a much lower activity (cf. EC 3.1.4.59).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity requires Mn(2+) and is inhibited by ppGpp.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24013631"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24566626"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26078723"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26691161"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27834680"/>
