<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.21.8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>T4 deoxyribonuclease II</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>T4 endonuclease II</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.21.8#SIP6D2A31E872A31CB9"/>
<rdfs:comment>This phage T4 enzyme is involved in degradation of host DNA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme primarily catalyzes nicking of the bottom strand of double stranded DNA between the first and second base pair to the right of a top-strand CCGC motif.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Double-stranded breaks are produced 5- to 10-fold less frequently.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It does not cleave the T4 native DNA, which contains 5-hydroxymethylcytosine instead of cytosine.</rdfs:comment>
