<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.1.26.13">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>retroviral ribonuclease H</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.1.26.13#SIP6D395FE572A08D84"/>
<rdfs:comment>Retroviral reverse transcriptase is a multifunctional enzyme responsible for viral replication.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>To perform this task the enzyme combines two distinct activities.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The polymerase domain (EC 2.7.7.49) occupies the N-terminal two-thirds of the reverse transcriptase whereas the ribonuclease H domain comprises the C-terminal remaining one-third.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The RNase H domain of Moloney murine leukemia virus and Human immunodeficiency virus display two metal binding sites.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1281479"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1376369"/>
