<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>alpha-amylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>glycogenase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.1#SIP1FFBE30F4E80FD14"/>
<rdfs:comment>Acts on starch, glycogen and related polysaccharides and oligosaccharides in a random manner; reducing groups are liberated in the alpha-configuration.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The term 'alpha' relates to the initial anomeric configuration of the free sugar group released and not to the configuration of the linkage hydrolyzed.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18134570"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.1#SIP1FFBE30F4E80FD14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Endohydrolysis of (1->4)-alpha-D-glucosidic linkages in polysaccharides containing three or more (1->4)-alpha-linked D-glucose units.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18134570">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
