<skos:altLabel>trehalase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.28#SIP829526DA8376BDC9"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is an anomer-inverting glucosidase that catalyzes the hydrolysis of the alpha-glucosidic O-linkage of alpha,alpha-trehalose, releasing initially equimolar amounts of alpha- and beta-D-glucose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is widely distributed in microorganisms, plants, invertebrates and vertebrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7104311"/>
