<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.40#SIP0454CDBBF92F277A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in animal tissues, plants, yeasts, fungi and bacteria, utilizes an inverting mechanism of hydrolysis, releasing beta-L-rhamnose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Substrates include naringin, rutin, quercitrin, hesperidin, dioscin, terpenyl glycosides and many other natural glycosides containing terminal alpha-L-rhamnose.</rdfs:comment>
