<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.70">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glucan 1,6-alpha-glucosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>exo-1,6-alpha-glucosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>glucodextranase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.70#SIPA32B6148DCD47A05"/>
<rdfs:comment>Hydrolysis is accompanied by inversion at C-1, so that new reducing ends are released in the beta-configuration.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Dextrans and isomaltosaccharides are hydrolyzed, as is isomaltose, but very slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from some sources also possesses the activity of EC 3.2.1.59.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4356399"/>
