<skos:altLabel>Glc3Man9NAc2 oligosaccharide glucosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>processing A-glucosidase I</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.106#SIP03D17ADC91BD082E"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the first step in the processing of the N-glycan tetradecasaccharide precursor Glc3Man9GlcNAc2, which takes place in the endoplasmic reticulum, by removing the distal alpha-1,2-linked glucose residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This and subsequent processing steps are required before complex N-glycans can be synthesized.</rdfs:comment>
