<skos:prefLabel>protein-glucosylgalactosylhydroxylysine glucosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.107#SIP883A46B17CE46470"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme specifically hydrolyzes glucose from alpha-D-glucosyl-(1->2)-beta-D-galactosyl disaccharide units that are linked to hydroxylysine residues of collagen and collagen-like proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Acetylation of the epsilon-amino group of the glycosylated hydroxylysine abolishes activity.</rdfs:comment>
