<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.114">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>mannosyl-oligosaccharide 1,3-1,6-alpha-mannosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ManII</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mannosidase II</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.114#SIP563FF6DD6FD74DB7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in plants and animals, participates in the processing of N-glycans in the Golgi apparatus.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It removes two mannosyl residues, one linked by alpha1,3 linkage, and the other linked by alpha1,6 linkage, both of which are removed by the same catalytic site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is sensitive to swainsonine.</rdfs:comment>
