<rdfs:comment>Within higher eukaryotes post-translational modification of protein serines/threonines with N-acetylglucosamine (O-GlcNAc) is dynamic, inducible and abundant, regulating many cellular processes by interfering with protein phosphorylation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>EC 2.4.1.155 transfers GlcNAc onto substrate proteins and EC 3.2.1.169 cleaves GlcNAc from the modified proteins.</rdfs:comment>
