<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.175">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>beta-D-glucopyranosyl abscisate beta-glucosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ABA-beta-D-glucosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-D-glucopyranosyl abscisate hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.175#SIPD7BC9868A551D816"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme hydrolzes the biologically inactive beta-D-glucopyranosyl ester of abscisic acid to produce active abscisate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Abscisate is a phytohormone critical for plant growth, development and adaption to various stress conditions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme does not hydrolyze beta-D-glucopyranosyl zeatin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10948220"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16990135"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17923167"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.175#SIPD7BC9868A551D816">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(+)-abscisic acid D-glucopyranosyl ester + H2O = 2-cis-(+)-abscisate + beta-D-glucose + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
