<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21147778"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21147778"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.181">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>galactan endo-beta-1,3-galactanase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>endo-beta-1,3-galactanase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.181#SIPB257968630E68642"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the fungus Flammulina velutipes (winter mushroom) hydrolyzes the beta(1->3) bonds found in type II plant arabinogalactans, which occur in cell walls of dicots and cereals.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is an endohydrolase, and requires at least 3 contiguous beta-1,3-residues. cf. EC 3.2.1.89 and EC 3.2.1.145.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21653698"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.181#SIPB257968630E68642">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>The enzyme specifically hydrolyzes beta-1,3-galactan and beta-1,3-galactooligosaccharides.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21653698">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21653698"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21653698"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1074/jbc.m111.251736</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.182">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>4-hydroxy-7-methoxy-3-oxo-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-2-yl glucoside beta-D-glucosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DIMBOAGlc hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DIMBOA glucosidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.182#SIPB12DB9625EDCE554"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.182#SIPA8964C2A569EE830"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Triticum aestivum (wheat) has a higher affinity for DIMBOA glucoside than DIBOA glucoside.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>With Secale cereale (rye) the preference is reversed.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10750901"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10773341"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11106394"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16751439"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21421370"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.182#SIPB12DB9625EDCE554">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>DIMBOA beta-D-glucoside + H2O = D-glucose + DIMBOA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.182#SIPA8964C2A569EE830">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>DIBOA beta-D-glucoside + H2O = D-glucose + DIBOA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
