<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.184">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>UDP-N,N'-diacetylbacillosamine 2-epimerase (hydrolyzing)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UDP-Bac2Ac4Ac 2-epimerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.184#SIP1135237F29BD1F68"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.184#SIPE1038DDBAC860C5D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in biosynthesis of legionaminic acid, a nonulosonate derivative that is incorporated by some bacteria into assorted virulence-associated cell surface glycoconjugates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The initial product formed by the enzyme from Legionella pneumophila, which incorporates legionaminic acid into the O-antigen moiety of its lipopolysaccharide, is 2,4-diacetamido-2,4,6-trideoxy-alpha-D-mannopyranose, which rapidly mutarotates to a mixture of anomers.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Campylobacter jejuni, which incorporates legionaminic acid into flagellin, prefers GDP-N,N'-diacetylbacillosamine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18275154"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19282391"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.184#SIP1135237F29BD1F68">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + UDP-N,N'-diacetylbacillosamine = 2,4-diacetamido-2,4,6-trideoxy-alpha-D-mannopyranose + H(+) + UDP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.184#SIPE1038DDBAC860C5D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>GDP-N,N'-diacetylbacillosamine + H2O = 2,4-diacetamido-2,4,6-trideoxy-alpha-D-mannopyranose + GDP + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18275154">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/18275154"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18275154"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19282391">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19282391"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19282391"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.185">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>non-reducing end beta-L-arabinofuranosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.185#SIPEB3DEF6EFA2478B7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which was identified in the bacterium Bifidobacterium longum JCM1217, removes the beta-L-arabinofuranose residue from the non-reducing end of multiple substrates, including beta-L-arabinofuranosyl-hydroxyproline (Ara-Hyp), Ara2-Hyp, Ara3-Hyp, and beta-L-arabinofuranosyl-(1->2)-1-O-methyl-beta-L-arabinofuranose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the presence of 1-alkanols, the enzyme demonstrates transglycosylation activity, retaining the anomeric configuration of the arabinofuranose residue. cf. EC 3.2.1.55.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24385433"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.185#SIPEB3DEF6EFA2478B7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>beta-L-arabinofuranosyl-(1->2)-beta-L-arabinofuranose + H2O = 2 beta-L-arabinofuranose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24385433">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/24385433"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24385433"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1074/jbc.m113.528711</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.186">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>protodioscin 26-O-beta-D-glucosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>furostanol 26-O-beta-D-glucoside glucohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>furostanol glycoside 26-O-beta-D-glucosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>torvosidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.186#SIP48E54F7AA0883132"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme has been characterized from the plants Cheilocostus speciosus and Solanum torvum.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It also hydrolyzes the 26-beta-D-glucose group from related steroid glucosides such as protogracillin, torvoside A and torvoside H.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8549824"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16289258"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.186#SIP48E54F7AA0883132">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + protodioscin = 26-deglucoprotodioscin + D-glucose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8549824">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8549824"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8549824"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16289258">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/16289258"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16289258"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.187">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(Ara-f)3-Hyp beta-L-arabinobiosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-L-arabinobiosidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.187#SIP95E958D233E52EC1"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which was identified in the bacterium Bifidobacterium longum JCM1217, is specific for (Ara-f)3-Hyp, a sugar chain found in hydroxyproline-rich glyoproteins such as extensin and lectin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme was not able to accept (Ara-f)2-Hyp or (Ara-f)4-Hyp as substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the presence of 1-alkanols, the enzyme demonstrates transglycosylation activity, retaining the anomeric configuration of the arabinofuranose residue.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21149454"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.187#SIP95E958D233E52EC1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>4-O-(beta-L-arabinofuranosyl-(1->2)-beta-L-arabinofuranosyl-(1->2)-beta-L-arabinofuranosyl)-(2S,4S)-4-hydroxyproline + H2O = 4-O-(beta-L-arabinofuranosyl)-(2S,4S)-4-hydroxyproline + beta-L-arabinofuranosyl-(1->2)-beta-L-arabinofuranose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21149454">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21149454"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21149454"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.188">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>avenacosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.188#SIPEA84F78779847A42"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from oat (Avena sativa) seedlings.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product acts as a defense system against fungal infection.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts on avenacoside A.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8000004"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8013661"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.188#SIPEA84F78779847A42">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>avenacoside B + H2O = 26-desgluco-avenacoside B + D-glucose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8000004">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8000004"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8000004"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8013661">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8013661"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8013661"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.189">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dioscin glycosidase (diosgenin-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dioscin glycosidase (aglycone-forming)</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.189#SIP453AAD254D80CC76"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in degradation of the steroid saponin dioscin by some fungi of the Absidia genus.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also hydrolyze 3-O-[alpha-L-Ara-(1->4)-[alpha-L-Rha-(1->2)]-beta-D-Glc]diosgenin into diosgenin and free sugars as the final products.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>(cf. EC 3.2.1.190).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20622501"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.189#SIP453AAD254D80CC76">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dioscin + 3 H2O = D-glucose + diosgenin + 2 L-rhamnopyranose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20622501">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20622501"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20622501"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.190">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dioscin glycosidase (3-O-beta-D-Glc-diosgenin-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dioscin-alpha-L-rhamnosidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.190#SIP14FE519D5D5D74F2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in the hydrolysis of the steroid saponin dioscin by the digestive system of Sus scrofa (pig). cf. EC 3.2.1.189.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16079518"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.190#SIP14FE519D5D5D74F2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dioscin + 2 H2O = diosgenin 3-O-beta-D-glucoside + 2 L-rhamnopyranose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16079518">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/16079518"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16079518"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1248/cpb.53.911</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.191">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ginsenosidase type III</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.191#SIPE92D876BF486A6D7"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.191#SIPD2C254BFF6A3424E"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.191#SIP89A9FBFC785EC58C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.191#SIP0747330A4DBDB509"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.191#SIPED3720B56330CBD2"/>
<rdfs:comment>Ginsenosidase type III catalyzes the sequential hydrolysis of the 3-O-beta-D-(1->2)-glucopyranosyl bond followed by hydrolysis of the 3-O-beta-D-glucopyranosyl bond of protopanaxadiol ginsenosides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>When acting for example on ginsenoside Rb1 the enzyme first generates ginsenoside XVII, and subsequently ginsenoside LXXV.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20622122"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22450790"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23717145"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.191#SIPE92D876BF486A6D7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a protopanaxadiol-type ginsenoside with two glucosyl residues at position 3 + 2 H2O = a protopanaxadiol-type ginsenoside with no glycosidic modification at position 3 + 2 D-glucopyranose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.191#SIPD2C254BFF6A3424E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside Rd + 2 H2O = (20S)-ginsenoside C-K + 2 D-glucose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.191#SIP89A9FBFC785EC58C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside Rb2 + 2 H2O = (20S)-ginsenoside C-Y + 2 D-glucose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.191#SIP0747330A4DBDB509">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside Rb1 + 2 H2O = 2 D-glucose + gypenoside LXXV.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.191#SIPED3720B56330CBD2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(20S)-ginsenoside Rg3 + 2 H2O = (20S)-protopanaxadiol + 2 D-glucose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
