<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.213">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>galactan exo-1,6-beta-galactobiohydrolase (non-reducing end)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>exo-beta-1,6-galactobiohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.213#SIP3D02C4BE84B1EBB8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bifidobacterium longum, specifically hydrolyzes (1->6)-beta-galactobiose from the non-reducing terminal of (1->6)-beta-D-galactooligosaccharides with a degree of polymerization (DP) of 3 or higher, using an exo mode of action.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme cannot hydrolyze alpha-L-arabinofuranosylated (1->6)-beta-galactans (as found in arabinogalactans) and does not act on (1->3)-beta-D- or (1->4)-beta-D-galactans. cf. EC 3.2.1.164.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30564851"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.213#SIP3D02C4BE84B1EBB8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Hydrolysis of (1->6)-beta-D-galactosidic linkages in arabinogalactan proteins and (1->3):(1->6)-beta-galactans to yield (1->6)-beta-galactobiose as the final product.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30564851">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/30564851"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30564851"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1007/s00253-018-9566-4</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.214">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>exo beta-1,2-glucooligosaccharide sophorohydrolase (non-reducing end)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.214#SIP6EA37CABF568B575"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Parabacteroides distasonis, specifically hydrolyzes (1->2)-beta-D-glucooligosaccharides to sophorose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The best substrates are the tetra- and pentasaccharides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is not able to cleave the trisaccharide, and activity with longer linear (1->2)-beta-D-glucans is quite low.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme acts in exo mode and is not able to hydrolyze cyclic (1->2)-beta-D-glucans.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29763309"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.214#SIP6EA37CABF568B575">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>[(1->2)-beta-D-glucosyl](n) + H2O = [(1->2)-beta-D-glucosyl](n-2) + sophorose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29763309">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/29763309"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29763309"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.215">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>arabinogalactan exo alpha-(1,3)-alpha-D-galactosyl-(1->3)-L-arabinofuranosidase (non-reducing end)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3-O-alpha-D-galactosyl-alpha-L-arabinofuranosidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.215#SIPB36A6F0B568040F5"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bifidobacterium longum, specifically hydrolyzes alpha-D-Galp-(1->3)-L-Araf disaccharides from the non-reducing terminal of arabinogalactan using an exo mode of action.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is particularly active with gum arabic arabinogalactan, a type II arabinogalactan produced by acacia trees.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also hydrolyze beta-L-Arap-(1->3)-L-Araf disaccharides, but this activity is significantly lower.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/33674431"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.215#SIPB36A6F0B568040F5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Hydrolysis of alpha-D-Galp-(1->3)-L-Araf disaccharides from non-reducing terminals in branches of type II arabinogalactan attached to proteins.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/33674431">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/33674431"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33674431"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1128/aem.02690-20</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.216">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>kojibiose hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>kojibiase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.1.216#SIPF4E05A497E6DE34D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Flavobacterium johnsoniae and Mucilaginibacter mallensis, uses anomer-inverting mechanism to release beta-glucose from the non-reducing ends of kojibiose and alpha-1,2-oligoglucans with a higher degree of polymerization.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/34684901"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/34728215"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.1.216#SIPF4E05A497E6DE34D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + kojibiose = beta-D-glucose + D-glucose.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/34684901">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/34684901"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34684901"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.3390/molecules26206321</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/34728215">
