</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.2.5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>NAD(+) glycohydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ADP-ribosyl cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-NAD(+) glycohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>diphosphopyridine nucleosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DPNase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DPN hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NAD(+) nucleosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NADase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NAD glycohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NAD nucleosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide glycohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide nucleosidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.2.5#SIP327CCCA2EEC40B37"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis of NAD(+), without associated ADP-ribosyl cyclase activity (unlike the metazoan enzyme EC 3.2.2.6, bifunctional ADP-ribosyl cyclase/cyclic ADP-ribose hydrolase).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Group A streptococci has been implicated in the pathogenesis of diseases such as streptococcal toxic shock-like syndrome (STSS) and necrotizing fasciitis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the venom of the snake Agkistrodon acutus also catalyzes EC 3.6.1.5.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/236282"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4322210"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18952139"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20018886"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21300288"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.2.5#SIP327CCCA2EEC40B37">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + NAD(+) = ADP-D-ribose + H(+) + nicotinamide.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
