<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.2.30">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>aminodeoxyfutalosine nucleosidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>AFL nucleosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>aminofutalosine nucleosidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>methylthioadenosine nucleosidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.2.2.30#SIP196441025168A264"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, found in several bacterial species, catalyzes a step in a modified futalosine pathway for menaquinone biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While the enzyme from some organisms also has the activity of EC 3.2.2.9 the enzyme from Chlamydia trachomatis is specific for 6-amino-6-deoxyfutalosine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18801996"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21098241"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21489995"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22891633"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23148563"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24419390"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25253688"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.2.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.2.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.2.2.30#SIP196441025168A264">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>6-amino-6-deoxyfutalosine + H2O = adenine + dehypoxanthine futalosine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
