<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.3.2.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>leukotriene-A4 hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>leukotriene A4 hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>LTA-4 hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.3.2.6#SIP046F4C23B193AF93"/>
<rdfs:comment>A bifunctional zinc metalloprotease that displays both epoxide hydrolase and aminopeptidase activities.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It preferentially cleaves tripeptides at an arginyl bond, with dipeptides and tetrapeptides being poorer substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It also converts leukotriene A4 into leukotriene B4, unlike EC 3.2.2.10 which converts leukotriene A4 into 5,6-dihydroxy-7,9,11,14-eicosatetraenoic acid.</rdfs:comment>
