<activity rdf:resource="3.4.11.5#SIPFD6CDEFF3B6E9920"/>
<rdfs:comment>Present in the cytosol of mammalian and microbial cells.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In contrast to the mammalian form, the bacterial form of the enzyme hydrolyzes both polyproline and prolyl-2-naphthylamide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The mammalian enzyme, which is not specific for prolyl bonds, is possibly identical with EC 3.4.11.1.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family S33.</rdfs:comment>
