<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.11.26">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>intermediate cleaving peptidase 55</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.11.26#SIP030305128174C506"/>
<rdfs:comment>Icp55 removes the destabilizing N-terminal amino acid residues that are left after cleavage by the mitochondrial processing peptidase, leading to the stabilization of the substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can remove single amino acids or a short peptide, as in the case of cysteine desulfurase (EC 2.8.1.7), where three amino acids are removed.</rdfs:comment>
