<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.13.23">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cysteinylglycine-S-conjugate dipeptidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.13.23#SIP681E4E8671105CF8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in a widespread glutathione-mediated detoxification pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In animals the activity is usually catalyzed by enzymes that have numerous additional activities, such as EC 3.4.11.1, EC 3.4.11.2 and EC 3.4.13.19.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However, in the bacterium Corynebacterium sp.Ax20, which degrades axillary secretions, the enzyme appears to be specific for this task.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2865778"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6108111"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12675513"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13436444"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18515361"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.4.13.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.4.13.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.13.23#SIP681E4E8671105CF8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an S-substituted L-cysteinylglycine + H2O = an S-substituted L-cysteine + glycine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
