<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.14.14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[mycofactocin precursor peptide] peptidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.14.14#SIPF7BC80DEC51E2053"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires Fe(2+) ad Zn(2+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of the enzyme cofactor mycofactocin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes cleavage of the mycofactocin precursor peptide following its modification by MftC to liberate its final two residues, which consist of a cross-linked valine-tyramine dipeptide.</rdfs:comment>
