<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>peptidyl-dipeptidase B</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>atrial di-(tri-)peptidyl carboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>atriopeptin convertase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dipeptidyl carboxyhydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.15.4#SIP35B9E2BD97A8317B"/>
<rdfs:comment>A membrane-bound, zinc metallopeptidase located in mammalian atrial, but not ventricular, myocytes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Although it is capable of converting the 126-residue atriopeptin III directly to atriopeptin I by releasing a C-terminal tripeptide Phe-Arg-Tyr, it is generally restricted to the release of dipeptides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In contrast to EC 3.4.15.1 it displays no chlorine dependence and shows no action on angiotensin I.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Conversely, peptidyl-dipeptidase a is unable to release Phe-Arg from the C-terminus of atriopeptin II.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2501770"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2999723"/>
