<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.19.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="3.4.15.2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>peptidyl-glycinamidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>carboxyamidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>peptidyl carboxyamidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.19.2#SIPDDD5950C18BC4462"/>
<rdfs:comment>Inactivates vasopressin and oxytocin by splitting off glycinamide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also cleaves ester substrates of trypsin and chymotrypsin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Although glycinamide is by far the preferred leaving group, other aminoacylamides may also be released, e.g. phenylalaninamide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The toad skin enzyme is inhibited by diisopropyl fluorophosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1122284"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6766314"/>
