<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.19.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>pyroglutamyl-peptidase II</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PAP-II</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pyroglutamyl aminopeptidase II</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>thyroliberinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>thyrotropin-releasing hormone degrading ectoenzyme</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TRH-DE</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TRH-degrading ectoenzyme</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TRH-specific aminopeptidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.19.6#SIP862125ED3B0C66E4"/>
<rdfs:comment>Highly specific for thyrotropin releasing hormone (pyroglutamyl-histidyl-prolylamide).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Will not cleave the pyroglutamyl-histidyl bond of luteinizing hormone releasing hormone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Found in serum and brain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Inhibited by metal chelators.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family M1.</rdfs:comment>
