<skos:prefLabel>coagulation factor Xa</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>prothrombase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>prothrombinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Stuart factor</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>thrombokinase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.21.6#SIPCC94611C1EFEC929"/>
<rdfs:comment>A blood coagulation factor formed from the proenzyme factor X by limited proteolysis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Factor X is a glycoprotein composed of a heavy chain and a light chain, which are generated from a precursor protein by the excision of the tripeptide RKR and held together by one or more disulfide bonds.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The activated factor Xa converts prothrombin to thrombin in the presence of factor Va, Ca(2+) and phospholipids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Scutelarin (EC 3.4.21.60) has similar specificity, but does not require factor Va.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family S1.</rdfs:comment>
