<skos:prefLabel>protein C (activated)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>activated blood coagulation factor XIV</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>autoprothrombin IIA</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.21.69#SIP02A3BD57DC3486A6"/>
<rdfs:comment>One of the gamma-carboxyglutamic acid-containing coagulation factors.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Formed from protein C, the proenzyme that circulates in plasma, by the action of a complex of thrombin with thrombomodulin, or by serine endopeptidases present in several snake venoms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family S1.</rdfs:comment>
