<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.93">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>proprotein convertase 1</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NEC 1</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>neuroendocrine convertase 1</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PC1</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>prohormone convertase I</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.21.93#SIP8369D0E55D6186D6"/>
<rdfs:comment>A calcium dependent enzyme, maximally active at about pH 5.5.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Substrates include pro-opiomelanocortin, prorenin, proenkephalin, prodynorphin, prosomatostatin and proinsulin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike prohormone convertase 2, does not cleave proluteinizing-hormone-releasing hormone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Usually processing of prodynorphin occurs at a bond in which P2 is Thr.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Present in the regulated secretory pathway of neuroendocrine cells, commonly actin co-operatively with prohormone convertase 2.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family S8.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1429684"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1988934"/>
