<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.105">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>rhomboid protease</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.21.105#SIPBA95CD102CE2C56D"/>
<rdfs:comment>These endopeptidases are multi-spanning membrane proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Their catalytic site is embedded within the membrane and they cleave type-1 transmembrane domains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Important for embryo development in Drosophila melanogaster.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Rhomboid is a key regulator of EGF receptor signaling and is responsible for cleaving Spitz, the main ligand of the Drosophila EGF receptor pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Parasite-encoded rhomboid enzymes are also important for invasion of host cells by Toxoplasma and the malaria parasite.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family S54.</rdfs:comment>
