<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.110">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>C5a peptidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>SCP</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>streptococcal C5a peptidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.21.110#SIP3D3AD77B31353D38"/>
<rdfs:comment>Surface-associated subtilisin-like serine peptidase with very specific substrate specificity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Virulent strains of streptococci, including Streptococcus pyogenes, can evade human detection and phagocytosis by destroying the complement chemotaxin C5a.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Cleavage of human C5a by this enzyme reduces the ability of C5a to bind receptors on the surface of polymorphonuclear neutrophil leukocytes (PMNLs) and thereby abolishes its chemotactic properties.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family S8A.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1452354"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1996961"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3906656"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10809707"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12354115"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16565520"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.4.21.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.4.21.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.110#SIP3D3AD77B31353D38">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>The primary cleavage site is at 67-His-|-Lys-68 in human C5a with a minor secondary cleavage site at 58-Ala-|-Ser-59.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
