<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.117">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>stratum corneum chymotryptic enzyme</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>kallikrein 7</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>SCCE</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>serine protease 6</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.21.117#SIP433003B7E794ED6D"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme has wide substrate specificity, being able to degrade heat-denatured bovine casein and the alpha-chain of native human fibrinogen.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It cleaves the B chain of bovine insulin at 6-Leu-|-Cya-7 (cysteic acid), 16-Tyr-|-Leu-17, 25-Phe-|-Tyr-26 and 26-Tyr-|-Thr-27.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is thought to play a role in the desquamation (skin-shedding) of the outer layer of skin, the stratum corneum, by degrading intercellular cohesive structures.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family S1A.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7794273"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8034709"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8393902"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10974542"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15191543"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.4.21.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.4.21.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.117#SIP433003B7E794ED6D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Cleavage of proteins with aromatic side chains in the P1 position.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
