<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.122">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>transmembrane protease serine 2</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>epitheliasin</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.21.122#SIP3EA801D2D92E2DA3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, present in mammalia, cleaves and inactivates EC 3.4.17.23 at arginine residues in the region R697 to R716, which enhances influenza and coronavirus uptake.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also cleaves and activates influenza and coronavirus spike glycoproteins and thus facilitates virus-cell membrane fusions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The cleavage of SARS-COV2 spike glycoprotein occurs between the S2 and S2' site at SKPSKR/SFIEDL, while the cleavage of MERS-COV glycoprotein occurs at GSRSAR/SAIEDL.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10683448"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11322890"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20237084"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21994442"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23536651"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23966399"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24227843"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31391268"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/32703818"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.4.21.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.4.21.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.21.122#SIP3EA801D2D92E2DA3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>The enzyme cleaves angiotensin-converting enzyme 2 (EC 3.4.17.23) and cleaves influenzea A and B virus and coronavirus spike glycoproteins at arginine residues.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
