<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.22.39">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>adenain</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.22.39#SIPCB06B435EE642135"/>
<rdfs:comment>A cysteine endopeptidase from adenoviruses.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity is greatly stimulated by the binding to the enzyme of an 11-residue peptide from the adenovirus capsid protein pre-VI at a site separate from the active site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family C5.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8422686"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8617222"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.4.22.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.4.22.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.22.39#SIPCB06B435EE642135">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Cleaves proteins of the adenovirus and its host cell at two consensus sites: -Yaa-Xaa-Gly-Gly-|-Xaa- and -Yaa-Xaa-Gly-Xaa-|-Gly- (in which Yaa is Met, Ile or Leu, and Xaa is any amino acid).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8422686">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8422686"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8422686"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8617222">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8617222"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8617222"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.22.40">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bleomycin hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>aminopeptidase C (Lactococcus lactis)</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.22.40#SIP7DEE48B7A7A025E8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The active sites are on the walls of a central channel through the molecule, and access of substrate molecules to them is obstructed by this and by the C-terminus of each polypeptide chain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Bleomycin can scarcely be the natural substrate, and there are reports of limited endopeptidase activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Known from bacteria as well as eukaryotic organisms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Hydrolase H from chicken muscle has many similarities to bleomycin hydrolase, but hydrolyzes Ph-CO-Arg-2-naphthylamine as well as aminopeptidase substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family C1.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8639621"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9151954"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9546047"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9546396"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.4.22.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.4.22.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.22.40#SIP7DEE48B7A7A025E8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Inactivates bleomycin B2 (a cytotoxic glycometallopeptide) by hydrolysis of a carboxyamide bond of beta-aminoalanine, but also shows general aminopeptidase activity. The specificity varies somewhat with source, but amino acid arylamides of Met, Leu and Ala are preferred.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8639621">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8639621"/>
