<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.22.54">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>calpain-3</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>calcium-activated neutral proteinase 3</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>calpain L3</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>calpain p94</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CANP 3</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CAPN3</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>muscle-specific calcium-activated neutral protease 3</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.22.54#SIP2E1BE940A5FD491D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Activated by autoproteolytic cleavage of insertion sequence 1 (IS1), which allows substrates and inhibitors gain access to the active site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Substrates include the protein itself and connectin/titin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family C2.</rdfs:comment>
