<skos:altLabel>human immunodeficiency virus type 1 protease</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.23.16#SIP1506ECF3754E08FD"/>
<rdfs:comment>Present in human immunodeficiency virus type 1.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Contributes to the maturation of the viral particle, and is a target of antiviral drugs.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Active enzyme is a dimer of identical 11-kDa subunits.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Similar enzymes occur in other retroviruses.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family A2.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.4.23.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.4.23.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.4.23.16#SIP1506ECF3754E08FD">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Specific for a P1 residue that is hydrophobic, and P1' variable, but often Pro.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
