<skos:prefLabel>cathepsin E</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>erythrocyte membrane aspartic proteinase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>slow-moving proteinase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.23.34#SIP6CB04BF957607ADE"/>
<rdfs:comment>Found in stomach, spleen, erythrocyte membrane; not lysosomal.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Pro-cathepsin E is an 86 kDa disulfide-linked dimer; activation or reduction produces monomers.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family A1.</rdfs:comment>
