<activity rdf:resource="3.4.24.36#SIP0C1AC0D5B9936B4F"/>
<rdfs:comment>A membrane-bound glycoprotein found on the promastigote of various species of Leishmania protozoans.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Contains consensus sequence for a zinc binding site; Z-Tyr-Leu-NHOH is a strong inhibitor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can activate its proenzyme by cleavage of the 100-Val-|-Val-101 bond.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>An acidic pH optimum is found with certain protein substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family M8.</rdfs:comment>
