<skos:altLabel>hemorrhagic toxin e</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.4.24.44#SIPC2AAC0B1C83DB11E"/>
<rdfs:comment>Hemorrhagic endopeptidase from the venom of the western diamondback rattlesnake (Crotalus atrox).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Digests basement membrane components, including the triple helix of type IV collagen.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Such action is believed to contribute to the hemorrhagic property by weakening capillary walls.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Belongs to peptidase family M12B.</rdfs:comment>
