<skos:altLabel>N-acyl-L-amino-acid amidohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.14#SIPB4497AC29F4E46EE"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.14#SIPF473C2F80E1793BD"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is found in animals and is involved in the hydrolysis of N-acylated or N-acetylated amino acids (except L-aspartate).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It acts on mercapturic acids (S-conjugates of N-acetyl-L-cysteine) and neutral aliphatic N-acyl-alpha-amino acids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Some bacterial aminoacylases demonstrate substrate specificity of both EC 3.5.1.14 and EC 3.5.1.114. cf. EC 3.5.1.15 and EC 3.5.1.114.</rdfs:comment>
