</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.57">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tryptophanamidase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.57#SIP04DB44FD3847F2ED"/>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts on N-ethylformamide and L-tyrosinamide, and on some tryptophan dipeptides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.57#SIP04DB44FD3847F2ED">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + L-tryptophanamide = L-tryptophan + NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.58">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>N-benzyloxycarbonylglycine hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.58#SIPDCCEEB71731963B3"/>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts, more slowly, on N-benzyloxycarbonylalanine, but not on the corresponding derivatives of other amino acids or on N-benzyloxycarbonylpeptides (cf. EC 3.5.1.64).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.58#SIPDCCEEB71731963B3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + H2O + N-benzyloxycarbonylglycine = benzyl alcohol + CO2 + glycine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.59">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>N-carbamoylsarcosine amidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CSHase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N-carbamoylsarcosine amidohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.59#SIP368A35DAB0E57ECA"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.59#SIP368A35DAB0E57ECA">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + H2O + N-carbamoylsarcosine = CO2 + NH4(+) + sarcosine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.60">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>N-(long-chain-acyl)ethanolamine deacylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N-acylethanolamine amidohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.60#SIP6F33C5AAA5DB835B"/>
<rdfs:comment>This lysosomal enzyme acts best on palmitoyl ethanolamide, with lower activity on other N-(long-chain-acyl)ethanolamines.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is only active at acidic pH.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 3.5.1.99 it does not act on primary amides such as oleamide, and has only a marginal activity with anandamide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is translated as an inactive proenzyme, followed by autocatalytic cleavage into two subunits that reassociate to form an active heterodimeric complex.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10431820"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11463796"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17980170"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22040171"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.60#SIP6F33C5AAA5DB835B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + N-(long-chain fatty acyl)ethanolamine = a long-chain fatty acid + ethanolamine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
