<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.84">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>biuret amidohydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.84#SIP72AE265AB81B49E3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Rhizobium leguminosarum bv. viciae 3841, participates in the degradation of cyanurate, an intermediate in the degradation of s-triazide herbicides such as atrazine [2-chloro-4-(ethylamino)-6-(isopropylamino)-1,3,5-triazine].</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrate, biuret, forms by the spontaneous decarboxylation of 1-carboxybiuret in the absence of 1-carboxybiuret hydrolase.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21897878"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29425231"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29523689"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.84#SIP72AE265AB81B49E3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>biuret + H2O = NH4(+) + urea-1-carboxylate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
