<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.94">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>gamma-glutamyl-gamma-aminobutyrate hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>gamma-glutamyl-GABA hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.94#SIPD12540FCFF8A6E86"/>
<rdfs:comment>Forms part of a novel putrescine-utilizing pathway in Escherichia coli, in which it has been hypothesized that putrescine is first glutamylated to form gamma-glutamylputrescine, which is oxidized to 4-(gamma-glutamylamino)butanal and then to 4-(gamma-glutamylamino)butanoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also can catalyze the reactions of EC 3.5.1.35 and EC 3.5.1.65.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15590624"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
