<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.105">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>chitin disaccharide deacetylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>chitin oligosaccharide amidohydolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>chitin oligosaccharide deacetylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>chitobiose amidohydolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.105#SIPAA560999EAA6B99C"/>
<rdfs:comment>Chitin oligosaccharide deacetylase is a key enzyme in the chitin catabolic cascade of chitinolytic Vibrio strains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Besides being a nutrient, the heterodisaccharide product 4-O-(N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl)-D-glucosamine is a unique inducer of chitinase production in Vibrio parahemolyticus.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In contrast to EC 3.5.1.41 this enzyme is specific for the chitin disaccharide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It also deacetylates the chitin trisaccharide with lower efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>No activity with higher polymers of GlcNAc.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16232910"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17334758"/>
