</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.121">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>protein N-terminal asparagine amidohydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.121#SIP05DE8F3D85BCC361"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme participates in the eukaryotic ubiquitin-dependent Arg/N-end rule pathway of protein degradation, promoting the turnover of intracellular proteins that initiate with Met-Asn.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Following the acetylation and removal of the initiator methionine, the exposed N-terminal asparagine is deaminated, resulting in its conversion to L-aspartate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The latter serves as a substrate for EC 2.3.2.8 making the protein susceptible to arginylation, polyubiquitination and degradation as specified by the N-end rule.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8089117"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8910481"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21375249"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.121#SIP05DE8F3D85BCC361">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + H2O + N-terminal L-asparaginyl-[protein] = N-terminal L-aspartyl-[protein] + NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8089117">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/8089117"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8089117"/>
</rdf:Description>
