</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.128">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>deaminated glutathione amidase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>dGSH deaminase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.128#SIPAAEAB59155D94FB3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, present in animals, fungi and bacteria, is involved in clearing cells of the toxic compound deaminated glutathione, which can be produced as an unwanted side product by several transaminases.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28373563"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.128#SIPAAEAB59155D94FB3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + N-(4-oxoglutaryl)-L-cysteinylglycine = 2-oxoglutarate + L-cysteinylglycine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28373563">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/28373563"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28373563"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.129">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>N(5)-(cytidine 5'-diphosphoramidyl)-L-glutamine hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N(5)-(cytidine 5'-diphosphoramidyl)-L-glutamine deacylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.129#SIP42CA287CAE5B0790"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Campylobacter jejuni, is involved in formation of a unique O-methyl phosphoramidate modification on specific sugar residues within the bacterium's capsular polysaccharides.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29023101"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.129#SIP42CA287CAE5B0790">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + N(5)-(cytidine 5'-diphosphoramidyl)-L-glutamine = cytidine 5'-diphosphoramidate + H(+) + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29023101">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/29023101"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29023101"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.1.130">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>[amino group carrier protein]-lysine hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.1.130#SIP66F895A10DFD5EF3"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in an L-lysine biosynthetic pathway in certain species of archaea and bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In some organisms the enzyme also catalyzes the activity of EC 3.5.1.132.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19620981"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23434852"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27566549"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28720495"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
