<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.2.16">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>maleimide hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cyclic imide hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>imidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.2.16#SIP1DA8B0065C5AD324"/>
<rdfs:comment>Succinimide and glutarimide, and sulfur-containing cyclic imides, such as rhodanine, can also act as substrates for the enzyme from Blastobacter sp. A17p-4.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reverse, cyclization, reaction is also catalyzed, but much more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has lower activity toward cyclic ureides, which are the substrates of EC 3.5.2.2.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9030755"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.2.16#SIP1DA8B0065C5AD324">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + maleimide = H(+) + maleamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9030755">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
