<skos:prefLabel>allantoate deiminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.3.9#SIPAFFF3A5CD79292A9"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is part of the ureide pathway, which permits certain organisms to recycle the nitrogen in purine compounds.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, which liberates ammonia from allantoate, is present in plants and bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In plants it is localized in the endoplasmic reticulum.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Requires manganese.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5328936"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20038185"/>
