<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.3.21">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>methylenediurea deaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>methylenediurease</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.3.21#SIPE44009887CBB2DB2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The methylenediurea is hydrolyzed and decarboxylated to give an aminated methylurea, which then spontaneously hydrolyzes to hydroxymethylurea.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Ochrobactrum anthropi also hydrolyzes dimethylenetriurea and trimethylenetetraurea as well as ureidoglycolate, which is hydrolyzed to urea and glyoxylate, and allantoate, which is hydrolyzed to ureidoglycolate, ammonia and carbon dioxide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.3.21#SIPE44009887CBB2DB2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 H(+) + 2 H2O + methylenediurea = CO2 + N-(hydroxymethyl)urea + 2 NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.3.22">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>proclavaminate amidinohydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PAH</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>proclavaminate amidino hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>proclavaminic acid amidino hydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.3.22#SIP8C305B40EB6070BE"/>
<rdfs:comment>Forms part of the pathway for the biosythesis of the beta-lactamase inhibitor clavulanate in Streptomyces clavuligerus.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It carries out an intermediary reaction between the first reaction of EC 1.14.11.21, and the second and third reactions of that enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1998687"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7601835"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12413541"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
