<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>S-adenosylhomocysteine deaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.4.28#SIP22D9486414ABE15F"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2592350"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.28#SIP22D9486414ABE15F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + H2O + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine = NH4(+) + S-inosyl-L-homocysteine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2592350">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/2592350"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2592350"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.29">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>GTP cyclohydrolase IIa</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GTP cyclohydrolase III</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.4.29#SIPAD880087019D4962"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis of the imidazole ring of guanosine 5'-triphosphate, N(7)-methylguanosine 5'-triphosphate or inosine 5'-triphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Xanthosine 5'-triphosphate and ATP are not substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It also catalyzes the hydrolysis of diphosphate to form two equivalents of phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 3.5.4.25, this enzyme does not release formate, but does hydrolyze the diphosphate from GTP to phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12475257"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.29#SIPAD880087019D4962">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>GTP + 3 H2O = 2-amino-5-formylamino-6-(5-phospho-D-ribosylamino)pyrimidin-4(3H)-one + 2 H(+) + 2 phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12475257">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/12475257"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12475257"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.30">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>dCTP deaminase (dUMP-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.4.30#SIP7FA4AE3B1B759433"/>
<rdfs:comment>Is highly specific for dCTP as substrate as dCMP, CTP, CDP, CMP, cytosine or deoxycytosine are not deaminated.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>While most bacteria require two enzymes to form dUMP from dCTP (EC 3.5.4.13 and EC 3.6.1.23), the archaeon Methanocaldococcus jannaschii uses a single enzyme to carry out both functions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme can also act as a dUTP diphosphatase, but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12538648"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.30#SIP7FA4AE3B1B759433">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>dCTP + 2 H2O = diphosphate + dUMP + NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12538648">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/12538648"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12538648"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.31">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="3.5.4.n1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine deaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>5-methylthioadenosine deaminase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MTA deaminase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.4.31#SIP24568480684C24C4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Thermotoga maritima also functions as S-adenosylhomocysteine deaminase (EC 3.5.4.28) and has some activity against adenosine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Adenosine-5-monophosphate (AMP) and S-adenosyl-L-methionine (SAM) are not substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17603473"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.31#SIP24568480684C24C4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + H2O + S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine = NH4(+) + S-methyl-5'-thioinosine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17603473">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/17603473"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17603473"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.32">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>8-oxoguanine deaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.4.32#SIPB8B1F0E0409283B0"/>
<rdfs:comment>8-oxoguanine is formed via the oxidation of guanine within DNA by reactive oxygen species.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>If uncorrected, this modification leads to the incorporation of 8-oxoG:A mismatches and eventually to G:C to T:A transversions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20088583"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.5.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.32#SIPB8B1F0E0409283B0">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>8-oxoguanine + H(+) + H2O = NH4(+) + urate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20088583">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20088583"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20088583"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.5.4.33">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tRNA(adenine(34)) deaminase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.5.4.33#SIP609FF1993163B636"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in editing of tRNA.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12110595"/>
