<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.1.58">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>8-oxo-dGDP phosphatase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.6.1.58#SIP6C9FF97634807A53"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.6.1.58#SIPA804FED6F26A3605"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis of both 8-oxo-dGDP and 8-oxo-GDP thereby preventing translational errors caused by oxidative damage.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The preferred in vivo substrate is not known.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme does not degrade 8-oxo-dGTP and 8-oxo-GTP to the monophosphates (cf. EC 3.6.1.55).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Ribonucleotide diphosphates and deoxyribonucleotide diphosphates are hydrolyzed with broad specificity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The bifunctional enzyme NUDT5 also hydrolyzes ADP-ribose to AMP and D-ribose 5-phosphate (cf. EC 3.6.1.13).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human enzyme NUDT18 also hydrolyzes 8-oxo-dADP and 2-hydroxy-dADP, the latter at a slower rate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12717453"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16002790"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17052728"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19699693"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21389046"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.1.58#SIP6C9FF97634807A53">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>8-oxo-dGDP + H2O = 8-oxo-dGMP + H(+) + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.1.58#SIPA804FED6F26A3605">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>8-oxo-GDP + H2O = 8-oxo-GMP + H(+) + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
