<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.1.59">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="3.6.1.30"/>
<skos:prefLabel>5'-(N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-[mRNA] diphosphatase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>m(7)GpppN m(7)GMP phosphohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>m(7)GpppX diphosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>m(7)GpppX pyrophosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.6.1.59#SIP3DEB1FE79E5DDE36"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.6.1.59#SIP62988DB0F6188B01"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme removes (decaps) the N(7)-methylguanosine 5-phosphate cap from an mRNA degraded to a maximal length of 10 nucleotides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Decapping is an important process in the control of eukaryotic mRNA degradation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme functions to clear the cell of cap structure following decay of the RNA body.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The nematode enzyme can also decap triply methylated substrates, 5'-(N(2),N(2),N(7)-trimethyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-[mRNA].</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12198172"/>
