<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.1.60">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>diadenosine hexaphosphate hydrolase (AMP-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.6.1.60#SIP2190C1C3AA8CAD5A"/>
<activity rdf:resource="3.6.1.60#SIP89B51D045D6E6AEC"/>
<rdfs:comment>A divalent cation is essential for activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Mn(2+) (2-6 mM) is most effective.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme controls intracellular levels of P(1),P(5)-bis(5'-adenosyl)pentaphosphate and P(1),P(6)-bis(5'-adenosyl)hexaphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Weak activity with P(1),P(4)-bis(5'-adenosyl)tetraphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Marked preference for adenine over guanine nucleotides.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10419486"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12121577"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.1.60#SIP2190C1C3AA8CAD5A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + P(1),P(6)-bis(5'-adenosyl) hexaphosphate = adenosine 5'-pentaphosphate + AMP + 2 H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.1.60#SIP89B51D045D6E6AEC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + P(1),P(5)-bis(5'-adenosyl) pentaphosphate = adenosine 5'-tetraphosphate + AMP + 2 H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
