<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.6.5.n1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>elongation factor 4</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.6.5.n1#SIP43FF428D8047AFDF"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is required for accurate and efficient protein synthesis under certain stress conditions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>May act as a fidelity factor of the translation reaction, by catalyzing a one-codon backward translocation of tRNAs on improperly translocated ribosomes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Back-translocation proceeds from a post-translocation (POST) complex to a pre-translocation (PRE) complex, thus giving elongation factor G a second chance to translocate the tRNAs correctly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Binds to ribosomes in a GTP-dependent manner.</rdfs:comment>
