<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.7.1.23">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>maleylpyruvate hydrolase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="3.7.1.23#SIPDDBBBE2070346656"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas alcaligenes NCIMB 9867, catalyzes the hydrolysis of 3-maleylpyruvate, the ring-cleavage product of gentisate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also act on a number of maleylpyruvate derivatives, such as (2E)-2-methyl-4,6-dioxohept-2-enedioate and (2E)-3-methyl-4,6-dioxohept-2-enedioate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>May be identical to EC 3.7.1.5.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5124802"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7400101"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23204427"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="3.7.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="3.7.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="3.7.1.23#SIPDDBBBE2070346656">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>3-maleylpyruvate + H2O = H(+) + maleate + pyruvate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
