<skos:altLabel>phosphoenolpyruvic carboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.31#SIPDBF1444BFAA0DAE7"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme replenishes oxaloacetate in the tricarboxylic acid cycle when operating in the reverse direction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction proceeds in two steps: formation of carboxyphosphate and the enolate form of pyruvate, followed by carboxylation of the enolate and release of phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
