<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.86">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>diaminobutyrate decarboxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DABA DC</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-2,4-diaminobutanoate carboxy-lyase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-2,4-diaminobutyrate decarboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.86#SIPBB20FA07643A9EBE"/>
<rdfs:comment>N(4)-acetyl-L-2,4-diaminobutanoate, 2,3-diaminopropanoate, ornithine and lysine are not substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Acinetobacter baumannii it is cotranscribed with the neighboring dat gene that encodes EC 2.6.1.76, which can supply the substrate for the decarboxylase.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1512577"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7813892"/>
