<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.115">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>indoleacetate decarboxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>IAD</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.115#SIP9C5DC03D4DBAE943"/>
<rdfs:comment>This glycyl radical enzyme has been isolate from a number of bacterial species.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Skatole contributes to the characteristic smell of animal feces.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30310076"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.115#SIP9C5DC03D4DBAE943">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(indol-3-yl)acetate + H(+) = CO2 + skatole.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30310076">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/30310076"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30310076"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.116">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>D-ornithine/D-lysine decarboxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DOKDC</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.116#SIP39A1011478B31460"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.116#SIP770BE1CF2B74D025"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Salmonella typhimurium LT2, is specific for D-ornithine and D-lysine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Requires pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29024617"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.116#SIP39A1011478B31460">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>D-ornithine + H(+) = CO2 + putrescine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.116#SIP770BE1CF2B74D025">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>D-lysine + H(+) = cadaverine + CO2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29024617">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/29024617"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29024617"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.117">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-[(L-alanin-3-ylcarbamoyl)methyl]-2-hydroxybutanedioate decarboxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.117#SIPA4F3187E9AA7C4CC"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Staphylococcus aureus, participates in the biosynthesis of the siderophore staphyloferrin B.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19775248"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.117#SIPA4F3187E9AA7C4CC">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-[(L-alanin-3-ylcarbamoyl)methyl]-2-hydroxybutanedioate + H(+) = 2-[(2-aminoethylcarbamoyl)methyl]-2-hydroxybutanedioate + CO2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19775248">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/19775248"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19775248"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.118">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>isophthalyl-CoA decarboxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>IPCD</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.118#SIP25210BCB8B08C697"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Syntrophorhabdus aromaticivorans, participates in an anaerobic isophthalate degradation pathway.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme requires a prenylated flavin mononucleotide cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30647456"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.118#SIP25210BCB8B08C697">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H(+) + isophthalyl-CoA = benzoyl-CoA + CO2.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30647456">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/30647456"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30647456"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.119">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phenylacetate decarboxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.1.119#SIP9965C1E3447EF869"/>
<rdfs:comment>This bacterial enzyme, isolated from anoxic, toluene-producing microbial communities, is a glycyl radical enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It needs to be activated by a dedicated activating enzyme (PhdA).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The activase catalyzes the reductive cleavage of AdoMet, producing a 5'-deoxyadenosyl radical that leads to the production of the glycyl radical in PhdB.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27506494"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/29556105"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31512343"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.1.119#SIP9965C1E3447EF869">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-phenylacetate + H(+) = CO2 + toluene.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
