<activity rdf:resource="4.1.2.13#SIP245CAFE9690A281D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts on (3S,4R)-ketose 1-phosphates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes increase electron-attraction by the carbonyl group, some (Class I) forming a protonated imine with it, others (Class II), mainly of microbial origin, polarizing it with a metal ion, e.g. zinc.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2649077"/>
