<skos:altLabel>DTA</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>low specificity D-threonine aldolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.2.42#SIP1A385B383524705D"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.2.42#SIP3288536EC0AEE9AE"/>
<rdfs:comment>Activated by divalent metal cations (e.g. Co(2+), Ni(2+), Mn(2+) or Mg(2+)).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction is reversible, which can lead to the interconversion of D-threonine and D-allo-threonine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Several other D-beta-hydroxy-alpha-amino acids, such as D-beta-phenylserine, D-beta-hydroxy-alpha-aminovaleric acid and D-beta-3,4-dihydroxyphenylserine, can also act as substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9346293"/>
