<replaces rdf:resource="4.1.2.39"/>
<skos:prefLabel>aliphatic (R)-hydroxynitrile lyase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(R)-hydroxynitrile lyase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(R)-oxynitrilase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.2.46#SIPDF51C57353A157C6"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the stereoselective synthesis of aliphatic (R)-cyanohydrins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>No activity toward mandelonitrile and 4-hydroxymandelonitrile.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Natural substrates for the (R)-oxynitrilase from Linum usitatissimum are acetone and butan-2-one, which are the building blocks of the cyanogen glycosides in Linum, linamarin and lotaustralin, or linustatin and neolinustatin, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3377504"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9030531"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.2.46#SIPDF51C57353A157C6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2R)-2-hydroxy-2-methylbutanenitrile = butan-2-one + hydrogen cyanide.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3377504">
