<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.2.48">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>low-specificity L-threonine aldolase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.2.48#SIP1971652FD4007D06"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.2.48#SIP193FF28F6871B67D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The low-specificity L-threonine aldolase can act on both L-threonine and L-allo-threonine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Escherichia coli can also act on L-threo-phenylserine and L-erythro-phenylserine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also catalyze the aldol condensation of glycolaldehyde and glycine to form 4-hydroxy-L-threonine, an intermediate of pyridoxal phosphate biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Different from EC 4.1.2.5 and EC 4.1.2.49.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5017702"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/5438301"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9151955"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9692922"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21119630"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.2.48#SIP1971652FD4007D06">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-threonine = acetaldehyde + glycine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.2.48#SIP193FF28F6871B67D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-allo-threonine = acetaldehyde + glycine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
