<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.3.25">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(S)-citramalyl-CoA lyase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(3S)-citramalyl-CoA pyruvate-lyase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>citramalyl-CoA lyase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.3.25#SIPFD6E06387E772645"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Clostridium tetanomorphum is a component of EC 4.1.3.22.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It also acts on (3S)-citramalyl thioacyl-carrier protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Chloroflexus aurantiacus also has the activity of EC 4.1.3.24.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has no activity with (3R)-citramalyl-CoA (cf. EC 4.1.3.46).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/923590"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4284209"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17259315"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.3.25#SIPFD6E06387E772645">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(3S)-citramalyl-CoA = acetyl-CoA + pyruvate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
