<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tryptophanase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-tryptophan indole-lyase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TNase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.99.1#SIP708741AB5C358715"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme cleaves a carbon-carbon bond, releasing indole and an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form, which undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form pyruvate and ammonia.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The latter reaction, which can occur spontaneously, can also be catalyzed by EC 3.5.99.10.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also catalyzes 2,3-elimination and beta-replacement reactions of some indole-substituted tryptophan analogs of L-cysteine, L-serine and other 3-substituted amino acids.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/236639"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14017164"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14284727"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.1#SIP708741AB5C358715">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + L-tryptophan = indole + NH4(+) + pyruvate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
