</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tyrosine phenol-lyase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-tyrosinase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.99.2#SIP171353AF8C6F2ED7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme cleaves a carbon-carbon bond, releasing phenol and an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form, which undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form pyruvate and ammonia.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The latter reaction, which can occur spontaneously, can also be catalyzed by EC 3.5.99.10.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also slowly catalyzes similar reactions with D-tyrosine, S-methyl-L-cysteine, L-cysteine, L-serine and D-serine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4908868"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4908869"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.2#SIP171353AF8C6F2ED7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + L-tyrosine = NH4(+) + phenol + pyruvate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
