<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.12">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3,4-dihydroxy-2-butanone-4-phosphate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>DHBP synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-3,4-dihydroxybutan-2-one-4-phosphate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.99.12#SIP19716F4CEAB0EB26"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction involves an intramolecular skeletal rearrangement, with the bonds in D-ribulose 5-phosphate that connect C-3 and C-5 to C-4 being broken, C-4 being removed as formate and reconnection of C-3 and C-5.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The phosphorylated four-carbon product (L-3,4-dihydroxybutan-2-one 4-phosphate) is an intermediate in the biosynthesis of riboflavin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2246238"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11342130"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11687623"/>
