<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.20">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="4.3.3.n1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-amino-4-hydroxybenzoate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3,4-AHBA synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.99.20#SIP2BB5DAC735F3F808"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction is suggested to take place in several steps.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Schiff base formation, double bond migration and dephosphorylation followed by ring opening and closing to form a pyrrolidine ring, and finally dehydration to form the product 3-amino-4-hydroxybenzoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the bacterium Streptomyces griseus the enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of grixazone, a yellow pigment that contains a phenoxazinone chromophore.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17003031"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.1.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.1.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.20#SIP2BB5DAC735F3F808">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-amino-4,5-dihydroxy-6-oxo-7-(phosphooxy)heptanoate = 3-amino-4-hydroxybenzoate + H(+) + 2 H2O + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17003031">
