<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.1.99.26">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-amino-5-[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-4,4-dimethylpyrrolidin-2-one synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.1.99.26#SIP6FAE1FB6C50F88C8"/>
<rdfs:comment>This is a bifunctional radical AdoMet (radical SAM) enzyme that catalyzes the first two steps in the biosynthesis of the enzyme cofactor mycofactocin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity requires the presence of the MftB chaperone.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction occurs in the right-to-left direction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The other activity of the enzyme is EC 1.3.98.7.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21223593"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27158836"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28634235"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30628436"/>
