<rdfs:comment>One form requires a cobamide cofactor, while the other is a glycyl radical enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The cobamide-dependent enzyme has been shown to also dehydrate ethylene glycol to acetaldehyde.</rdfs:comment>
