<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/22528483"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22528483"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.78">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(S)-norcoclaurine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(S)-norlaudanosoline synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.78#SIP067C1F7440B032CA"/>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction makes a 6-membered ring by forming a bond between C-6 of the 3,4-dihydroxyphenyl group of the dopamine and C-1 of the aldehyde in the imine formed between the substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product is the precursor of the benzylisoquinoline alkaloids in plants.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Will also catalyze the reaction of 4-(2-aminoethyl)benzene-1,2-diol + (3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)acetaldehyde to form (S)-norlaudanosoline, but this alkaloid has not been found to occur in plants.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12107162"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.78#SIP067C1F7440B032CA">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(4-hydroxyphenyl)acetaldehyde + dopamine = (S)-norcoclaurine + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12107162">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/12107162"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12107162"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.79">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-methylcitrate dehydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-hydroxybutane-1,2,3-tricarboxylate hydro-lyase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-methylcitrate hydro-lyase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.79#SIP8E0CBCE02ECF15A8"/>
<rdfs:comment>Specific for (2S,3S)-methylcitrate, showing no activity with (2R,3S)-methylcitrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Can also use cis-aconitate as a substrate but more slowly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Both this enzyme and EC 4.2.1.3 are required to complete the isomerization of (2S,3S)-methylcitrate to (2R,3S)-2-methylisocitrate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12473114"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.79#SIP8E0CBCE02ECF15A8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2S,3S)-2-methylcitrate = 2-methyl-cis-aconitate + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12473114">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/12473114"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12473114"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.80">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-oxopent-4-enoate hydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-keto-4-pentenoate hydratase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>OEH</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.80#SIP5F994718C311596F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in the catechol meta-cleavage pathway, a major mechanism for degradation of aromatic compounds.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Also acts, more slowly, on cis-2-oxohex-4-enoate, but not on the trans-isomer.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme was named when it was thought that the substrate is 2-oxopent-4-enoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However, it was later found that the actual substrate is its tautomer (2Z)-2-hydroxypenta-2,4-dienoate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In some organisms the enzyme forms a complex with EC 4.1.1.77.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2681159"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7287632"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9492273"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.80#SIP5F994718C311596F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(S)-4-hydroxy-2-oxopentanoate = (2Z)-2-hydroxypenta-2,4-dienoate + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
