<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.119">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>enoyl-CoA hydratase 2</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-enoyl-CoA hydratase 2</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-3-hydroxyacyl-CoA hydro-lyase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-specific 2-trans-enoyl-CoA hydratase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ECH2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.119#SIP32DF4AF635BB4AE3"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme catalyzes a hydration step in peroxisomal beta-oxidation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The human multifunctional enzyme type 2 (MFE-2) is a 79000 Da enzyme composed of three functional units: (3R)-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase, 2-enoyl-CoA hydratase 2 and sterol carrier protein 2-like units.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from Aeromonas caviae and Arabidopsis thaliana are monofunctional enzymes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>2-enoyl-CoA hydratase 3 from Candida tropicalis is a part from multifunctional enzyme type 2.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1879422"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9457873"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11134939"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12832794"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15644212"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16982622"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
