<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.140">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>gluconate/galactonate dehydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>gluconate dehydratase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.140#SIP160C992FFF38C280"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.140#SIPF2911D71D7348CCB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in glucose and galactose catabolism via the nonphosphorylative variant of the Entner-Doudoroff pathway in Picrophilus torridus and via the branched variant of the Entner-Doudoroff pathway in Sulfolobus solfataricus.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In vitro it utilizes D-gluconate with 6-10 fold higher catalytic efficiency than D-galactonate. cf. EC 4.2.1.6 and EC 4.2.1.39.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15474024"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15869466"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20023024"/>
