<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.157">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(R)-2-hydroxyisocaproyl-CoA dehydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-hydroxyisocaproyl-CoA dehydratase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.157#SIP9984778E2B22B9B2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Peptoclostridium difficile, is involved in the reductive branch of L-leucine fermentation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes an alpha/beta-dehydration, which depends on the reductive formation of ketyl radicals on the substrate generated by injection of a single electron from the ATP-dependent activator protein HadI.</rdfs:comment>
