<skos:prefLabel>(R)-2-hydroxyglutaryl-CoA dehydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.167#SIPCD86676E0E21F875"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from the bacteria Acidaminococcus fermentans and Clostridium symbiosum are involved in the fermentation of L-glutamate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme contains [4Fe-4S] clusters, FMNH2 and riboflavin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It must be activated by a an activator protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Once activated, it can catalyze many turnovers.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3691501"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7398622"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7607244"/>
