<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.169">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d 3(1)-hydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.169#SIPF683BD26D8579A6C"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, found in green sulfur bacteria (Chlorobiaceae) and green flimentous bacteria (Chloroflexaceae), is involved in the biosynthesis of bacteriochlorophylls c, d and e.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It acts it the direction of hydration, and the hydroxyl group that is formed is essential for the ability of the resulting bacteriochlorophylls to self-aggregate in the chlorosomes, unique light-harvesting antenna structures found in these organisms.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16245042"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/26331578"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.169#SIPF683BD26D8579A6C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a bacteriochlorophyllide d = a 3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
