<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.1.170">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-(omega-methylthio)alkylmalate dehydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.170#SIP954DA1E684C6CAA8"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.170#SIPDE71665626CBE026"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.170#SIP06380022CF087341"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.170#SIP967EF8BD356CFD23"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.170#SIPD35345B80C2027CE"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.1.170#SIP093CFE92E6B566D7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana, is involved in the L-methionine side-chain elongation pathway, forming substrates for the biosynthesis of aliphatic glucosinolates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>By catalyzing a dehydration of a 2-(omega-methylsulfanyl)alkylmaleate, followed by a hydration at a different position, the enzyme achieves the isomerization of its substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is a heterodimer comprising a large and a small subunits.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The large subunit can also bind to an alternative small subunit, forming EC 4.2.1.33, which participates in L-leucine biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19597944"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
