<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.40">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(Z)-gamma-bisabolene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.40#SIP2CF290A15A15AE14"/>
<rdfs:comment>This sesquiterpenoid enzyme is constitutively expressed in the root, hydathodes and stigma of the plant Arabidopsis thaliana.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>If the leaves of the plant are wounded, e.g. by cutting, the enzyme is also induced close to the wound site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The sesquiterpenoids (E)-nerolidol and alpha-bisabolol are also produced by this enzyme as minor products.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16297850"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.40#SIP2CF290A15A15AE14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (Z)-gamma-bisabolene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
