<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.88">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>viridiflorene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TPS31</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.88#SIP3F25824D313AE2A1"/>
<rdfs:comment>Viridiflorene is the only product of this enzyme from Solanum lycopersicum.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21818683"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.88#SIP3F25824D313AE2A1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = diphosphate + viridiflorene.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21818683">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21818683"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21818683"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.89">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(+)-beta-caryophyllene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.89#SIPA1CEF426EA021628"/>
<rdfs:comment>A multifunctional enzyme which also converts the (+)-beta-caryophyllene to (+)-caryolan-1-ol (see EC 4.2.1.138). cf. EC 4.2.3.57.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21693706"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.89#SIPA1CEF426EA021628">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (+)-(E)-beta-caryophyllene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21693706">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21693706"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21693706"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1074/jbc.m111.265652</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.90">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>5-epi-alpha-selinene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>8a-epi-alpha-selinene synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.90#SIPD1E410F4DA3C5F42"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme forms 5-epi-alpha-selinene possibly via germecrene A or a 1,6-hydride shift mechanism.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18658271"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.90#SIPD1E410F4DA3C5F42">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = 5-epi-alpha-selinene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18658271">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/18658271"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18658271"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.91">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cubebol synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.91#SIPE86BB920FF4BF02A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme gives 28% cubebol, 29% (-)-germacrene D, 10% (+)-delta-cadinene and traces of several other sesquiterpenoids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>See also EC 4.2.3.75 and EC 4.2.3.13.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20419721"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.91#SIPE86BB920FF4BF02A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H2O = cubebol + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20419721">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20419721"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20419721"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.92">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(+)-gamma-cadinene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.92#SIP2297EFBA35D79C45"/>
<rdfs:comment>The cloned enzyme from the melon, Cucumis melo, gave mainly delta- and gamma-cadinene with traces of several other sesquiterpenoids cf. EC 4.2.3.62 and EC 4.2.3.13.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15516500"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18264780"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.92#SIP2297EFBA35D79C45">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (+)-gamma-cadinene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15516500">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/15516500"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15516500"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18264780">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/18264780"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18264780"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.93">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>delta-guaiene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.93#SIP027B08D9A7D8FFD6"/>
<rdfs:comment>In Aquilaria crassna three clones of the enzyme gave about 80% delta-guaiene and 20% alpha-guaiene (see also EC 4.2.3.87).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A fourth clone gave 54% delta-guaiene and 45% alpha-guaiene.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Pogostemon cablin gives 13% delta-guaiene as well as 37% (-)-patchoulol (see EC 4.2.3.70), 13% alpha-guaiene (see EC 4.2.3.87), and traces of at least ten other sesquiterpenoids.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16970904"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20959422"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.93#SIP027B08D9A7D8FFD6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = delta-guaiene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16970904">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/16970904"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16970904"/>
</rdf:Description>
