<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20959422"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20959422"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.94">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>gamma-curcumene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.94#SIPA64461B56AA6BE1A"/>
<rdfs:comment>One of five sesquiterpenoid synthases in Pogostemon cablin (patchouli).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16970904"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.94#SIPA64461B56AA6BE1A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = diphosphate + gamma-curcumene.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16970904">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/16970904"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16970904"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.95">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(-)-alpha-cuprenene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.95#SIPDA0F0105012BC9D1"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Coprinus cinereus produces (-)-alpha-cuprenene with high selectivity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20419721"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.95#SIPDA0F0105012BC9D1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (-)-alpha-cuprenene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20419721">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20419721"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20419721"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.96">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>avermitilol synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.96#SIP424FB11704130658"/>
<rdfs:comment>The recombinent enzyme gives avermitilol (85%) plus traces of germacrene A, germacrene B and viridiflorol.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The (1S)-hydrogen of farnesyl diphosphate is retained.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20536237"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.96#SIP424FB11704130658">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H2O = avermitilol + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20536237">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20536237"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20536237"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.97">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(-)-delta-cadinene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.97#SIPF01A6234A8CE2147"/>
<rdfs:comment>The cyclization mechanism involves an intermediate nerolidyl diphosphate leading to a helminthogermacradienyl cation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Following a 1,3-hydride shift of the original 1-pro-S hydrogen of (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate, cyclization and deprotonation gives (-)-delta-cadinene.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21276937"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.97#SIPF01A6234A8CE2147">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (-)-delta-cadinene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21276937">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21276937"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21276937"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.98">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(+)-T-muurolol synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.98#SIPBBAE71A13931C5A8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The cyclization mechanism involves an intermediate nerolidyl diphosphate leading to a helminthogermacradienyl cation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>After a 1,3-hydride shift of the original 1-pro-S hydrogen of farnesyl diphosphate, cyclization and deprotonation result in (+)-T-muurolol.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21276937"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.98#SIPBBAE71A13931C5A8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H2O = (+)-T-muurolol + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21276937">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21276937"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21276937"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.99">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>labdatriene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.99#SIPB44E0F37B9BFC99B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from rice (Oryza sativa), expressed in Escherichia coli, also produces ent-sandaracopimara-8(14),15-diene from ent-copalyl diphosphate, another naturally occurring copalyl isomer in rice (cf. EC 4.2.3.29).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21323642"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.99#SIPB44E0F37B9BFC99B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>9alpha-copalyl diphosphate = (12E)-9alpha-labda-8(17),12,14-triene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21323642">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21323642"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21323642"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.100">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>bicyclogermacrene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.100#SIP8E056582098261FB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from oregano (Origanum vulgare) gives mainly bicyclogermacrene with Mn(2+) as a cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>With Mg(2+) a more complex mixture is produced.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20419468"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.100#SIP8E056582098261FB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = bicyclogermacrene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20419468">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/20419468"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20419468"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.101">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>7-epi-sesquithujene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TPS4-B73</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.101#SIPCC5CF7754D70FA17"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Zea mays, variety B73, gives mainly 7-epi-sesquithujene with (S)-beta-bisabolene and traces of other sesquiterpenoids, cf. EC 4.2.3.55.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The product ratio is dependent on which metal ion is present.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>7-epi-sesquithujene is an attractant for the emerald ash borer beetle.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15075399"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.101#SIPCC5CF7754D70FA17">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = 7-epi-sesquithujene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15075399">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/15075399"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15075399"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.102">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>sesquithujene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>TPS5-Del1</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.102#SIP86F6F4BCF65D830D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Zea mays, variety Delprim, gives mainly sesquithujene with (S)-beta-bisabolene and (E)-beta-farnesene plus traces of other sesquiterpenoids, cf. EC 4.2.3.55 and EC 4.2.3.47.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The exact product ratio is dependent on which metal ion is present.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15075399"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.102#SIP86F6F4BCF65D830D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = diphosphate + sesquithujene.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15075399">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/15075399"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15075399"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.103">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="4.2.3.n8"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ent-isokaurene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ent-isokaur-15-ene synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.103#SIP40A2011F49CC199E"/>
<rdfs:comment>Two enzymes of the rice sub-species Oryza sativa subsp. indica, OsKSL5 and OsKSL6, produce ent-isokaurene.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A variant of OsKSL5 from the sub-species Oryza sativa subsp. japonica produces ent-pimara-8(14),15-diene instead (cf. EC 4.2.3.30).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17141283"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17456599"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
