<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.107">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(+)-car-3-ene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3-carene cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.107#SIP8CAF237033847947"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme reacts with (3S)-linalyl diphosphate twice as rapidly as geranyl diphosphate, but 25 times as rapidly as (3R)-linalyl diphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is assumed that (3S)-linalyl diphosphate is normally formed as an enzyme bound intermediate in the reaction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the reaction the 5-pro-R hydrogen of geranyl diphosphate is eliminated during cyclopropane ring formation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Picea abies (Norway spruce) and Picea sitchensis (Sitka spruce) terpinolene is also formed.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>See EC 4.2.3.113.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>(+)-car-3-ene is associated with resistance of Picea sitchensis (Sitka spruce) to white pine weevil.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7625832"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8307957"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8373196"/>
