<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.108">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>1,8-cineole synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>1,8-cineole cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.108#SIPF2CA59E600B3F2E0"/>
<rdfs:comment>1,8-cineole is the main product from the enzyme with just traces of other monoterpenoids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The oxygen atom is derived from water.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction proceeds via linalyl diphosphate and alpha-terpineol, the stereochemistry of both depends on the organism.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>However neither intermediate can substitute for geranyl diphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction in Salvia officinalis (sage) proceeds via (-)-(3R)-linalyl diphosphate while that in Arabidopsis (rock cress) proceeds via (+)-(3S)-linalyl diphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8117108"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9614092"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12941302"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15299125"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20399476"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
