<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.117">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="4.2.3.n4"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(-)-camphene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.117#SIPF6A58EBBF39AC8DD"/>
<rdfs:comment>(-)-Camphene is the major product in Abies grandis (grand fir) with traces of other monoterpenoids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Pseudotsuga menziesii (Douglas-fir) there are about equal parts of (-)-camphene and (-)-alpha-pinene with traces of four other monoterpenoids.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Solanum lycopersicum (tomato) tricyclene, beta-myrcene, limonene, and traces of several other monoterpenoids are also formed.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>See also EC 4.2.3.15, EC 4.2.3.16, EC 4.2.3.119 and EC 4.2.3.105.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10441373"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15921711"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15978541"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21813655"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.117#SIPF6A58EBBF39AC8DD">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(2E)-geranyl diphosphate = (1S,4R)-camphene + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
