<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.121">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(+)-alpha-pinene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(+)-alpha-pinene cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.121#SIPA8A975AED8BE9B32"/>
<rdfs:comment>Cyclase I of Salvia officinalis (sage) gives about equal parts (+)-alpha-pinene and (+)-camphene, whereas cyclase III gives about equal parts of (+)-alpha-pinene and (+)-beta-pinene.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>(3R)-linalyl diphosphate can also be used by the enzyme in preference to (3S)-linalyl diphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The 4-pro-R hydrogen of geranyl diphosphate is lost.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>With synthase II of Pinus taeda (loblolly pine) (+)-beta-pinene was the only product.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>See also EC 4.2.3.122 and EC 4.2.3.116.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3392006"/>
