<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.132">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>neoabietadiene synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.132#SIPFFDD84E4CBF59991"/>
<rdfs:comment>Isolated from Abies grandis (grand fir).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This class I enzyme forms about equal proportions of abietadiene, levopimaradiene and neoabietadiene; see also EC 4.2.3.18 and EC 4.2.3.32.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>An X-ray study of this multifunctional enzyme showed that the class I activity is in the alpha domain, while EC 5.5.1.12 activity (a class II activity) is in the beta and gamma domains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Pinus taeda (loblolly pine) the major product is levopimaradiene, with less abietadiene and neoabietadiene.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11112547"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16497345"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22219188"/>
