<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.153">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="4.1.99.21"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(5-formylfuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2-furaldehyde phosphate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>4-HFC-P synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.2.3.153#SIP97A3CCB32C9A0D5A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the reaction in the direction of producing (5-formylfuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate, an intermediate in the biosynthesis of methanofuran.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The sequence of events starts with the removal of a phosphate group, followed by aldol condensation and cyclization.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Methanofuran is a carbon-carrier cofactor involved in the first step of the methanogenic reduction of carbon dioxide by methanogenic archaea.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24977328"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25372812"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25905665"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.2.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.2.3.153#SIP97A3CCB32C9A0D5A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2 D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate = 4-(hydroxymethyl)-2-furancarboxaldehyde phosphate + 2 H2O + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24977328">
