<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.3.1.27">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>threo-3-hydroxy-D-aspartate ammonia-lyase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-threo-3-hydroxyaspartate dehydratase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.3.1.27#SIPA2BCB494F4EB57A4"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, purified from the bacterium Delftia sp. HT23, also has activity against L-threo-3-hydroxyaspartate, L-erythro-3-hydroxyaspartate, and D-serine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Different from EC 4.3.1.20 and EC 4.3.1.16.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Requires a divalent cation such as Mn(2+), Co(2+) or Ni(2+).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20843822"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
