<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.3.3.8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="3.5.1.61"/>
<skos:prefLabel>mimosinase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mimosine amidohydrolase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.3.3.8#SIPC6302D928B97CBDB"/>
<rdfs:comment>A pyridoxal 5'-phosphate protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme degrades the toxic amino acid L-mimosine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It cleaves a carbon-nitrogen bond, releasing 3-hydroxy-4H-pyrid-4-one and an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form, which undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form pyruvate and ammonia.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is thought to have evolved from EC 4.4.1.13.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has been described in both mimosine-producing plants and some bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/SIPA92E437F3CD7880E"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/24351687"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31368041"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/35908235"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.3.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.3.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.3.3.8#SIPC6302D928B97CBDB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + L-mimosine = 3-hydroxy-4H-pyrid-4-one + NH4(+) + pyruvate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/SIPA92E437F3CD7880E">
