<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.4.1.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>homocysteine desulfhydrase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>homocysteine desulfurase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.4.1.2#SIPF28B47BD2C12E3B9"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme cleaves a carbon-sulfur bond, releasing hydrogen sulfide and an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form, which undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form 2-oxobutanoate and ammonia.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The latter reaction, which can occur spontaneously, can also be catalyzed by EC 3.5.99.10.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14917685"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.4.1.2#SIPF28B47BD2C12E3B9">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>H2O + L-homocysteine = 2-oxobutanoate + H(+) + hydrogen sulfide + NH4(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
