<activity rdf:resource="4.4.1.16#SIP1DCA0E9018C5B1B6"/>
<rdfs:comment>Dithiothreitol or 2-sulfanylethan-1-ol (2-mercaptoethanol) can act as the reducing agent in the reaction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from animals does not act on cysteine, serine or chloroalanine, while the enzyme from bacteria shows activity with cysteine (cf. EC 2.8.1.7).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6461656"/>
