<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phosphosulfolactate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(2R)-phospho-3-sulfolactate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PSL synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.4.1.19#SIP7043C8ADD781A3F2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Methanococcus jannaschii catalyzes the Michael addition of sulfite to phosphoenolpyruvate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It specifically requires phosphoenolpyruvate and its broad alkaline pH optimum suggests that it uses sulfite rather than hydrogensulfite.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11830598"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
