<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30962433"/>
<dcterms:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41467-019-09618-8</dcterms:identifier>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.4.1.39">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>C-phycoerythrin alpha-cysteine-82 phycoerythrobilin lyase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.4.1.39#SIPBD369812E95882F7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the cyanobacterium Microchaete diplosiphon, catalyzes the attachment of the phycobilin chromophore (3E)-phycoerythrobilin (PEB) to cysteine 82 of the alpha subunit of the phycobiliprotein C-phycoerythrin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The numbering used here corresponds to the enzyme from Microchaete diplosiphon, and could vary slightly in other organisms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Activity is greatly enhanced in the presence of the chaperone-like protein CpeZ.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction could also be catalyzed by EC 4.4.1.29, but much less efficiently.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21865169"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31173730"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.4.1.39#SIPBD369812E95882F7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>phycoerythrobilin-L-cysteinyl(82)-[C-phycoerythrin alpha-subunit] = (2R,3E)-phycoerythrobilin + apo-L-cysteinyl(82)-[C-phycoerythrin alpha-subunit].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21865169">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/21865169"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21865169"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31173730">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/31173730"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31173730"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.4.1.40">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>C-phycoerythrin beta-cysteine-48/59 phycoerythrobilin lyase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.4.1.40#SIP50769323A1321D8B"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the cyanobacterium Microchaete diplosiphon, catalyzes the attachment of the phycobilin chromophore (3E)-phycoerythrobilin (PEB) to cysteine 48 and 59 of the beta subunits of the phycobiliprotein C-phycoerythrin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme first ligates the A ring of PEB to cysteine-48, followed by the attachment of the D ring to cysteine-59.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The numbering used here corresponds to the enzyme from Microchaete diplosiphon, and could vary slightly in other organisms.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction requires the presence of the chaperone-like protein CpeZ.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21865169"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/31173730"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.4.1.40#SIP50769323A1321D8B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>phycoerythrobilin-L-cysteinyl(48)/L-cysteinyl(59)-[C-phycoerythrin beta-subunit] = (2R,3E)-phycoerythrobilin + apo-L-cysteinyl(48)/L-cysteinyl(59)-[C-phycoerythrin beta-subunit].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21865169">
