<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.6.1.15">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>FAD-AMP lyase (cyclizing)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>FMN cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.6.1.15#SIP1C78EF7B62B0DFCB"/>
<rdfs:comment>While FAD was the best substrate tested the enzyme also splits ribonucleoside diphosphate-X compounds in which X is an acyclic or cyclic monosaccharide or derivative bearing an X-OH group that is able to attack internally the proximal phosphorus with the geometry necessary to form a P=X product; either a five-atom monocyclic phosphodiester or a cis-bicyclic phosphodiester-pyranose fusion.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction is strongly inhibited by ADP or ATP but is unaffected by the presence of the product, cFMN.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9480905"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11695920"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.6.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.6.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.6.1.15#SIP1C78EF7B62B0DFCB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>FAD = AMP + H(+) + riboflavin cyclic-4',5'-phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
