<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.8.1.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-piperazate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.8.1.1#SIP34FCF417FBF8E838"/>
<rdfs:comment>Contains a heme b cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Kutzneria sp. 744, is one of very few enzymes known to result in the formation of an N-N bond.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>(3S)-1,2-diazinane-3-carboxylate (piperazate) is known to be incorporated into assorted secondary products that are produced by nonribosomal peptide synthetase or nonribosomal peptide synthetase/polyketide synthase hybrid pathways, such as the kutznerides, padanamides, himastatins, and sanglifehrins.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/28628093"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.8.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.8.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.8.1.1#SIP34FCF417FBF8E838">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>N(5)-hydroxy-L-ornithine = (3S)-1,2-diazinane-3-carboxylate + H(+) + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
