</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.8.1.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="4.99.1.5"/>
<skos:prefLabel>aliphatic aldoxime dehydratase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>aliphatic aldoxime hydro-lyase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.8.1.2#SIP2B410BDC5984A1AE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Pseudomonas chlororaphis contains Ca(2+) and protoheme IX, the iron of which must be in the form iron(II) for activity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme exhibits a strong preference for aliphatic aldoximes, such as butyraldoxime and acetaldoxime, over aromatic aldoximes, such as pyridine-2-aldoxime, which is a poor substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>No activity was found with the aromatic aldoximes benzaldoxime and pyridine-4-aldoxime.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12773527"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14556637"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16233624"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="4.8.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="4.8.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.8.1.2#SIP2B410BDC5984A1AE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an aliphatic aldoxime = a nitrile + H2O.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
