<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.8.1.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>N-(sulfonatooxy)alkenimidothioic acid sulfate-lyase (epithionitrile-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>epithionitrile-specifier protein</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>epithiospecifier protein</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.8.1.6#SIPBE772CD77A0E28C2"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in the breakdown of glucosinolates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It acts only on aliphatic N-(sulfonatooxy)alkenimidothioic acids produced from omega-alkenyl-glucosinolates, and forms epithionitrile-containing products. cf. EC 4.8.1.5 and EC 4.8.1.7.</rdfs:comment>
