<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.8.1.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phenyl-N-(sulfonatooxy)methanimidothioate sulfolyase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>thiocyanate-forming protein</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.8.1.7#SIP2F8944895702FBF7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the plant Lepidium sativum, is involved in the breakdown of the glucosinolate glucotropaeolin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Depending on the substrate, it can also form simple nitrile- and epithionitrile-containing products. cf. EC 4.8.1.5 and EC 4.8.1.6.</rdfs:comment>
