<rdf:Description rdf:about="4.99.1.10">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>magnesium dechelatase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Mg-dechelatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="4.99.1.10#SIP3D05164333BE7E0C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="4.99.1.10#SIP2322A94D0105903E"/>
<rdfs:comment>SGR has very low activity with chlorophyllide a and none with chlorophyll b.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It acts on chlorophyll a both in its free form and in protein complex.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>SGRL, on the other hand, is more active with chlorophyllide a than with chlorophyll a.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The magnesium formed is scavenged by MCS (metal-chelating substance).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11204197"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15154496"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15890522"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27604697"/>
