<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.1.1.14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>nocardicin-A epimerase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.1.14#SIPEC50DDC164AB664B"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.1.14#SIP65ACC4A48C71E86F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Nocardia uniformis, is involved in the biosynthesis of the monolactam antibiotic nocardicin A.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It catalyzes the epimerization of the amino group at position 9' from (S) configuration to (R).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can act on both isonocardicin A and isonocardicin C, but the in vivo substrate appears to be the latter.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15252031"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15629944"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
