<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.1.3.23">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>UDP-2,3-diacetamido-2,3-dideoxyglucuronic acid 2-epimerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2,3-diacetamido-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucuronic acid 2-epimerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UDP-alpha-D-GlcNAc3NAcA 2-epimerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>UDP-GlcNAc3NAcA 2-epimerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.3.23#SIPB9E49BEBB0DCDE4B"/>
<rdfs:comment>Participates in the biosynthetic pathway for UDP-alpha-D-ManNAc3NAcA (UDP-2,3-diacetamido-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-mannuronic acid), an important precursor of the B-band lipopolysaccharide of Pseudomonas aeroginosa serotype O5 and of the band-A trisaccharide of Bordetella pertussis, both important respiratory pathogens.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Highly specific as UDP-alpha-D-GlcNAc, UDP-alpha-D-GlcNAcA (UDP-2-acetamido-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucuronic acid) and UDP-alpha-D-GlcNAc3NAc (UDP-2,3-diacetamido-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucose) cannot act as substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11526328"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17346239"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.1.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.1.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.1.3.23#SIPB9E49BEBB0DCDE4B">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>UDP-2,3-diacetamido-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucuronate = UDP-2,3-diacetamido-2,3-dideoxy-alpha-D-mannuronate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
