<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is involved in the biosynthetic pathway of dTDP-6-deoxy-alpha-D-allose, which is converted to mycinose after attachment og the aglycones of several macrolide antibiotics, including tylosin, chalcomycin, dihydrochalcomycin, and mycinamicin II.</rdfs:comment>
