<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.1.3.31">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>D-tagatose 3-epimerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ketose 3-epimerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>L-ribulose 3-epimerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.3.31#SIPFA06B6A8BF460AA4"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.3.31#SIPC4EEEC2CB1603A72"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.3.31#SIP3DD1538A0B8F9265"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.3.31#SIPB6EF57DB5C7CE952"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes isolated from the bacteria Pseudomonas cichorii, Pseudomonas sp. ST-24, Rhodobacter sphaeroides and Mesorhizobium loti catalyze the epimerization of various ketoses at the C3 position, interconverting D-fructose and D-psicose, D-tagatose and D-sorbose, D-ribulose and D-xylulose, and L-ribulose and L-xylulose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The specificity depends on the species.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17936787"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19205890"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23470755"/>
