<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>NAD(P)H-hydrate epimerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>NAD(P)HX epimerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.99.6#SIPFCCD815B026B87A7"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.1.99.6#SIP35B28CA12CB6255F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can use either (R)-NADH-hydrate or (R)-NADPH-hydrate as a substrate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Its physiological role is to convert the (R) forms to the (S) forms, which could then be restored to active dinucleotides by EC 4.2.1.93.</rdfs:comment>
