<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.3.1.5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>xylose isomerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-xylose aldose-ketose-isomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-xylose isomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-xylose ketoisomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>D-xylose ketol-isomerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.1.5#SIPCFCD2E54DCD0C4D6"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.1.5#SIPD6B86653BFB2621D"/>
<rdfs:comment>Contains two divalent metal ions, preferably magnesium, located at different metal-binding sites within the active site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the interconversion of aldose and ketose sugars with broad substrate specificity.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme binds the closed form of its sugar substrate (in the case of xylose and glucose, only the alpha anomer) and catalyzes ring opening to generate a form of open-chain conformation that is coordinated to one of the metal sites.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Isomerization proceeds via a hydride-shift mechanism.</rdfs:comment>
