<skos:altLabel>6-phospho-3-hexulose isomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>PHI</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phospho-3-hexuloisomerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.1.27#SIPE90F7F8EC5DBDFB6"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, along with EC 4.1.2.43, plays a key role in the ribulose-monophosphate cycle of formaldehyde fixation, which is present in many microorganisms that are capable of utilizing C1-compounds.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The hyperthermophilic and anaerobic archaeon Pyrococcus horikoshii OT3 constitutively produces a bifunctional enzyme that sequentially catalyzes the reactions of EC 4.1.2.43 and this enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
