<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.3.2.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-hydroxymuconate tautomerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>4-oxalocrotonate isomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>4-oxalocrotonate tautomerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.2.6#SIP19F98E33A2F204FD"/>
<rdfs:comment>Involved in the meta-cleavage pathway for the degradation of phenols, modified phenols and catechols.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enol form (2Z,4E)-2-hydroxyhexa-2,4-dienedioate is produced as part of this pathway and is converted to the keto form (3E)-2-oxohex-3-enedioate by the enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Another keto form, (4E)-2-oxohex-4-enedioate (4-oxalocrotonate), was originally thought to be produced by the enzyme but later shown to be produced non-enzymatically.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8547259"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8547260"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17902707"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19717587"/>
