<skos:prefLabel>ascopyrone tautomerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>1,5-anhydro-D-glycero-hex-3-en-2-ulose tautomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>APM tautomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>APTM</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ascopyrone intramolecular oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ascopyrone isomerase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ascopyrone P tautomerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.2.7#SIP446203AC9D577228"/>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes one of the steps in the anhydrofructose pathway, which leads to the degradation of glycogen and starch via 1,5-anhydro-D-fructose.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The other enzymes involved in this pathway are EC 4.2.1.110, EC 4.2.1.111 and EC 4.2.2.13.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Ascopyrone P is an anti-oxidant.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15110094"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16822618"/>
