</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.3.3.19">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-[(4R)-4-hydroxycyclohexa-1,5-dien-1-yl]-2-oxopropanoate isomerase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.3.19#SIP399057514A529FDA"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacillus subtilis, is involved in the biosynthesis of the nonribosomally synthesized dipeptide antibiotic bacilysin, composed of L-alanine and L-anticapsin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can interconvert the (E) isomer formed in the reaction into the (Z) isomer, although this isomerization is not part of the pathway leading to bacilysin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20052993"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22483065"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23317005"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.3.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.3.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
