<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.3.3.21">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>Delta(3,5)-Delta(2,4)-dienoyl-CoA isomerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3,5-tetradecadienoyl-CoA isomerase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.3.21#SIP96743F001BB5420A"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in an alternative degradation route of fatty acids with cis-double bonds on odd-number carbons such as oleate and linoleate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The main physiological substrate is (3E,5Z)-tetradeca-3,5-dienoyl-CoA, but other (3E,5Z)-dienoyl-CoAs with varying carbon chain lengths are also substrates.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9417087"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9739087"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10381339"/>
