<activity rdf:resource="5.3.99.12#SIP54B978183F9423F3"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.99.12#SIPB90DE8EA7315FA28"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.3.99.12#SIPB51FD79F4F2FBF27"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is responsible for production of the irritating lachrymatory factor that is released by onions and related species when they are chopped.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It acts on the product of EC 4.4.1.4.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Allium cepa (onion) acts on (E)-prop-1-en-1-SO-peroxol and produces (Z)-propanethial oxide, while the enzyme from Allium siculum (honey garlic) acts on (E)-but-1-en-1-SO-peroxol and produces (Z)-butanethial oxide.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2384686"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12384686"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18583530"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20047275"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.3.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.3.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
