<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="2.7.5.3"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="5.4.2.1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phosphoglycerate mutase (2,3-diphosphoglycerate-independent)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2,3-diphosphoglycerate-independent phosphoglycerate mutase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cofactor independent phosphoglycerate mutase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphoglycerate phosphomutase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>phosphoglyceromutase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.4.2.12#SIP0266882B831B162C"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzymes from higher plants, algae, some fungi, nematodes, sponges, coelenterates, myriapods, arachnids, echinoderms, archaea and some bacteria (particularly Gram-positive) have maximum activity in the absence of 2,3-bisphospho-D-glycerate. cf. EC 5.4.2.11.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction involves a phosphotransferase reaction to serine followed by transfer back to the glycerate at the other position.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Both metal ions are involved in the reaction.</rdfs:comment>
