<skos:prefLabel>glutamate 2,3-aminomutase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.4.3.9#SIP66ED0AB9344EC04E"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is a member of the 'AdoMet radical' (radical SAM) family.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It contains pyridoxal phosphate and a [4Fe-4S] cluster, which is coordinated by 3 cysteines and binds an exchangeable S-adenosyl-L-methionine molecule.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>During the reaction cycle, the AdoMet forms a 5'-deoxyadenosyl radical, which is regenerated at the end of the reaction.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17222594"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.4.3.-"/>
