</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.4.4.5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>9,12-octadecadienoate 8-hydroperoxide 8R-isomerase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxy-9,12-octadecadienoate mutase ((5S,8R,9Z,12Z)-5,8-dihydroxy-9,12-octadecadienoate-forming)</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.4.4.5#SIP845E411785E52100"/>
<rdfs:comment>The bifunctional enzyme from Aspergillus nidulans uses different heme domains to catalyze two separate reactions.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Linoleic acid is oxidized within the N-terminal heme peroxidase domain to (8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate (cf. EC 1.13.11.60), which is subsequently isomerized to (5S,8R,9Z,12Z)-5,8-dihydroxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate within the C-terminal P450 heme thiolate domain.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19286665"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20045744"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21130068"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.4.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.4.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.4.4.5#SIP845E411785E52100">
