<skos:prefLabel>5-(carboxyamino)imidazole ribonucleotide mutase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N(5)-CAIR mutase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N(5)-carboxyaminoimidazole ribonucleotide mutase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.4.99.18#SIP6D3D13848799C902"/>
<rdfs:comment>In eubacteria, fungi and plants, this enzyme, along with EC 6.3.4.18, is required to carry out the single reaction catalyzed by EC 4.1.1.21 in vertebrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the absence of EC 6.3.2.6, the reaction is reversible.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrate is readily converted into 5-amino-1-(5-phospho-D-ribosyl)imidazole by non-enzymic decarboxylation.</rdfs:comment>
