<activity rdf:resource="5.4.99.55#SIP2961A1FDC84EB414"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from tomato (Solanum lycopersicum) gives 48% delta-amyrin, 18% alpha-amyrin, 13% beta-amyrin and traces of three or four other triterpenoid alcohols.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>See also EC 5.4.99.40 and EC 5.4.99.39.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21059824"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.4.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.4.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.4.99.55#SIP2961A1FDC84EB414">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(S)-2,3-epoxysqualene = delta-amyrin.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
