<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.4.99.58">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>methylornithine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.4.99.58#SIPC0B9374A470DF1E8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is a member of the superfamily of S-adenosyl-L-methionine-dependent radical (radical AdoMet) enzymes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Binds a [4Fe-4S] cluster that is coordinated by 3 cysteines and an exchangeable S-adenosyl-L-methionine molecule.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction is part of the biosynthesis pathway of pyrrolysine, a naturally occurring amino acid found in some archaeal methyltransferases.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21455182"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22095926"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.4.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.4.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.4.99.58#SIPC0B9374A470DF1E8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>L-lysine = (3R)-3-methyl-D-ornithine.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
