<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.4.99.64">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="5.3.3.20"/>
<skos:prefLabel>2-hydroxyisobutanoyl-CoA mutase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.4.99.64#SIP098C1623884FE8FB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Aquincola tertiaricarbonis, uses radical chemistry to rearrange the positions of both a methyl group and a hydroxyl group.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It consists of two subunits, the smaller one containing a cobalamin cofactor.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It plays a central role in the degradation of assorted substrates containing a tert-butyl moiety.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22433853"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/25720495"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.4.99.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.4.99.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.4.99.64#SIP098C1623884FE8FB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>2-hydroxyisobutanoyl-CoA = (3S)-3-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
