<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.5.1.22">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(-)-bornyl diphosphate synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>(-)-bornyl pyrophosphate cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>bornyl pyrophosphate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.5.1.22#SIPE47A5FFBFB3424F9"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Tanacetum vulgare (tansey) can also use (3S)-linalyl diphosphate or more slowly neryl diphosphate in vitro.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The reaction proceeds via isomeration of geranyl diphosphate to (3S)-linalyl diphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The oxygen and phosphorus originally linked to C-1 of geranyl diphosphate end up linked to C-2 of (-)-bornyl diphosphate. cf. EC 5.5.1.8.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2178556"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3970524"/>
