<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.6.1.6">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="3.6.3.49"/>
<skos:prefLabel>channel-conductance-controlling ATPase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>CFTR</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cystic-fibrosis membrane-conductance-regulating protein</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.6.1.6#SIP601945F38EE1BF9C"/>
<rdfs:comment>ABC-type (ATP-binding cassette-type) ATPase, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is found in animals, and in humans its absence brings about cystic fibrosis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike most of the ABC transporters, chloride pumping is not directly coupled to ATP hydrolysis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Instead, the passive flow of anions through the channel is gated by cycles of ATP binding and hydrolysis by the ATP-binding domains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is also involved in the functioning of other transmembrane channels.</rdfs:comment>
