<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.6.1.7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="3.6.4.9"/>
<skos:prefLabel>chaperonin ATPase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>chaperonin</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.6.1.7#SIP002D43C4C35378BA"/>
<rdfs:comment>Multisubunit proteins with 2x7 (Type I, in most cells) or 2x8 (Type II, in Archaea) ATP-binding sites involved in maintaining an unfolded polypeptide structure before folding or entry into mitochondria and chloroplasts.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Molecular masses of subunits ranges from 10-90 kDa.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>They are a subclass of molecular chaperones that are related to EC 5.6.1.5.</rdfs:comment>
