<skos:prefLabel>myosin ATPase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.6.1.8#SIP642872660B67D816"/>
<rdfs:comment>Proteins of the contractile apparatus of muscle and nonmuscle cells; myosin molecule consists of two heavy chains (about 200 kDa) and two pairs of light chains (15-27 kDa).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The head region of the heavy chain contains actin- and ATP-binding sites.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>ATP hydrolysis provides energy for actomyosin contraction.</rdfs:comment>
