<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP-dependent breakage, passage and rejoining of double-stranded DNA.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6267993">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/6267993"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6267993"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.6.2.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>DNA 5'-3' helicase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>5' to 3' DNA helicase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>replication fork helicase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>replicative DNA helicase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="5.6.2.3#SIP83452CBBF4DF9E44"/>
<activity rdf:resource="5.6.2.3#SIP05AEEC61C40E23D7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The activity is stimulated by DNA polymerase III.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>As the lagging ssDNA is created, it becomes coated with S Single-Stranded DNA Binding protein (SSB).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Once every 500-2000 nucleotides, primase is stimulated by DnaB helicase to synthesize a primer at the replication fork.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This primer is elongated by the lagging strand half of DNA polymerase III holoenzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8381400"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8626772"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12050116"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12058079"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15220459"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23839989"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="5.6.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="5.6.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.6.2.3#SIP83452CBBF4DF9E44">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>Couples ATP hydrolysis with the unwinding of duplex DNA at the replication fork by translocating in the 5'-3' direction. This creates two antiparallel DNA single strands (ssDNA). The leading ssDNA polymer is the template for DNA polymerase III holoenzyme which synthesizes a continuous strand.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="5.6.2.3#SIP05AEEC61C40E23D7">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + H2O = ADP + H(+) + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
