<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.1.2.1">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>D-alanine--(R)-lactate ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.1.2.1#SIP9C59E33210A927F7"/>
<rdfs:comment>The product of this enzyme, the depsipeptide D-alanyl-(R)-lactate, can be incorporated into the peptidoglycan pentapeptide instead of the usual D-alanyl-D-alanine dipeptide, which is formed by EC 6.3.2.4.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The resulting peptidoglycan does not bind the glycopeptide antibiotics vancomycin and teicoplanin, conferring resistance on the bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1931965"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7957913"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9303405"/>
