<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.2.1.19">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>long-chain-fatty-acid--protein ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>acyl-protein synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.2.1.19#SIPC44F78AFB6E4F4FE"/>
<rdfs:comment>Together with a hydrolase component (EC 3.1.2.2/3.1.2.14) and a reductase component (EC 1.2.1.50), this enzyme forms a multienzyme fatty acid reductase complex that produces the long-chain aldehyde substrate of the bacterial luciferase enzyme (EC 1.14.14.3).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme activates free long-chain fatty acids, generated by the action of the transferase component, forming a fatty acyl-AMP intermediate, followed by the transfer of the acyl group to an internal L-cysteine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It then transfers the acyl group to EC 1.2.1.50.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2023262"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3968067"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7085612"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8941351"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
