</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.2.1.66">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>glyine--[glycyl-carrier protein] ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.2.1.66#SIPB482C28071DFE76F"/>
<rdfs:comment>The adenylation domain of the enzyme catalyzes the activation of glycine to (glycyl)adenylate, followed by the transfer of the activated compound to the free thiol of a phosphopantetheine arm of a peptidyl-carrier protein domain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The peptidyl-carrier protein domain may be part of the same protein (as in the case of DhbF in bacillibactin biosynthesis), or of a different protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This activity is often found as part of a larger non-ribosomal peptide synthase.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11112781"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17981978"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.2.1.66#SIPB482C28071DFE76F">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + glycine + holo-[peptidyl-carrier protein] = AMP + diphosphate + glycyl-[peptidyl-carrier protein].</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
