<rdfs:comment>The adenylation domain of the enzyme catalyzes the activation of L-tryptophan to (L-tryptophyl)adenylate, followed by the transfer of the activated compound to the free thiol of a phosphopantetheine arm of a peptidyl-carrier protein domain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The peptidyl-carrier protein domain may be part of the same protein, or of a different protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This activity is often found as part of a larger non-ribosomal peptide synthase.</rdfs:comment>
