<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.2.1.n2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>amino acid--[acyl-carrier-protein] ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.2.1.n2#SIP43C9A0242870706E"/>
<rdfs:comment>Catalyzes the ATP-dependent activation of L-alanine, and to a lesser extent of L-glycine and L-serine, and their transfer to the phosphopantetheine cofactor covalently attached to a vicinal carrier protein.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>May participate in nonribosomal peptide synthesis or related processes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>L-proline and L-glutamate are very poor substrates whereas D-amino acids are not substrates for ATP-dependent activation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Does not display tRNA aminoacylation activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20663952"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.2.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.2.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.2.1.n2#SIP43C9A0242870706E">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>an L-alpha-amino acid + ATP + holo-[ACP] = AMP + an L-alpha-aminoacyl-[ACP] + diphosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20663952">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
