<activity rdf:resource="6.3.1.2#SIP71A54EA4080BC562"/>
<rdfs:comment>Glutamine synthetase, which catalyzes the incorporation of ammonium into glutamate, is a key enzyme of nitrogen metabolism found in all domains of life.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Several types have been described, differing in their oligomeric structures and cofactor requirements.</rdfs:comment>
