<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.1.13">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="6.1.1.n1"/>
<skos:prefLabel>L-cysteine:1D-myo-inositol 2-amino-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranoside ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>MshC ligase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>mycothiol ligase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.1.13#SIPD2319C180A7A9639"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is a key enzyme in the biosynthesis of mycothiol, a small molecular weight thiol found in Mycobacteria spp. and other actinomycetes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Mycothiol plays a fundamental role in these organisms by helping to provide protection from the effects of reactive oxygen species and electrophiles, including many antibiotics.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme may represent a novel target for new classes of antituberculars.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16908186"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17848100"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19053270"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.1.13#SIPD2319C180A7A9639">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>1D-myo-inositol 2-amino-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranoside + ATP + L-cysteine = 1D-myo-inositol 2-(L-cysteinylamino)-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranoside + AMP + diphosphate + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16908186">
