<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.1.14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="6.3.2.22"/>
<skos:prefLabel>diphthine--ammonia ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>diphthamide synthase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>diphthamide synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.1.14#SIPACDCB42342C6241A"/>
<rdfs:comment>This amidase catalyzes the last step in the conversion of an L-histidine residue in the translation elongation factor translation elongation factor 2 to diphthamide.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This factor is found in all archaebacteria and eukaryotes, but not in eubacteria, and is the target of bacterial toxins such as the diphtheria toxin and the Pseudomonas exotoxin A (see EC 2.4.2.36).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrate of the enzyme, diphthine, is produced by EC 2.1.1.98.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3346227"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23169644"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.1.14#SIPACDCB42342C6241A">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + diphthine-[translation elongation factor 2] + NH4(+) = AMP + diphosphate + diphthamide-[translation elongation factor 2] + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3346227">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/3346227"/>
