<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.1.18">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>gamma-glutamylanilide synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.1.18#SIPFFADAC0FF6C23791"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Acinetobacter sp. YAA, catalyzes the first step in the degradation of aniline.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It can also accept chlorinated and methylated forms of aniline, preferrably in the o- and p-positions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23893114"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
