<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.1.21">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>phosphoribosylglycinamide formyltransferase 2</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>5'-phosphoribosylglycinamide transformylase 2</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GART2</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GAR transformylase 2</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>GAR transformylase T</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>glycinamide ribonucleotide transformylase 2</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.1.21#SIPCBFE38B4E9E2D5B5"/>
<rdfs:comment>Two enzymes are known to catalyze the third step in de novo purine biosynthesis.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme requires ATP and utilizes formate, which is provided by the hydrolysis of 10-formyltetrahydrofolate by EC 3.5.1.10.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The other enzyme, EC 2.1.2.2, utilizes 10-formyltetrahydrofolate directly.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Formyl phosphate is formed during catalysis as an intermediate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli can also catalyze the activity of EC 2.7.2.1.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8117714"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8226647"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8501063"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9184151"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10913290"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/27113361"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.1.21#SIPCBFE38B4E9E2D5B5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + formate + N(1)-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)glycinamide = ADP + H(+) + N(2)-formyl-N(1)-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)glycinamide + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
