<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.11">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>carnosine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>carnosine synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.11#SIP5AC4EBB264973944"/>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.11#SIPA13D683863D7077C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.11#SIPBC55BF170F99058C"/>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.11#SIPCE267A0A6FEE5B94"/>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.11#SIPF167A140D97638C7"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme was thought to form AMP, but studies with highly purified enzyme proved that it forms ADP.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Carnosine is a dipeptide that is present at high concentrations in skeletal muscle and the olfactory bulb of vertebrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is also found in the skeletal muscle of some invertebrates.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also catalyze the formation of homocarnosine from 4-aminobutyrate and L-histidine, with much lower activity.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4988625"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14404206"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16748858"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20097752"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
