<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>enterobactin synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>2,3-dihydroxybenzoate--serine ligase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-serine synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.14#SIPB5BA9F3D2C940BC3"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme complex catalyzes the conversion of three molecules each of 2,3-dihydroxybenzoate and L-serine to form the siderophore enterobactin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Escherichia coli the complex is formed by EntB (an aryl carrier protein that has to be activated by 4'-phosphopantetheine), EntD (a phosphopantetheinyl transferase that activates EntB), EntE (catalyzes the ATP-dependent condensation of 2,3-dihydroxybenzoate and holo-EntB to form the covalently arylated form of EntB), and EntF (a four domain protein that catalyzes the activation of L-serine by ATP, the condensation of the activated L-serine with the activated 2,3-dihydroxybenzoate, and the trimerization of three such moieties to a single enterobactin molecule).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1826089"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2139796"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2531000"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4966114"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9485415"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10375542"/>
