<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>cyanophycin synthase (L-aspartate-adding)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cyanophycin synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>multi-L-arginyl-poly-L-aspartate synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.29#SIPAEDA75B9EC8015FF"/>
<rdfs:comment>Both this enzyme and EC 6.3.2.30 are required for the elongation of cyanophycin, which is a protein-like cell inclusion that is unique to cyanobacteria and acts as a temporary nitrogen store.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Both enzymes are found in the same protein but have different active sites.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Both L-Asp and L-Arg must be present before either enzyme will display significant activity.</rdfs:comment>
