<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.44">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="6.3.2.n5"/>
<skos:prefLabel>pantoate--beta-alanine ligase (ADP-forming)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pantoate--beta-alanine ligase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>pantothenate synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.44#SIP31B22A85F29878BB"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Methanosarcina mazei, is involved in the biosynthesis of pantothenate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is different from EC 6.3.2.1, the AMP-forming pantoate-beta-alanine ligase found in bacteria and eukaryota.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18422645"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.44#SIP31B22A85F29878BB">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>(R)-pantoate + ATP + beta-alanine = (R)-pantothenate + ADP + H(+) + phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18422645">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Citation"/>
<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/pubmed/18422645"/>
<foaf:primaryTopicOf rdf:resource="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18422645"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.45">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>UDP-N-acetylmuramate L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioate ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>murein peptide ligase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.45#SIP684D0B6C29DC0011"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes the reincorporation into peptidoglycan of the tripeptide L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-2,6-meso-diaminoheptanedioate released during the maturation and constant remodeling of this bacterial cell wall polymer that occur during cell growth and division.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme can also use the tetrapeptide L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioyl-D-alanine or the pentapeptide L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine in vivo and in vitro.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8808921"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17384195"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.45#SIP684D0B6C29DC0011">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-diaminoheptanedioate + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramate = ADP + H(+) + phosphate + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramoyl-L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
