<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.59">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>3-methyl-D-ornithine--L-lysine ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>3-methylornithine--L-lysine ligase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>N(6)-[(2R,3R)-3-methylornithyl]-L-lysine synthase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.59#SIP9B6373C20F644BE9"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of L-pyrrolysine, a naturally occurring, genetically coded amino acid found in some methanogenic archaea and a few bacterial species.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>L-pyrrolysine is present in several methyltransferases that are involved in methyl transfer from methylated amine compounds to coenzyme M.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21455182"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/21525873"/>
