<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.2.62">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>beta-tubulin-glutamate ligase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-tubulin polyglutamylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.62#SIP7BDA02A07C550A24"/>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.62#SIPB80DC750D567F5DF"/>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.62#SIP545DA38C3184FCE0"/>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.2.62#SIPA7F363A6770F6C22"/>
<rdfs:comment>The eukaryotic tubulin proteins, which polymerize into microtubules, are highly modified by the addition of side-chains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The polyglutamylation reaction catalyzed by this group of enzymes consists of two biochemically distinct steps: initiation and elongation.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Initiation comprises the formation of an isopeptide bond with the gamma-carboxyl group of the glutamate acceptor site, whereas elongation consists of the addition of glutamate residues linked by regular peptide bonds to the gamma-linked residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes enzymes that act on beta-tubulins and other proteins with glutamate-rich regions but not on alpha-tubulins.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9622491"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10564646"/>
