<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.3.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>(carboxyethyl)arginine beta-lactam-synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>beta-lactam synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.3.4#SIPF52E63C22D11ECC4"/>
<rdfs:comment>Forms part of the pathway for the biosythesis of the beta-lactamase inhibitor clavulanate in Streptomyces clavuligerus.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It has been proposed that L-N(2)-(2-carboxyethyl)arginine is first converted into an acyl-AMP by reaction with ATP and loss of diphosphate, and that the beta-lactam ring is then formed by the intramolecular attack of the beta-nitrogen on the activated carboxy group.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9689037"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12413541"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.3.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.3.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.3.4#SIPF52E63C22D11ECC4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + N(2)-(2-carboxyethyl)-L-arginine = AMP + deoxyamidinoproclavaminate + diphosphate + H(+).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
