<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.4.22">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>tRNA(Ile)(2)-agmatinylcytidine synthase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tRNA(Ile)-2-agmatinylcytidine synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tRNA(Ile)-agm(2)C synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tRNA(Ile)-agmatidine synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.4.22#SIP37E41F7330073B4C"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the archaeon Archaeoglobus fulgidus modifies the wobble base of the CAU anticodon of the archaeal tRNA(Ile)(2) at the oxo group in position 2 of cytidine(34).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This modification is crucial for accurate decoding of the genetic code.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In bacteria EC 6.3.4.19, catalyzes the modification of [tRNA(Ile)(2)]-cytidine(34) to [tRNA(Ile)(2)]-lysidine(34).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/20139989"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22002222"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22102245"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.4.22#SIP37E41F7330073B4C">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>agmatine + ATP + cytidine(34) in tRNA(Ile2) + H2O = 2-agmatinylcytidine(34) in tRNA(Ile2) + AMP + 2 H(+) + 2 phosphate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
