<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.5.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>asparagine synthase (glutamine-hydrolyzing)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>AS-B</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>asparagine synthetase (glutamine-hydrolyzing)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>asparagine synthetase B</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>glutamine-dependent asparagine synthetase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.3.5.4#SIP37E7ED6E5E48C83D"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Escherichia coli has two active sites that are connected by an intramolecular ammonia tunnel.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme catalyzes three distinct chemical reactions: glutamine hydrolysis to yield ammonia takes place in the N-terminal domain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The C-terminal active site mediates both the synthesis of a beta-aspartyl-AMP intermediate and its subsequent reaction with ammonia.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The ammonia released is channeled to the other active site to yield asparagine.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/4295091"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7907328"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9559053"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10587437"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10852734"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11395405"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12706338"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.3.5.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.3.5.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.3.5.4#SIP37E7ED6E5E48C83D">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>ATP + H2O + L-aspartate + L-glutamine = AMP + diphosphate + H(+) + L-asparagine + L-glutamate.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
