<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.4.1.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>acetyl-CoA carboxylase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.4.1.2#SIP8EA84E3FF4B2E8B4"/>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme is a multi-domain polypeptide that catalyzes three different activities - a biotin carboxyl-carrier protein (BCCP), a biotin carboxylase that catalyzes the transfer of a carboxyl group from hydrogencarbonate to the biotin molecule carried by the carrier protein, and the transfer of the carboxyl group from biotin to acetyl-CoA, forming malonyl-CoA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In some organisms these activities are catalyzed by separate enzymes (see EC 6.3.4.14 and EC 2.1.3.15).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The carboxylation of the carrier protein requires ATP, while the transfer of the carboxyl group to acetyl-CoA does not.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7628470"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/13905314"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14317957"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/14317958"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16854592"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17223360"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.4.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.4.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
