<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.5.1.4">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>RNA 3'-terminal-phosphate cyclase (ATP)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RNA-3'-phosphate cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RNA cyclase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.5.1.4#SIPF937038F131454FE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme converts the 3'-terminal phosphate of various RNA substrates into the 2',3'-cyclic phosphodiester in an ATP-dependent reaction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Catalysis occurs by a three-step mechanism, starting with the activation of the enzyme by ATP, forming a phosphoramide bond between adenylate and a histidine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The adenylate group is then transferred to the 3'-phosphate terminus of the substrate, forming the capped structure [RNA]-3'-(5'-diphosphoadenosine).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Finally, the enzyme catalyzes an attack of the vicinal O-2' on the 3'-phosphorus, which results in formation of cyclic phosphate and release of the adenylate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme also has a polynucleotide 5' adenylation activity. cf. EC 6.5.1.5.</rdfs:comment>
