<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.5.1.5">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>RNA 3'-terminal-phosphate cyclase (GTP)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>RNA-3'-phosphate cyclase (GTP)</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="6.5.1.5#SIPD41F58DD8BD91EC8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, which is specific for GTP, was characterized from the archaeon Pyrococcus furiosus.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme converts the 3'-terminal phosphate of various RNA substrates into the 2',3'-cyclic phosphodiester in a GTP-dependent reaction.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Catalysis occurs by a three-step mechanism, starting with the activation of the enzyme by GTP, forming a phosphoramide bond between guanylate and a histidine residue.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The guanylate group is then transferred to the 3'-phosphate terminus of the substrate, forming the capped structure [RNA]-3'-(5'-diphosphoguanosine).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Finally, the enzyme catalyzes an attack of the vicinal O-2' on the 3'-phosphorus, which results in formation of cyclic phosphate and release of the guanylate. cf. EC 6.5.1.4.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22074260"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="6.5.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="6.5.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="6.5.1.5#SIPD41F58DD8BD91EC8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a 3'-end 3'-phospho-ribonucleotide-RNA + GTP = a 3'-end 2',3'-cyclophospho-ribonucleotide-RNA + diphosphate + GMP.</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/22074260">
