<replaces rdf:resource="1.6.1.5"/>
<skos:prefLabel>proton-translocating NAD(P)(+) transhydrogenase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.1.1.1#SIPD860CE9055DB3AD8"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is a membrane bound proton-translocating pyridine nucleotide transhydrogenase that couples the reversible reduction of NADP by NADH to an inward proton translocation across the membrane.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the bacterium Escherichia coli the enzyme provides a major source of cytosolic NADPH.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Detoxification of reactive oxygen species in mitochondria by glutathione peroxidases depends on NADPH produced by this enzyme.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/3884596"/>
