<rdf:Description rdf:about="7.1.1.3">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.10.3.10"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ubiquinol oxidase (H(+)-transporting)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cytochrome bb3 oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cytochrome bo3 oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cytochrome bo oxidase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.1.1.3#SIP2AA0A0988D4F837A"/>
<rdfs:comment>Contains a dinuclear center comprising heme and copper.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This terminal oxidase enzyme generates proton motive force by two mechanisms: (1) transmembrane charge separation resulting from utilizing protons and electrons originating from opposite sides of the membrane to generate water, and (2) active pumping of protons across the membrane.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The bioenergetic efficiency (the number of charges driven across the membrane per electron used to reduce oxygen to water) of enzymes that have been characterized so far is 2. cf. EC 7.1.1.7.</rdfs:comment>
