<rdf:Description rdf:about="7.1.1.8">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="1.10.2.2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>quinol--cytochrome-c reductase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>complex III (mitochondrial electron transport)</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cytochrome bc1 complex</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ubiquinol--cytochrome-c reductase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>ubiquinone--cytochrome-c oxidoreductase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.1.1.8#SIP2090A1341C2C8802"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, often referred to as the cytochrome bc1 complex or complex III, is the third complex in the electron transport chain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It is present in the mitochondria of all aerobic eukaryotes and in the inner membranes of most bacteria.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The mammalian enzyme contains cytochromes b-562, b-566 and c1, and a 2-iron ferredoxin.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Depending on the organism and physiological conditions, the enzyme extrudes either two or four protons from the cytoplasmic to the non-cytoplasmic compartment (cf. EC 1.6.99.3).</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/597492"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/788795"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/6267990"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8647852"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/9535866"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10358017"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="7.1.1.-"/>
