<rdf:Description rdf:about="7.1.1.12">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>succinate dehydrogenase (electrogenic, proton-motive force generating)</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.1.1.12#SIP1E2D3FAFE3936D89"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is very similar to EC 1.3.5.1 but differs by containing two heme molecules (located in the membrane anchor component) in addition to FAD and three iron-sulfur clusters.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Unlike EC 1.3.5.1, this enzyme catalyzes an electrogenic reaction, enabled by electron-bifurcation via the heme molecules.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the direction of succinate oxidation by menaquinone, which is endergonic, the reaction is driven by the transmembrane electrochemical proton potential.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In the direction of fumarate reduction, the electrogenic electron transfer reaction is compensated by transmembrane proton transfer pathway known as the E-pathway, which results in overall electroneutrality.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/12409197"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17154542"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/18793177"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/23466335"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/30297797"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="7.1.1.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="7.1.1.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="7.1.1.12#SIP1E2D3FAFE3936D89">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Catalytic_Activity"/>
<rdfs:label>a menaquinone + 2 H(+)(out) + succinate = a menaquinol + fumarate + 2 H(+)(in).</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>
