<skos:prefLabel>ABC-type ferric hydroxamate transporter</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>iron(III) hydroxamate ABC transporter</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>iron(III) hydroxamate transporting ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.2.2.16#SIP7C3D7EB33FC7BD66"/>
<rdfs:comment>An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A bacterial enzyme that interacts with an extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and mediates the import of Fe(3+)-complexed hydroxamate siderophores such as coprogen, ferrichrome and the ferric hydroxamate antibiotic, albomycin.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1830209"/>
