<replaces rdf:resource="7.1.3.2"/>
<skos:prefLabel>Na(+)-exporting diphosphatase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>Na(+)-translocating membrane pyrophosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>sodium-translocating pyrophosphatase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.2.3.1#SIPF40770E308BC57B2"/>
<rdfs:comment>Requires Na(+) and K(+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This enzyme, found in some bacteria and archaea, couples the energy from diphosphate hydrolysis to active sodium translocation across the membrane.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme is electrogenic, as the Na(+) transport results in generation of a positive potential in the inner side of the membrane.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/15697234"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/17605473"/>
