<rdf:Description rdf:about="7.2.4.2">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="4.1.1.3"/>
<skos:prefLabel>oxaloacetate decarboxylase (Na(+) extruding)</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oxalacetic acid decarboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oxalate beta-decarboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>oxaloacetate beta-decarboxylase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.2.4.2#SIPF5EDF9240414CEAD"/>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Klebsiella aerogenes is a biotinyl protein and also decarboxylates glutaconyl-CoA and methylmalonyl-CoA.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The process is accompanied by the extrusion of two sodium ions from cells.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Some animal enzymes require Mn(2+).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Differs from EC 4.1.1.112 (oxaloacetate decarboxylase) for which there is no evidence for involvement in Na(+) transport.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7016536"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7037395"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="7.2.4.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="7.2.4.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
