<skos:prefLabel>ABC-type sulfate transporter</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>sulfate ABC transporter</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>sulfate-transporting ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.3.2.3#SIPD251ED0EA49078E9"/>
<activity rdf:resource="7.3.2.3#SIP8E1E81EE81CE6AEC"/>
<rdfs:comment>An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Escherichia coli can interact with either of two periplasmic binding proteins and mediates the high affinity uptake of sulfate and thiosulfate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>May also be involved in the uptake of selenite, selenate and possibly molybdate.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Does not undergo phosphorylation during the transport.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/7569321"/>
