<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<replaces rdf:resource="3.6.3.55"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ABC-type tungstate transporter</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tungstate-importing ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tungstate-specific ABC transporter</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>tungstate transporter</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.3.2.6#SIPA890E422B040EEBF"/>
<rdfs:comment>An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Pyrococcus furiosus, the Gram-positive bacterium Eubacterium acidaminophilum and the Gram-negative bacterium Campylobacter jejuni, interacts with an extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and mediates the import of tungstate into the cell for incorporation into tungsten-dependent enzymes.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/11292832"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/16952940"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/19818021"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="7.3.2.-"/>
<skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="7.3.2.-"/>
</rdf:Description>
