<replaces rdf:resource="3.6.3.16"/>
<skos:prefLabel>arsenite-transporting ATPase</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>arsenical pump-driving ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>arsenical resistance ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>arsenite-translocating ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.3.2.7#SIP1611DE6FF173806E"/>
<rdfs:comment>This bacterial transporter does not belong to the ABC superfamily, and instead is a member of its own family, referred to as the Ars family.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme usually contains two subunits where one (with 12 membrane-spanning segments) forms the 'channel' part and the other (occurring in pairs peripherally to the membrane) contains the ATP-binding site.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>It forms an arsenite efflux pump that removes arsenite from the cytoplasm, and can also remove antimonite anions.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/1703401"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2484581"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8674982"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10089335"/>
