<skos:prefLabel>protein-secreting ATPase</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.4.2.8#SIP70410A153C15E430"/>
<rdfs:comment>A non-phosphorylated, non-ABC (ATP-binding cassette) ATPase that is involved in protein transport.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>There are several families of enzymes included here, e.g. ATP-hydrolyzing enzymes of the general secretory pathway (Sec or Type II), of the virulence-related secretory pathway (Type III) and of the conjugal DNA-protein transfer pathway (Type IV).</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Type II enzymes occur in bacteria, archaea and eucarya, whereas type III and type IV enzymes occur in bacteria where they form components of a multi-subunit complex.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/8022262"/>
