<skos:altLabel>dipeptide transporting ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.4.2.9#SIPB7FA59A8DCDFEADA"/>
<rdfs:comment>ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A bacterial enzyme that interacts with an extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and mediates the uptake of di- and tripeptides.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Pseudomonas aeruginosa can interact with five different substrate binding proteins.</rdfs:comment>
