<skos:prefLabel>ABC-type cystine transporter</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cystine ABC transporter</skos:altLabel>
<skos:altLabel>cystine transporting ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.4.2.12#SIP05217C55F5878C20"/>
<activity rdf:resource="7.4.2.12#SIP946608528A75E4B3"/>
<rdfs:comment>ABC-type (ATP-binding cassette-type) transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>A bacterial enzyme that interacts with an extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and mediates the high affinity import of trace cystine.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from Escherichia coli K-12 can import both isomers of cystine and a variety of related molecules including djenkolate, lanthionine, diaminopimelate and homocystine.</rdfs:comment>
