<rdf:Description rdf:about="7.4.2.14">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/core/Enzyme"/>
<skos:prefLabel>ABC-type antigen peptide transporter</skos:prefLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.4.2.14#SIP8A892B7F7D6A2036"/>
<rdfs:comment>An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Does not undergo phosphorylation during the transport process.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>This entry describes vertebrate transporters involved in the transport of antigens from the cytoplasm to the endoplasmic reticulum for association with major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class I molecules.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The substrates are generated mainly from degradation of cytosolic proteins by the proteasome.</rdfs:comment>
