<skos:prefLabel>ABC-type fatty-acyl-CoA transporter</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>fatty-acyl-CoA-transporting ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.6.2.4#SIP37F10B68C7D1D7FF"/>
<rdfs:comment>An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>Does not undergo phosphorylation during the transport process.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>An animal and yeast enzyme that transports fatty acyl CoA into and out of peroxisomes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In humans, it is associated with Zellweger's syndrome.</rdfs:comment>
