<skos:prefLabel>ABC-type guanine transporter</skos:prefLabel>
<skos:altLabel>guanine-transporting ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.6.2.6#SIPE99288D136AF7847"/>
<rdfs:comment>An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter found in insects that transports guanine and other purines into pigment granules in the eye, where they are converted to pteridine pigments.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The transporter is a hererodimer composed of two different peptides, each containing one membrane-spanning and one cytoplasmic ATP-binding domain.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>In Drosophila, this transporter is encoded by the white and brown genes.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/117796"/>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/2503416"/>
