<skos:altLabel>alkane sulfonate ABC transporter</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.6.2.14#SIP3AD10CD0ADE8051C"/>
<rdfs:comment>ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli K-12 interacts with an extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and imports a broad range of aliphatic sulfonates for use as a source of sulfur.</rdfs:comment>
<citation rdf:resource="http://purl.uniprot.org/citations/10506196"/>
