<skos:altLabel>thiamine transporting ATPase</skos:altLabel>
<activity rdf:resource="7.6.2.15#SIPFCC45CDAB87298EC"/>
<rdfs:comment>ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral membrane domains/proteins.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:comment>The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Salmonella typhimurium, is a heterodimeric complex that interacts with an extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and functions to import thiamine, thiamine monophosphate and thiamine diphosphate.</rdfs:comment>
